1
00:00:04,838 --> 00:00:06,975
♪ IN THE NOT-TOO-DISTANT
FUTURE ♪

2
00:00:07,008 --> 00:00:10,212
♪ NEXT SUNDAY, A.D. ♪

3
00:00:10,245 --> 00:00:13,047
♪ THERE WAS A GUY
NAMED JOEL ♪

4
00:00:13,080 --> 00:00:16,550
♪ NOT TOO DIFFERENT
FROM YOU OR ME ♪

5
00:00:16,583 --> 00:00:19,420
♪ HE WORKED
AT GIZMONIC INSTITUTE ♪

6
00:00:19,453 --> 00:00:22,857
♪ JUST ANOTHER FACE
IN A RED JUMPSUIT ♪

7
00:00:22,890 --> 00:00:25,393
♪ HE DID A GOOD JOB
CLEANING UP THE PLACE ♪

8
00:00:25,427 --> 00:00:27,195
♪ BUT HIS BOSSES
DIDN'T LIKE HIM ♪

9
00:00:27,228 --> 00:00:29,630
♪ SO THEY SHOT HIM
INTO SPACE ♪

10
00:00:31,933 --> 00:00:35,070
♪ WE'LL SEND HIM
CHEESY MOVIES ♪

11
00:00:35,103 --> 00:00:38,272
- ♪ THE WORST WE CAN FIND ♪
- ♪ LA LA LA ♪

12
00:00:38,305 --> 00:00:41,142
♪ HE'LL HAVE TO SIT
AND WATCH THEM ALL ♪

13
00:00:41,175 --> 00:00:44,445
- ♪ AND WE'LL MONITOR HIS MIND ♪
- ♪ LA LA LA ♪

14
00:00:44,478 --> 00:00:47,482
♪ NOW KEEP IN MIND
JOEL CAN'T CONTROL ♪

15
00:00:47,515 --> 00:00:50,652
- ♪ WHERE THE MOVIES
BEGIN OR END ♪
- ♪ LA LA LA ♪

16
00:00:50,685 --> 00:00:53,888
♪ BECAUSE HE USED
THOSE SPECIAL PARTS ♪

17
00:00:53,888 --> 00:00:56,825
♪ TO MAKE HIS ROBOT FRIENDS ♪

18
00:00:58,493 --> 00:01:00,428
LET'S GO.

19
00:01:00,462 --> 00:01:01,728
- CAMBOT.
- PAN LEFT.

20
00:01:01,763 --> 00:01:03,030
HI, GIRL.

21
00:01:03,063 --> 00:01:04,832
WHAT A COOL GUY.

22
00:01:04,865 --> 00:01:06,400
A WISECRACKER.

23
00:01:06,433 --> 00:01:09,403
♪ IF YOU'RE WONDERING HOW
HE EATS AND BREATHES ♪

24
00:01:09,437 --> 00:01:12,273
- ♪ AND OTHER SCIENCE FACTS ♪
- ♪ LA LA LA ♪

25
00:01:12,307 --> 00:01:15,310
♪ THEN REPEAT TO YOURSELF
"IT'S JUST A SHOW ♪

26
00:01:15,343 --> 00:01:18,680
♪ "I SHOULD REALLY
JUST RELAX ♪

27
00:01:18,713 --> 00:01:21,548
♪ FOR..." ♪

28
00:01:33,293 --> 00:01:34,795
YEAH, LET'S SEE
IF WE CAN GET THIS ON.

29
00:01:34,828 --> 00:01:38,198
UH, "CD/WP51."
"RETURN."

30
00:01:38,232 --> 00:01:40,802
OH, CRIMINY.
STUPID CLONES.

31
00:01:40,835 --> 00:01:41,970
I REALLY MISS MY MACK.

32
00:01:42,003 --> 00:01:43,303
HEY, CROW,
WHAT'S THIS MEAN?

33
00:01:43,337 --> 00:01:46,407
"TOO MANY
PARAMENTERS-WP51."

34
00:01:46,440 --> 00:01:48,408
WHAT?
OH.

35
00:01:48,442 --> 00:01:51,112
UH, YOU USED A FORWARD SLASH
INSTEAD OF A BACKSLASH.

36
00:01:51,145 --> 00:01:53,013
A WHAT?
OH. OH, OKAY.

37
00:01:53,047 --> 00:01:56,885
CD BACKSLASH WP51.
RETURN.

38
00:01:56,918 --> 00:01:57,985
JEEZ.

39
00:01:58,018 --> 00:01:59,387
30 SECONDS
TO COMMERCIAL SIGN.

40
00:01:59,420 --> 00:02:02,257
HI, EVERYONE. WELCOME BACK
TO THE SATELLITE OF LOVE.

41
00:02:02,257 --> 00:02:03,958
TOM SERVO AND CROW
ARE IN THE MIDDLE

42
00:02:03,992 --> 00:02:05,560
OF ANOTHER
USER INTERFACE WAR.

43
00:02:05,593 --> 00:02:06,793
LET'S WATCH.

44
00:02:06,828 --> 00:02:08,897
OH, THIS IS RICH.
"BAD COMMAND OR FILE NAME."

45
00:02:08,930 --> 00:02:10,598
BOY, THEY EXPECT YOU
TO BE A MACHINE

46
00:02:10,632 --> 00:02:12,067
TO OPERATE THIS MACHINE.

47
00:02:12,100 --> 00:02:14,635
OH, AND I SUPPOSE YOU'D PREFER
A LITTLE, ANIMATED CLOWN

48
00:02:14,668 --> 00:02:16,570
WHO WOULD JUGGLE OVER
TO THE LITTLE FILE CABINET

49
00:02:16,603 --> 00:02:19,073
AND THEN WINK AT YOU
AND POINT TO THE RIGHT DRAWER.

50
00:02:19,107 --> 00:02:20,475
WELL, YEAH, SURE.

51
00:02:20,508 --> 00:02:22,310
AT LEAST I DON'T HAVE TO HAVE
A PHOTOGRAPHIC MEMORY

52
00:02:22,343 --> 00:02:23,545
TO GET MY MAC TO WORK.

53
00:02:23,578 --> 00:02:25,980
BOTH USER INTERFACES
WORK PERFECTLY WELL.

54
00:02:26,013 --> 00:02:28,583
IT'S REALLY JUST A MATTER
OF THE INDIVIDUAL'S
PERSONAL PREFERENCE.

55
00:02:28,617 --> 00:02:31,252
WE THINK THE JOKE'LL BE
ON TOM SERVO AND CROW.

56
00:02:31,285 --> 00:02:33,320
NOW HERE. THE PROBLEM
WITH IBMs AND COMPATIBLES

57
00:02:33,353 --> 00:02:36,223
IS THAT THEY LACK THE ELEGANCE
AND INTUITIVE NATURE OF THE MAC.

58
00:02:36,257 --> 00:02:40,027
MAC PRODUCTS ARE RELIABLE,
PROVEN, AND THEY ALWAYS WORK.

59
00:02:40,060 --> 00:02:42,130
OH, YEAH?
WHAT ABOUT SYSTEM SEVEN?

60
00:02:42,163 --> 00:02:43,932
IT'S COMING!
IT'S COMING, OKAY?

61
00:02:43,965 --> 00:02:46,100
THERE WERE A FEW BUGS
IN IT, OKAY?

62
00:02:46,133 --> 00:02:47,368
YOU CAN HAVE A LOT OF FUN

63
00:02:47,402 --> 00:02:49,737
WITH PEOPLE HOPELESSLY MIRED
IN COMPUTER NUANCE.

64
00:02:49,770 --> 00:02:53,742
WATCH THIS. HEY, HAS ANYBODY
SEEN THE MOUSE FOR MY AMIGA?

65
00:02:53,775 --> 00:02:56,110
- AMIGA!
- AMIGA? OH, COME ON.

66
00:02:56,143 --> 00:02:57,645
THERE'S A MACHINE FOR YOU.

67
00:02:57,678 --> 00:02:59,480
YEAH. HEY, HAS ANYONE
SEEN MY ANGUS DRIVE?

68
00:02:59,513 --> 00:03:03,517
COMMERCIAL SIGN
IN FIVE, FOUR, THREE, TWO...

69
00:03:03,552 --> 00:03:05,820
COMMERCIAL SIGN NOW.

70
00:03:12,327 --> 00:03:14,395
OH, NOW THIS
IS REALLY, REALLY NEAT.

71
00:03:14,428 --> 00:03:16,097
"UNRECOVERABLE
APPLICATION ERROR."

72
00:03:16,130 --> 00:03:17,198
THIS IS REALLY CUTE, CROW.

73
00:03:17,232 --> 00:03:18,365
I SUPPOSE
WE'LL HAVE TO RE-ENTER

74
00:03:18,398 --> 00:03:19,867
THE ENTIRE
SPREADSHEET NOW, HMM?

75
00:03:19,900 --> 00:03:21,368
NO. NO, NO, NO.

76
00:03:21,402 --> 00:03:23,403
JUST REWRITE
THE AUTO-EXEC BAT FILE

77
00:03:23,437 --> 00:03:24,705
AND STICK IN
THE MEMORY MANAGER.

78
00:03:24,738 --> 00:03:26,307
THAT'S ALL.
JUST TAKE A MINUTE.

79
00:03:26,340 --> 00:03:27,508
DON'T WORRY.

80
00:03:27,542 --> 00:03:28,977
...REBOOT THE DANG THING,
SEE WHAT HAPPENS.

81
00:03:29,010 --> 00:03:31,212
YEAH, WHILE, UH, TOM SERVO'S
REBOOTING THE COMPUTER,

82
00:03:31,245 --> 00:03:32,780
UH, I THOUGHT
IT'D BE A GOOD TIME

83
00:03:32,813 --> 00:03:34,515
TO SHOW THIS WEEK'S
INVENTION EXCHANGE.

84
00:03:34,548 --> 00:03:35,850
AND, UH,
WHAT I'VE GET HERE--

85
00:03:35,883 --> 00:03:37,352
LET ME TURN IT ON A SECOND.

86
00:03:37,385 --> 00:03:41,888
IS A NEW TOOL TO HELP
EXPAND PEOPLE'S CONSCIOUSNESS.

87
00:03:41,923 --> 00:03:43,123
YOU KNOW, JOEL,
THERE'S SOME THINGS

88
00:03:43,157 --> 00:03:44,858
THAT PEOPLE SHOULDN'T
BE CONSCIOUS ABOUT.

89
00:03:44,892 --> 00:03:45,960
LIKE WHAT?

90
00:03:45,993 --> 00:03:47,462
WELL, LIKE THE FACT
THAT THEIR TONGUES

91
00:03:47,495 --> 00:03:49,297
ARE JUST SITTING
IN THE BOTTOM OF THEIR MOUTHS

92
00:03:49,330 --> 00:03:51,665
ALL DAY, ALL NIGHT,
EVEN WHEN THEY SLEEP.

93
00:03:51,698 --> 00:03:52,867
YECH.

94
00:03:52,900 --> 00:03:55,202
UH, CHATTER BOT,
WOULD YOU LET ME FINISH?

95
00:03:55,235 --> 00:03:58,505
I'M TALKING ABOUT EXPANDING
PEOPLE'S CONSCIOUSNESS

96
00:03:58,538 --> 00:04:00,375
ABOUT THE RECYCLING CAUSE.

97
00:04:00,408 --> 00:04:03,712
THAT'S WHY I BUILT THIS AUDIO
ANIMATRONIC POP CAN HERE.

98
00:04:03,745 --> 00:04:06,513
ENOUGH MAGIC
FOR MANY EVENINGS.

99
00:04:06,547 --> 00:04:08,950
YEAH, SO WHAT I THOUGHT
WE COULD DO

100
00:04:08,983 --> 00:04:10,852
IS USE IT AS A SPOKESPERSON

101
00:04:10,885 --> 00:04:12,320
FOR, LIKE,
RECYCLING COMMERCIALS

102
00:04:12,353 --> 00:04:13,553
WHEN WE GET BACK TO EARTH.

103
00:04:13,587 --> 00:04:15,623
HERE'S A BAFFLER
WORTH TWICE THE PRICE.

104
00:04:15,623 --> 00:04:16,690
YEAH, WHATEVER.

105
00:04:16,723 --> 00:04:18,192
ANYWAY, CROW,
LET'S DO THAT THING

106
00:04:18,225 --> 00:04:20,862
WHERE I MAKE HIM WORK
AND I'LL MANIPULATE THE CAN.

107
00:04:20,895 --> 00:04:21,895
YOU DO THE VOICE, OKAY?

108
00:04:21,928 --> 00:04:22,930
ALL RIGHT. OKAY.

109
00:04:22,963 --> 00:04:24,498
YOUNG MAGICIANS
LOVE THIS ONE.

110
00:04:24,532 --> 00:04:28,302
HELLO, FOLKS.
REMEMBER, I RECYCLE.

111
00:04:28,335 --> 00:04:29,403
GOODNIGHT.

112
00:04:29,437 --> 00:04:31,438
NO SKILL REQUIRED.
OH, THIS IS RICH.

113
00:04:31,472 --> 00:04:32,473
STANDS RIGID INSPECTION.

114
00:04:32,507 --> 00:04:35,910
A QUALITY PRODUCT.
THAT ONE STUNG--

115
00:04:35,943 --> 00:04:37,545
WHAT DO YOU THINK, SIRS?

116
00:04:37,578 --> 00:04:41,415
I THINK YOU'VE GOT A KOOKY
SCREW LOOSE, IS WHAT I THINK.

117
00:04:42,950 --> 00:04:44,452
OH, WE HAVE FUN.

118
00:04:44,485 --> 00:04:46,920
OH, QUIT YOUR CLOWNING,
ITCHY MANGO,

119
00:04:46,953 --> 00:04:49,990
AND GO AND GET YOUR HARNESS ON.
ALL OF IT.

120
00:04:50,023 --> 00:04:52,627
DISCO'S BACK,
FROG BAIT, AND SO AM I.

121
00:04:52,660 --> 00:04:55,095
AND SO IS THIS NEW
DISCO CUMMER BUBBLE BUND.

122
00:04:55,128 --> 00:04:58,098
ENTER FRANK.

123
00:04:58,132 --> 00:05:01,768
THAT'S IT, BABY.
WORK THAT BODY.

124
00:05:01,802 --> 00:05:03,203
MAKE IT BURN.
THERE YOU GO.

125
00:05:03,237 --> 00:05:04,238
THERE'S A GOOD ONE.

126
00:05:04,272 --> 00:05:05,440
OH, ANOTHER GOOD ONE,
FRANK.

127
00:05:05,473 --> 00:05:08,108
YES. COME ON.
YOU CAN MAKE A BUBBLE.

128
00:05:08,142 --> 00:05:11,245
YOU JUST PUT YOUR KNEES
TOGETHER AND SQUEEZE.

129
00:05:11,278 --> 00:05:14,682
YES. I HAVE SEEN THE FUTURE
OF HIP HOP, JOEL,

130
00:05:14,715 --> 00:05:16,183
AND IT IS FRANK.

131
00:05:16,217 --> 00:05:18,485
AS FOR YOUR EXPERIMENT
THIS WEEK,

132
00:05:18,518 --> 00:05:20,220
IT'S ANOTHER IN A LONG LINE

133
00:05:20,253 --> 00:05:22,890
OF GAMERA GIANT FLYING
TURTLE MOVIES.

134
00:05:22,923 --> 00:05:24,725
THIS ONE'S FEATURING BARUGON,

135
00:05:24,758 --> 00:05:27,728
WHO'S SORT OF
A GIANT LIZARD DOG

136
00:05:27,762 --> 00:05:29,730
WITH ITCHY SCALP.

137
00:05:29,763 --> 00:05:32,200
TAKE THIS FILM
AND SHOVE IT, JOEL.

138
00:05:32,233 --> 00:05:34,768
WELL, YOU SEE, YOU CAN PRESS IT
BACK DOWN AGAIN, CROW,

139
00:05:34,802 --> 00:05:36,403
'CAUSE HE'S
A ROCK 'EM SOCK 'EM ROBOT--

140
00:05:36,437 --> 00:05:39,207
OH, WE GOT MOVIE SIGN!

141
00:05:50,017 --> 00:05:51,418
YOU KNOW,
THAT CUMMER BUBBLE BUND

142
00:05:51,452 --> 00:05:53,855
LOOKS KINDA FAMILIAR
FOR SOME REASON.

143
00:05:53,888 --> 00:05:58,793
WATER. THE SOURCE
OF ALL SANDY FRANK FILMS.

144
00:05:58,827 --> 00:06:02,563
OH, ♪ D-A-E-I-E-O ♪

145
00:06:02,597 --> 00:06:04,432
♪ E-I-E-I-O ♪

146
00:06:04,465 --> 00:06:08,468
HEY, LOOKS LIKE A KID
WROTE THIS WITH A CRAYON.

147
00:06:08,502 --> 00:06:11,938
OH, I WOULDN'T FOR ONE
NEGATE NAGATA.

148
00:06:11,972 --> 00:06:13,140
YOU GOTTA, THOUGH.

149
00:06:13,173 --> 00:06:14,942
OH, PLANNING.
I HATE WHEN HE PLANS.

150
00:06:14,975 --> 00:06:16,177
THERE'S NEVER ENOUGH BUNS.

151
00:06:27,555 --> 00:06:29,323
MUSIC SUPPLIED BY OUR OWN

152
00:06:29,390 --> 00:06:32,427
OSAKA HIGH SCHOOL
FLYING PIPERS DRUM CORPS.

153
00:06:32,460 --> 00:06:33,627
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

154
00:06:33,660 --> 00:06:36,630
♪ KILL THE "WABBIT"
KILL THE "WABBIT ♪

155
00:06:36,663 --> 00:06:39,233
HEY, I THINK
I SEE MY LAUNDRY.

156
00:06:39,267 --> 00:06:42,437
♪ KILL THE "WABBIT" ♪

157
00:06:44,572 --> 00:06:46,873
A LITTLE BACKGROUND FIRST.

158
00:06:46,907 --> 00:06:48,708
[ANNOUNCER]
SIX MONTHS AGO,

159
00:06:48,742 --> 00:06:50,478
AN AIRPLANE
CARRYING AN ATOM BOMB

160
00:06:50,512 --> 00:06:52,947
CRASHED WHILE FLYING OVER
THE ARCTIC OCEAN.

161
00:06:52,980 --> 00:06:54,515
- SEEN IN.
- HATED IT.

162
00:06:54,548 --> 00:06:55,650
TAPED IT.

163
00:06:55,683 --> 00:06:56,883
...SHATTERING
THE HUGE ICE FLOWS

164
00:06:56,917 --> 00:06:59,320
AND RELEASING FROM THE DEPTHS,
GAMERA...

165
00:06:59,353 --> 00:07:00,555
BILL GAMERA.

166
00:07:00,588 --> 00:07:02,022
...WHO HAD BEEN
IMPRISONED IN THE ICE

167
00:07:02,055 --> 00:07:03,757
FOR THOUSANDS OF YEARS.

168
00:07:03,792 --> 00:07:06,427
HEY, BILL.

169
00:07:06,460 --> 00:07:08,395
FREE AT LAST,
FREE AT LAST,

170
00:07:08,428 --> 00:07:11,398
THANK GOD ALMIGHTY
I'M FREE AT LAST.

171
00:07:11,432 --> 00:07:12,667
...WAS TO ATTACK JAPAN.

172
00:07:12,700 --> 00:07:13,700
OOH.

173
00:07:13,733 --> 00:07:14,768
ALL MANMADE WEAPONS

174
00:07:14,802 --> 00:07:16,603
PROVED POWERLESS
AGAINST HIM.

175
00:07:16,637 --> 00:07:19,073
ALL SCALE MODELS
WERE POWERLESS AGAINST HIM.

176
00:07:22,543 --> 00:07:25,112
THERE WAS ONLY
ONE LAST RESORT--

177
00:07:25,145 --> 00:07:26,813
THE "Z" PLAN.

178
00:07:26,847 --> 00:07:29,283
GAMERA WAS JETTISONED
TO MARS IN A ROCKET.

179
00:07:29,317 --> 00:07:30,785
AGAIN, THERE WAS FAILURE.

180
00:07:30,818 --> 00:07:32,787
AND DEEP, PERSONAL SHAME.

181
00:07:32,820 --> 00:07:34,022
...AND SPLIT OPEN,

182
00:07:34,055 --> 00:07:35,857
LIBERATING GAMERA
FROM THE CAPSULE.

183
00:07:35,890 --> 00:07:37,925
AND MAYBE, JUST MAYBE,
IN A SMALL WAY,

184
00:07:37,958 --> 00:07:40,962
LIBERATING ALL MONSTERS
EVERYWHERE.

185
00:07:40,995 --> 00:07:42,597
HMM.

186
00:07:42,630 --> 00:07:44,598
GAMERA RETURNED TO JAPAN

187
00:07:44,632 --> 00:07:46,133
AND ATTACKED THE KUROBE DAM,

188
00:07:46,167 --> 00:07:48,568
THE LARGEST OF ITS KIND
IN THE ENTIRE ORIENT.

189
00:07:48,602 --> 00:07:49,670
SO YOU KNOW IT'S GOOD.

190
00:07:49,703 --> 00:07:51,505
GAMERA MUST
HAVE A SOURCE OF FUEL,

191
00:07:51,538 --> 00:07:52,973
AND SO,
FROM THE POWER PLANT,

192
00:07:53,007 --> 00:07:55,677
HE EXTRACTED ELECTRICITY
TO STORE IN HIS OWN BODY.

193
00:07:55,710 --> 00:07:57,278
WEIRD, HUH?

194
00:07:57,312 --> 00:07:59,047
HMM. HEY.

195
00:07:59,080 --> 00:08:00,147
[IMITATES METALLIC DING]

196
00:08:00,180 --> 00:08:04,285
HEY. WHAT'S THAT?

197
00:08:04,318 --> 00:08:05,720
HEY, IT'S GAMERA!

198
00:08:05,753 --> 00:08:06,920
GAMERA!

199
00:08:06,953 --> 00:08:09,723
OH, YOU KNOW, I THOUGHT
HE LOOKED FAMILIAR.

200
00:08:09,790 --> 00:08:11,192
LOOK OUT!

201
00:08:11,225 --> 00:08:12,227
[MEN CONTINUE SHOUTING]

202
00:08:12,260 --> 00:08:13,862
OH, DAM.

203
00:08:13,895 --> 00:08:15,997
HEY, STOP TALKING!
ONE AT A TIME!

204
00:08:16,030 --> 00:08:19,967
QUIT TALKING
ALL AT THE SAME TIME.

205
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:22,370
[MEN CONTINUE SHOUTING]

206
00:08:22,403 --> 00:08:24,872
LOOKS LIKE A BIG
CHICKEN POT PIE, KIND OF.

207
00:08:24,905 --> 00:08:27,308
HMM.

208
00:08:27,342 --> 00:08:29,443
OOH.

209
00:08:29,477 --> 00:08:33,513
I JUST CAN'T GET CLOSE
TO ANYONE ANYMORE!

210
00:08:35,015 --> 00:08:38,452
OH, YOU MEN.
TURN OFF THE MAIN SWITCHES!

211
00:08:38,485 --> 00:08:39,487
BONG.

212
00:08:39,520 --> 00:08:42,323
OH, YOU GOT HIM.

213
00:08:42,323 --> 00:08:44,358
HUH. FUNNY.
IN COLOR, I EXPECTED GAMERA

214
00:08:44,392 --> 00:08:46,427
TO BE MORE
OF A STRAWBERRY BLONDE.

215
00:08:46,460 --> 00:08:48,462
HE'S KIND OF A TAWNY...

216
00:08:48,495 --> 00:08:50,363
CAMERA PUTS ON 50,000 POUNDS.

217
00:08:50,397 --> 00:08:51,832
OH, LUNCH FOR ME?
OH, THANK YOU.

218
00:08:51,865 --> 00:08:55,335
[SCREECHING]

219
00:08:55,368 --> 00:08:58,872
WHY DOES HE SOUND LIKE SOMEONE
PLAYING THE TRUMPET BADLY?

220
00:08:58,907 --> 00:09:02,710
OH, YOU MEAN LIKE
CHUCK MANGIONE?

221
00:09:02,743 --> 00:09:03,843
TOKYO, I THINK IT'S TIME

222
00:09:03,877 --> 00:09:06,313
TO START THINKING
ABOUT SOLAR POWER.

223
00:09:06,347 --> 00:09:07,882
AH, HE CAN'T RESIST.

224
00:09:07,915 --> 00:09:09,650
HE'S A SLAVE
TO HIS OWN PASSION.

225
00:09:09,683 --> 00:09:14,288
GAMERA CRAVES
THE CREAMY TASTE OF FLAMES.

226
00:09:14,322 --> 00:09:16,290
OH, NOW WAS THAT NECESSARY,
YOUNG MAN?

227
00:09:16,290 --> 00:09:17,792
I MEAN...

228
00:09:17,825 --> 00:09:20,027
CHARBROILED CITY.

229
00:09:20,060 --> 00:09:22,897
[ALL]
CHARBROILED CITY.

230
00:09:22,930 --> 00:09:23,932
CHARBROILED...

231
00:09:23,965 --> 00:09:25,365
OOH.

232
00:09:25,398 --> 00:09:28,435
MAN,
HE'S GOT A SHORT REACH.

233
00:09:28,468 --> 00:09:31,972
NOW BAKE THE CITY
AT 7,500 DEGREES...

234
00:09:34,108 --> 00:09:36,810
QUICK,
GET THE KC MASTERPIECE SAUCE.

235
00:09:36,843 --> 00:09:38,678
I THINK HE MEANS IT
THIS TIME.

236
00:09:38,712 --> 00:09:39,847
WHOA!

237
00:09:39,880 --> 00:09:40,882
MOVE IT.

238
00:09:40,915 --> 00:09:43,883
- HEY, HURRY UP.
- COME ON.

239
00:09:43,917 --> 00:09:45,418
OH, I'M FULL.

240
00:09:45,452 --> 00:09:46,453
[BELCHES]

241
00:09:46,487 --> 00:09:47,922
OH, YOU KNOW
WHAT YOU WANNA DO IS,

242
00:09:47,955 --> 00:09:49,223
YOU WANNA
PULL OFF THEM PETALS

243
00:09:49,257 --> 00:09:50,490
AND DIP IT
IN THAT SAUCE THERE.

244
00:09:50,523 --> 00:09:51,758
OH, THAT'S REALLY
SUPER NEAT.

245
00:09:51,792 --> 00:09:52,760
OH, YEAH.
TRY THE LEMON.

246
00:09:52,793 --> 00:09:53,995
WELL, THAT REMINDS ME.

247
00:09:54,028 --> 00:09:56,230
I SHOULD SHINGLE MY ROOF
WHEN I GET BACK TO EARTH.

248
00:09:56,263 --> 00:09:59,267
HUH?

249
00:09:59,300 --> 00:10:01,168
BYE.

250
00:10:01,202 --> 00:10:03,437
WHOA, IT LOOKS LIKE WEMBLEY
STADIUM AFTER A SOCCER MATCH.

251
00:10:03,470 --> 00:10:08,275
OH, THERE'S A LOT OF STUFF
GOING ON DOWN THERE.

252
00:10:08,308 --> 00:10:12,212
SO...

253
00:10:12,245 --> 00:10:14,315
OOPS. THAT WAS ME.
MY FAULT.

254
00:10:14,348 --> 00:10:15,983
UH, SORRY.
CAN'T SEE.

255
00:10:16,017 --> 00:10:17,818
MY HEAD'S INSIDE,
YOU KNOW.

256
00:10:17,852 --> 00:10:19,320
HIGHER, GAMERA, HIGHER.

257
00:10:19,353 --> 00:10:23,357
ABOUT 50 FEET UP.
OKAY, BACK UP AND PUSH.

258
00:10:23,390 --> 00:10:24,825
UH-OH.

259
00:10:24,858 --> 00:10:28,028
A SPECTACULAR CASCADE
OF ALKA SELTZER.

260
00:10:28,062 --> 00:10:30,965
I CAN'T BELIEVE GAMERA
ATE THE WHOLE THING.

261
00:10:30,998 --> 00:10:33,000
HE ATE IT, RALPH.

262
00:10:33,033 --> 00:10:35,402
LOOK, WATER,
THE SOURCE OF ALL--

263
00:10:35,435 --> 00:10:37,972
WE KNOW. WE KNOW.

264
00:10:41,208 --> 00:10:42,242
OOH.

265
00:10:42,275 --> 00:10:44,145
GAMERA LOVES FLAMES.

266
00:10:44,178 --> 00:10:45,680
BUT THEY GO STRAIGHT
TO HIS HIPS.

267
00:10:45,713 --> 00:10:47,515
HE LEFT JAPAN AS SUDDENLY
AS HE HAD ARRIVED,

268
00:10:47,548 --> 00:10:49,983
AND HEADED FOR MOUNT UZAL
AND THE EQUATOR,

269
00:10:50,017 --> 00:10:52,920
FLYING DIRECTLY TOWARD
THE FLOWING MOLTEN LAVA.

270
00:10:52,953 --> 00:10:55,222
HE HAD A CONTRACT
WITH WHAM-O.

271
00:10:55,288 --> 00:10:56,290
HMM.

272
00:10:56,290 --> 00:10:57,392
WHEN IN CLEVELAND,

273
00:10:57,425 --> 00:10:58,958
VISIT THE GOLDEN DRAGON INN,

274
00:10:58,992 --> 00:11:00,728
ONLY 15 MINUTES
FROM OUR CINEMA.

275
00:11:00,762 --> 00:11:02,295
AND NOW BACK TO OUR FILM--

276
00:11:02,328 --> 00:11:04,165
SKY KING,
THE MOTION PICTURE.

277
00:11:08,302 --> 00:11:11,338
TELL ME, ARE YOU REALLY
GOING TO RESIGN?

278
00:11:11,372 --> 00:11:14,475
YEAH.
THIS IS MY LAST DAY UP HERE.

279
00:11:14,508 --> 00:11:16,143
I WILL SERVE MY MASTER
DOWN THERE.

280
00:11:16,177 --> 00:11:17,378
BUT YOU'VE JUST
EARNED YOUR WINGS

281
00:11:17,412 --> 00:11:18,412
AFTER SO MUCH
DEDICATED WORK.

282
00:11:18,445 --> 00:11:19,513
CLARENCE.

283
00:11:19,547 --> 00:11:21,182
WHAT MADE YOU DECIDE
TO QUIT?

284
00:11:21,215 --> 00:11:22,917
TIRED OF FLYING ALREADY?

285
00:11:22,950 --> 00:11:24,418
CERTAINLY NOT.

286
00:11:24,452 --> 00:11:26,587
MY DREAM
IS TO CONTINUE FLYING.

287
00:11:26,620 --> 00:11:27,622
AND HAVE MY VOICE DUBBED.

288
00:11:27,655 --> 00:11:29,423
OR ELSE LIFE
WOULD BE WORTHLESS.

289
00:11:29,457 --> 00:11:31,192
SO THAT'S WHY
I'M QUITTING NOW.

290
00:11:31,225 --> 00:11:33,727
- I WANT TO LEARN MORE.
- YOU SHOULD TOO.

291
00:11:33,760 --> 00:11:37,130
SO THAT LATER
I WILL BE MORE SKILLED.

292
00:11:37,163 --> 00:11:38,698
FAIR ENOUGH.

293
00:11:42,335 --> 00:11:44,905
HEY, DIDN'T GEORGE HARRISON
WRITE THIS SONG?

294
00:11:44,938 --> 00:11:47,775
YEAH.
"MY SWEET WARLORD."

295
00:11:47,808 --> 00:11:48,908
OH, THAT'S CUTE.

296
00:11:48,942 --> 00:11:51,545
33 1/3, I THINK.

297
00:11:51,578 --> 00:11:54,548
HEY, I NEVER
KNEW A CHEESE-CUTTER
COULD SOUND THIS GOOD.

298
00:11:57,150 --> 00:11:59,853
OH, IT'S THE JOY LUCK CLUB
BLUES BAND.

299
00:11:59,887 --> 00:12:02,355
[LAUGHS]

300
00:12:02,388 --> 00:12:07,260
COME ON. PLAY IT LIKE YOU
FEEL IT, MR. EDDIE'S FATHER.

301
00:12:07,293 --> 00:12:10,463
AND NOW IT'S PINK LADY
UNPLUGGED.

302
00:12:12,467 --> 00:12:14,868
AH, THIS OUGHT
TO SHUT 'EM UP.

303
00:12:14,902 --> 00:12:18,905
COME ON.
OH, THEY'RE NOT THAT BAD.

304
00:12:22,342 --> 00:12:24,712
UH, GANG,
MAYBE YOU SHOULDN'T BE SMOKING

305
00:12:24,745 --> 00:12:26,780
AROUND ALL THOSE THINGS, HMM?

306
00:12:26,813 --> 00:12:28,548
HMM.

307
00:12:28,582 --> 00:12:31,585
THIS ONE KINDA
LOOKS LIKE AN AVOCADO.

308
00:12:31,618 --> 00:12:33,820
HEY, CAN THE PINEAPPLE.
IT'S SOMEBODY.

309
00:12:33,853 --> 00:12:35,622
SHH.
IXNAY.

310
00:12:35,622 --> 00:12:38,692
I'LL GET IT.
AH, DAMN CHARLIE HORSE.

311
00:12:38,725 --> 00:12:42,228
SITTING ON MY LEG.

312
00:12:42,262 --> 00:12:44,298
HMM?

313
00:12:44,332 --> 00:12:45,332
SUPER FLY?

314
00:12:45,365 --> 00:12:47,067
OH, IT'S YOU.

315
00:12:47,100 --> 00:12:48,102
GOT 'EM.

316
00:12:48,135 --> 00:12:50,103
COME IN.

317
00:12:52,105 --> 00:12:54,175
TEA, BISCUITS?

318
00:12:54,208 --> 00:12:57,210
MY BROTHER.

319
00:12:57,243 --> 00:12:59,913
HI, I'M DANGEROUS
TO MYSELF AND OTHERS.

320
00:12:59,947 --> 00:13:01,015
HERE'S ALL MY MONEY.

321
00:13:01,048 --> 00:13:02,048
HOW MUCH?

322
00:13:02,082 --> 00:13:03,517
IT'S MY PENSION.

323
00:13:03,550 --> 00:13:04,552
- OOH.
- 50 BUCKS.

324
00:13:04,585 --> 00:13:05,685
NOT A BIG HELP.

325
00:13:05,718 --> 00:13:07,120
YEAH, IT'S NO USE
WORKING FOR OTHERS.

326
00:13:07,153 --> 00:13:09,357
I'VE GOT TO GET MY OWN
AIRCRAFT COMPANY.

327
00:13:09,390 --> 00:13:11,092
- NOW.
- HOWEVER SMALL.

328
00:13:11,125 --> 00:13:12,225
THAT'LL TAKE MONEY.

329
00:13:12,258 --> 00:13:14,060
AND YOU DON'T HAVE ANY.
HE JUST TOOK IT.

330
00:13:14,093 --> 00:13:15,095
NAH, NAH.

331
00:13:15,128 --> 00:13:17,097
WELL,
NOW THAT WE'RE ALL HERE,

332
00:13:17,130 --> 00:13:18,298
I'LL TELL YOU THE PLANS.

333
00:13:18,332 --> 00:13:20,800
DURING THE WAR,
I FOUND A HUGE OPAL.

334
00:13:20,835 --> 00:13:22,135
HMM. BIG.

335
00:13:22,168 --> 00:13:24,472
BELIEVE ME, IT WAS ABOUT
THE SIZE OF AN OSTRICH EGG.

336
00:13:24,505 --> 00:13:26,773
OH, IT GETS BIGGER
EVERY TIME HE TELLS THE STORY.

337
00:13:26,807 --> 00:13:29,710
JUST BEFORE I WAS TAKEN AWAY
TO A PRISONER OF WAR CAMP,

338
00:13:29,743 --> 00:13:31,445
- I MANAGED TO...
- DID YOU EVER GET OUT?

339
00:13:31,478 --> 00:13:33,113
...AGAIN IN THE CAVE
WHERE I FOUND IT.

340
00:13:33,147 --> 00:13:34,248
THAT WAS 20 YEARS AGO.

341
00:13:34,282 --> 00:13:36,317
[LOUD WHISPER]
DON'T MENTION THE WAR.

342
00:13:36,350 --> 00:13:38,418
THE CAVE LIES DEEP
IN THE DENSE JUNGLE

343
00:13:38,452 --> 00:13:40,820
WHERE EVEN THE NATIVES
NEVER GO.

344
00:13:40,855 --> 00:13:42,890
I THINK THAT IT'LL BE SAFE.

345
00:13:42,923 --> 00:13:44,292
WE'LL BE TAKING A BIG GABLE.

346
00:13:44,325 --> 00:13:47,360
[GOOFY LAUGHTER]
ME LIKE GAMBLE.

347
00:13:47,393 --> 00:13:49,463
WE'LL BE ABLE TO SELL IT
FOR AN ABSOLUTE FORTUNE.

348
00:13:49,497 --> 00:13:51,732
ARE YOU SURE
IT'S A REAL OPAL?

349
00:13:51,765 --> 00:13:53,200
- IT'S REAL.
- YEP.

350
00:13:53,233 --> 00:13:55,368
IT MUST BE.
AND THERE MIGHT BE MORE AS WELL.

351
00:13:55,402 --> 00:13:56,970
SINCE I CAN'T GET AWAY,

352
00:13:57,003 --> 00:13:58,505
KEISUKE, YOU GO.

353
00:13:58,538 --> 00:14:00,007
NAME'S QUESADILLA.

354
00:14:00,040 --> 00:14:03,010
- GLADLY.
- YEAH.

355
00:14:09,115 --> 00:14:11,285
YOU WILL ALL GO
ON A CARGO BOAT.

356
00:14:11,318 --> 00:14:13,253
WITH CRUTCH CARGO.
GET IT?

357
00:14:13,287 --> 00:14:16,957
FALSE NAMES,
AND YOU'LL CARRY FORGED PAPERS.

358
00:14:17,023 --> 00:14:17,992
YOU GOT THEM?

359
00:14:18,025 --> 00:14:19,427
OH, YEAH, YEAH.
'COURSE I HAVE.

360
00:14:19,460 --> 00:14:22,262
COST ME A SMALL FORTUNE.

361
00:14:22,295 --> 00:14:23,297
FOR THE FORGERY.

362
00:14:23,330 --> 00:14:25,498
THIS IS FOR YOU.
THIS ONE FOR YOU.

363
00:14:25,532 --> 00:14:26,767
AND THE PASSWORD IS...

364
00:14:26,800 --> 00:14:28,602
YOU TWO WILL BOARD THE SHIP
AS ORDINARY SEAMEN.

365
00:14:28,635 --> 00:14:30,137
FOR GOD'S SAKE
DON'T BUNGLE.

366
00:14:30,170 --> 00:14:31,205
IN THE JUNGLE.

367
00:14:31,238 --> 00:14:32,238
- WE'RE COUNTING ON YOU.
- THANKS.

368
00:14:32,272 --> 00:14:34,308
- OKAY?
- OKAY.

369
00:14:34,342 --> 00:14:37,678
THE AWAJI MARU WILL REACH
NEW GUINEA IN 25 DAYS,

370
00:14:37,712 --> 00:14:41,348
UNLOAD HERE, AND THEN
CONTINUE AROUND THIS AREA.

371
00:14:41,382 --> 00:14:43,917
AND THEN IT RETURNS BACK
TO THE ORIGINAL HARBOR

372
00:14:43,950 --> 00:14:45,518
JUST ABOUT
A FORTNIGHT LATER.

373
00:14:45,552 --> 00:14:47,420
YOU THREE HAVE
GOT THAT TWO-WEEK PERIOD

374
00:14:47,453 --> 00:14:49,088
IN WHICH TO LOCATE THE OPAL.

375
00:14:49,155 --> 00:14:50,925
YOU MEAN WE'RE TO QUIT
THE SHIP WITHOUT LEAVE

376
00:14:50,958 --> 00:14:51,958
AND THEN REBOARD IT AGAIN?

377
00:14:51,992 --> 00:14:53,260
THAT'S DISHONEST!

378
00:14:53,293 --> 00:14:56,197
WE SAY WE WANT TO PICK UP
THE BONES OF OUR BODIES

379
00:14:56,230 --> 00:14:57,965
WHO DIED INLAND
DURING THE WAR.

380
00:14:57,998 --> 00:15:01,035
OH, THAT'S RICH!
[LOUD LAUGHTER]

381
00:15:01,068 --> 00:15:02,670
THEN WHEN YOU GET
TO THE AIRPORT HERE,

382
00:15:02,703 --> 00:15:04,872
YOU'LL HAVE TO CHARTER
A HELICOPTER.

383
00:15:04,905 --> 00:15:08,042
KEISUKE, YOU'LL BE ABLE
TO FLY IT FOR THEM.

384
00:15:08,075 --> 00:15:09,977
THAT'S WHY YOU'RE HERE.

385
00:15:10,010 --> 00:15:12,980
AND NEXT, MONEY.

386
00:15:13,013 --> 00:15:15,848
REMEMBER TO TAKE PLENTY OF
BLACK-MARKET DOLLARS WITH YOU.

387
00:15:15,882 --> 00:15:17,818
MAKE SURE THEY HAVE
ART LINKLETTER'S
PICTURE ON THEM.

388
00:15:17,852 --> 00:15:19,520
BE CAREFUL
OF THE SCORPIONS.

389
00:15:19,553 --> 00:15:20,553
AND WHITESNAKE.

390
00:15:20,587 --> 00:15:22,155
YOU'VE HAD IT IF THEY STING.

391
00:15:22,188 --> 00:15:25,092
THE JUNGLE IS FULL
OF MANY OTHER DANGERS AS WELL.

392
00:15:25,125 --> 00:15:27,828
SO TAKE THESE
JUST TO BE SAFE.

393
00:15:27,862 --> 00:15:29,563
AND DON'T RUN BY THE POOL.

394
00:15:29,597 --> 00:15:31,265
AND BRING A WASHCLOTH
AND A ZIPLOCK BAG

395
00:15:31,298 --> 00:15:32,298
TO CLEAN UP AFTER BABY.

396
00:15:32,332 --> 00:15:33,733
YEAH, AND DON'T
GO INTO THE WATER

397
00:15:33,767 --> 00:15:35,802
UNTIL AN HOUR AFTER
YOU'VE EATEN.

398
00:15:35,835 --> 00:15:38,005
ARE THOSE CHICK JEANS?

399
00:15:38,038 --> 00:15:39,973
[WHISTLES]

400
00:15:40,007 --> 00:15:42,677
JUST WHO DO THEY THINK WE ARE,
ANYWAY?

401
00:15:42,710 --> 00:15:46,713
OH, STOP GRUMBLING.
PATIENCE.

402
00:15:46,747 --> 00:15:49,215
D'OH.

403
00:15:49,248 --> 00:15:52,018
YOU, THAT ROOM'S FILTHY.

404
00:15:52,052 --> 00:15:53,053
SO CLEAN IT!

405
00:15:53,087 --> 00:15:54,622
DO IT YOURSELF.

406
00:15:54,655 --> 00:15:58,725
IT'S TV's MR. T.

407
00:15:58,758 --> 00:16:00,393
I PITY THOSE FOOLS.

408
00:16:00,427 --> 00:16:01,528
WORKING HARD?

409
00:16:01,562 --> 00:16:03,197
NO, HARDLY WORKING.
IT'S THE...

410
00:16:03,230 --> 00:16:05,365
WHY COULDN'T YOU FIND US
SOME EASIER WORK TO DO?

411
00:16:05,398 --> 00:16:06,467
JUST STICK WITH IT.

412
00:16:06,500 --> 00:16:08,668
OH, HELP US OUT.
COME ON, HUH?

413
00:16:08,702 --> 00:16:10,537
WE HAVE TO CLEAN
THE WASHROOM TOO.

414
00:16:10,570 --> 00:16:11,572
[LAUGHS]

415
00:16:11,605 --> 00:16:12,605
IT'S NO JOKE.

416
00:16:12,638 --> 00:16:14,575
OH, SORRY.
I FORGOT. I LAUGHED.

417
00:16:17,745 --> 00:16:20,213
HEY. MY CABIN.
TONIGHT.

418
00:16:22,783 --> 00:16:24,952
ONLY THREE MORE DAYS.

419
00:16:24,985 --> 00:16:27,053
ARE YOU ABSOLUTELY SURE?
MM-HMM.

420
00:16:27,087 --> 00:16:28,388
I'VE GOT A CALENDAR.
I KNOW.

421
00:16:28,422 --> 00:16:30,023
DON'T GIVE IT UP NOW.

422
00:16:31,158 --> 00:16:32,292
OKAY.

423
00:16:32,325 --> 00:16:33,327
[IMITATES INHALING SMOKE]

424
00:16:33,360 --> 00:16:35,162
NEARING THE SANTANA CONCERT,

425
00:16:35,195 --> 00:16:36,763
WE PUT ON OUR LOVE BEADS

426
00:16:36,797 --> 00:16:39,933
AND PUT DOWN THE LANDING GEAR
OF OUR VW MICROBUS.

427
00:16:39,967 --> 00:16:42,002
KILLER.

428
00:16:42,035 --> 00:16:44,372
HEY, AND WE'RE
JUST IN TIME TO SEE DON HO.

429
00:16:44,405 --> 00:16:47,373
AND HIS SISTER HEIDI.

430
00:16:47,407 --> 00:16:48,475
ALL THE EARTH MOTHERS

431
00:16:48,508 --> 00:16:52,412
ARE EXPRESSING
THEIR POLITICAL STANCES.

432
00:16:52,445 --> 00:16:53,580
IT'S QUITE A STANCE TOO.

433
00:16:53,613 --> 00:16:54,815
WISH I HAD A LAWNMOWER.

434
00:16:54,848 --> 00:16:56,750
HEY.

435
00:16:56,783 --> 00:16:58,718
THE MALE OF THE TRIBE
IS SAYING,

436
00:16:58,752 --> 00:16:59,920
"HOW ABOUT DINNER
AND A MOVIE?"

437
00:16:59,953 --> 00:17:01,355
THE FEMALE RESPONDS WITH,

438
00:17:01,388 --> 00:17:03,623
"OKAY, BUT I'VE SEEN
MANNEQUIN ALREADY."

439
00:17:03,657 --> 00:17:05,658
THE MALE SAYS HE JUST WANTS
TO GO TO SLEEP,

440
00:17:05,692 --> 00:17:09,997
BUT THE FEMALE
WANTS TO TALK.

441
00:17:10,030 --> 00:17:12,398
CAN'T SEE.

442
00:17:12,432 --> 00:17:13,433
[HELICOPTER APPROACHING]

443
00:17:13,467 --> 00:17:16,837
[SHOUTING]

444
00:17:16,870 --> 00:17:19,707
WHAT, DID SOMEONE DROP
A COKE BOTTLE ALL OF A SUDDEN?

445
00:17:19,740 --> 00:17:21,242
ATTENTION ALL PERSONNEL.

446
00:17:21,275 --> 00:17:23,110
TONIGHT'S MOVIE
IS THE JUNGLE GODDESS,

447
00:17:23,143 --> 00:17:26,080
STARRING GEORGE REEVES, A GUY
WHO LOOKS LIKE ERNIE KOVACS,

448
00:17:26,113 --> 00:17:27,915
AND LOTS OF
FRENCH FRIED POTATOES.

449
00:17:31,385 --> 00:17:33,053
HEY, WE'RE FROM AMERICA.

450
00:17:33,087 --> 00:17:34,488
WE'VE COME TO DECIMATE
YOUR JUNGLE,

451
00:17:34,522 --> 00:17:36,857
CONVERT YOUR YOUTH,
AND MAKE YOU FEEL INFERIOR.

452
00:17:36,890 --> 00:17:38,358
LOOK, IT'S ROBERT DUVALL.

453
00:17:38,392 --> 00:17:40,093
HELLO? ANYBODY HERE?

454
00:17:40,127 --> 00:17:41,328
YOU KNOW, I SWEAR

455
00:17:41,362 --> 00:17:43,363
THERE WERE A LOT OF DANCERS
HERE A MINUTE AGO.

456
00:17:43,397 --> 00:17:45,565
DOESN'T MAKE--FIGURE.
GO FIGURE.

457
00:17:48,302 --> 00:17:49,837
HI. HOW WAS YOUR FLIGHT?

458
00:17:49,870 --> 00:17:50,937
HEY, QUIT CLOWNING.

459
00:17:50,970 --> 00:17:52,705
IT'S PROBABLY QUITE FAR
TO THE CAVES.

460
00:17:52,738 --> 00:17:55,675
AH.

461
00:17:55,708 --> 00:17:59,580
OOH. THEY SEEM RUDE.

462
00:17:59,613 --> 00:18:01,882
HEY, GET ME.
I'M A STRANGER IN PARADISE.

463
00:18:01,915 --> 00:18:04,618
BIG TIE.

464
00:18:04,652 --> 00:18:05,618
- HUH?
- HUH?

465
00:18:05,652 --> 00:18:07,620
LOOK. THERE'S WRITING.

466
00:18:07,653 --> 00:18:09,457
IT SAYS "YANKEES GO HOME."

467
00:18:09,490 --> 00:18:10,890
IT'S A GUIDE POST.

468
00:18:10,923 --> 00:18:12,492
NOT MUCH USE
IF WE CAN'T READ IT.

469
00:18:12,525 --> 00:18:13,893
ARE THEY WORDS OR PICTURES?

470
00:18:13,927 --> 00:18:14,928
UH-HUH.

471
00:18:14,962 --> 00:18:17,163
HEY, GIVE ME THE MAP,
WILL YOU?

472
00:18:17,197 --> 00:18:18,832
I THINK THAT THERE MIGHT
BE A SHORTCUT

473
00:18:18,865 --> 00:18:20,233
THROUGH THE JUNGLE
SOMEWHERE.

474
00:18:20,267 --> 00:18:21,268
HOO!

475
00:18:21,302 --> 00:18:23,170
OH, WHO GOOSED ME?

476
00:18:23,203 --> 00:18:25,338
PAT MORITA,
DENTURE WEARER.

477
00:18:28,575 --> 00:18:30,777
HEY, WATCH IT.
DON'T WAVE THAT GUN.

478
00:18:30,810 --> 00:18:32,212
- WE'RE QUITE SAFE.
- YES, IT'S A MOVIE.

479
00:18:32,245 --> 00:18:33,247
THEY'RE PLEASED.

480
00:18:33,280 --> 00:18:35,015
THEY HELPED US A LOT
DURING THE WAR.

481
00:18:35,048 --> 00:18:36,048
THEY'RE GOOD PEOPLE.

482
00:18:36,082 --> 00:18:37,818
SO BETTER LET ME KEEP IT.

483
00:18:37,852 --> 00:18:38,852
GIVE IT HERE, HUH?

484
00:18:38,885 --> 00:18:40,520
UH-OH.

485
00:18:40,553 --> 00:18:44,625
I'LL, UH, SHOOT MYSELF
TO PROVE WE'RE FRIENDLY.

486
00:18:44,658 --> 00:18:48,228
HEY. ASK ONE OF 'EM
TO BE OUR GUIDE.

487
00:18:48,262 --> 00:18:51,130
HOW CAN I? NONE OF THEM
UNDERSTAND US.

488
00:18:51,165 --> 00:18:53,700
YOU'RE WRONG.
I UNDERSTAND PERFECTLY.

489
00:18:53,733 --> 00:18:55,968
HEY, HAS ANYBODY
CALLED DIBS YET?

490
00:18:56,002 --> 00:18:56,970
DIBS. DIBS.

491
00:18:57,003 --> 00:19:01,007
OH, DARN. DARN.

492
00:19:01,040 --> 00:19:04,612
ARE YOU SMITTEN BY MY EYES
BY NOW?

493
00:19:04,645 --> 00:19:06,913
[IMITATES PURRING]

494
00:19:06,947 --> 00:19:10,217
OH, IT'S MY DAD.
I GOT TO GO NOW.

495
00:19:10,250 --> 00:19:11,552
OH, IT'S TOM WOLFE.

496
00:19:11,585 --> 00:19:14,588
OH, THANK GOD.
THE CONTEMPORARY NOVEL IS SAVED.

497
00:19:21,093 --> 00:19:24,230
DARN FOOL KID.

498
00:19:24,263 --> 00:19:26,433
YOU GENTLEMEN
COME DIRECTLY FROM JAPAN?

499
00:19:26,467 --> 00:19:27,467
YES. WHO ARE YOU?

500
00:19:27,500 --> 00:19:28,468
A DOCTOR.

501
00:19:28,502 --> 00:19:29,737
I'VE BEEN LIVING AND WORKING

502
00:19:29,770 --> 00:19:31,772
WITH THE PEOPLE OF THESE ISLANDS
FOR OVER TEN YEARS.

503
00:19:31,805 --> 00:19:34,173
HE HAS TENURE THEN.
TENURE.

504
00:19:34,207 --> 00:19:35,808
OUR FRIEND THE DOCTOR
CAME WITH HIS WIFE

505
00:19:35,842 --> 00:19:37,477
TO STUDY CERTAIN DISEASES.

506
00:19:37,510 --> 00:19:40,547
THEN HIS WIFE DIED OF THE VERY
DISEASE HE WAS CURING.

507
00:19:40,580 --> 00:19:41,782
CONVENIENT.

508
00:19:41,815 --> 00:19:44,017
HE DECIDED TO STAY HERE
THE REST OF HIS LIFE.

509
00:19:44,050 --> 00:19:45,685
WE'RE IMPRESSED.

510
00:19:45,718 --> 00:19:47,487
IT IS QUIET HERE.

511
00:19:47,520 --> 00:19:50,623
I FEEL NOW THAT I BELONG
TO THIS PEACEFUL VILLAGE.

512
00:19:50,657 --> 00:19:53,293
I NEVER EVEN THINK
OF MY OWN HOME ANY LONGER.

513
00:19:53,327 --> 00:19:54,728
NOT EVEN A LITTLE?

514
00:19:54,762 --> 00:19:56,463
AND I'VE BEEN
EXTREMELY FORTUNATE,

515
00:19:56,497 --> 00:19:58,098
FOR KAREN IS MY ASSISTANT,

516
00:19:58,132 --> 00:19:59,132
AND AN EXCELLENT ONE.

517
00:19:59,165 --> 00:20:00,367
OH, WE GET THE PICTURE.

518
00:20:00,400 --> 00:20:02,335
AH.

519
00:20:02,368 --> 00:20:03,803
OH.

520
00:20:03,837 --> 00:20:06,172
BY THE WAY,
WHAT HAS BROUGHT YOU

521
00:20:06,205 --> 00:20:07,740
TO SUCH A BACKWARDS SPOT?

522
00:20:07,773 --> 00:20:10,410
THE WIND, MAN.
THE WILD WIND.

523
00:20:10,443 --> 00:20:13,480
WELL, SIR, WE'VE COME
TO INVESTIGATE A CERTAIN CAVE.

524
00:20:13,513 --> 00:20:14,582
IT ISN'T FAR FROM HERE.

525
00:20:14,615 --> 00:20:17,650
HMM.

526
00:20:17,683 --> 00:20:20,520
NO GO, NAVAJO.
UH-UH.

527
00:20:20,553 --> 00:20:22,755
DOCTOR.
YOU KNOW WHERE THE CAVE IS?

528
00:20:22,788 --> 00:20:24,792
OH, YOU MUST NOT
GO NEAR THAT CAVE.

529
00:20:24,825 --> 00:20:26,360
BELIEVE ME.

530
00:20:26,393 --> 00:20:28,462
AND WHY NOT?

531
00:20:28,495 --> 00:20:30,697
IT'S CALLED RAINBOW VALLEY.

532
00:20:30,730 --> 00:20:31,698
THE CARE BEARS LIVE THERE.

533
00:20:31,732 --> 00:20:32,933
WHAT IS THAT?

534
00:20:32,967 --> 00:20:36,403
ON THAT STONE,
THERE'S A WARNING TO ALL.

535
00:20:36,437 --> 00:20:37,470
IT SAYS "WARNING."

536
00:20:37,503 --> 00:20:38,705
IT FORBIDS US TO GO THERE,

537
00:20:38,738 --> 00:20:41,207
AND HE WHO DISOBEYS IT
WILL NOT RETURN.

538
00:20:41,240 --> 00:20:42,242
BUT WHY?

539
00:20:42,275 --> 00:20:43,843
NOBODY KNOWS.

540
00:20:43,877 --> 00:20:45,478
THE TROUBLE I'VE SEEN.

541
00:20:45,512 --> 00:20:49,048
...IT STOOD THERE THOUSANDS
OF YEARS, SO THEY SAY.

542
00:20:49,082 --> 00:20:50,650
ONLY A FOOL WOULD DISOBEY.

543
00:20:50,683 --> 00:20:52,418
OUR ANCESTORS
HANDED DOWN A WARNING

544
00:20:52,452 --> 00:20:54,187
THAT AN EVIL SPIRIT
DWELLS THERE,

545
00:20:54,220 --> 00:20:55,755
AND IT IS DANGEROUS
EVEN TO APPROACH

546
00:20:55,788 --> 00:20:57,123
THE VALLEY OF THE RAINBOW.

547
00:20:57,190 --> 00:20:58,158
GO ON.

548
00:20:58,192 --> 00:20:59,993
THEN NO ONE HERE
WILL ACT AS OUR GUIDE?

549
00:21:00,027 --> 00:21:01,227
CERTAINLY NOT.

550
00:21:01,260 --> 00:21:03,797
ALL THE PEOPLE
ARE BEGGING YOU NOT TO GO.

551
00:21:03,830 --> 00:21:06,065
YOU MUST RESPECT THEIR WISHES
ON THIS POINT.

552
00:21:06,098 --> 00:21:10,137
EVEN HIS ROYAL
NECK BRACE SAYS SO.

553
00:21:10,170 --> 00:21:11,170
ALL RIGHT,
HUDDLE UP, EVERYBODY.

554
00:21:11,203 --> 00:21:13,507
BRING IT IN. COME ON.
BRING IT IN.

555
00:21:16,777 --> 00:21:18,345
DARN TOURISTS.

556
00:21:18,378 --> 00:21:19,578
HA.

557
00:21:19,612 --> 00:21:21,682
THEY DON'T ANYONE
TO GO NEAR THAT CAVE.

558
00:21:21,715 --> 00:21:22,882
WHAT MORE PROOF
COULD THERE BE

559
00:21:22,915 --> 00:21:24,150
THAT THERE'S HIDDEN TREASURE
THERE?

560
00:21:24,183 --> 00:21:25,752
OF COURSE. AND THEY'VE
EVEN CREATED A LEGEND

561
00:21:25,785 --> 00:21:27,353
TO PROTECT IT.

562
00:21:27,387 --> 00:21:31,223
THE EVIL SPIRIT
IS REALLY THE SCORPION
MY BROTHER MENTIONED THEN.

563
00:21:31,257 --> 00:21:32,658
WE'LL NEVER GET A GUIDE
FROM THEM.

564
00:21:32,692 --> 00:21:34,327
AH, I'LL HAVE TO CALL
KELLY GIRLS.

565
00:21:34,360 --> 00:21:36,028
LET'S GO ALONE.
THIS WAY.

566
00:21:36,062 --> 00:21:39,132
BUT WHAT IF THE TREASURE REALLY
DOES BELONG TO THESE NATIVES?

567
00:21:39,165 --> 00:21:40,867
SO?
WE'RE GONNA TAKE IT ANYWAY.

568
00:21:40,900 --> 00:21:42,635
OKAY. HEY, LET'S GO.

569
00:21:42,668 --> 00:21:44,470
- BUT I--
- LET'S GO.

570
00:21:44,503 --> 00:21:46,907
NO! NO!
YOU MUSTN'T GO IN THERE.

571
00:21:46,940 --> 00:21:48,408
WAIT! DON'T GO!

572
00:21:48,442 --> 00:21:50,077
[SHOUTS]

573
00:21:50,110 --> 00:21:51,512
DISTURBED NATIVE REBUTTAL.

574
00:21:51,545 --> 00:21:55,615
DON'T!
DON'T GO IN THERE.

575
00:21:55,648 --> 00:21:56,817
OH!

576
00:21:56,850 --> 00:21:58,452
HEY, WATCH OUT!

577
00:21:58,485 --> 00:21:59,920
ALL RIGHT, ALL RIGHT.

578
00:21:59,953 --> 00:22:02,222
I DIDN'T THINK THIS GUN
WOULD COME IN HANDY SO SOON.

579
00:22:02,255 --> 00:22:03,857
RIGHT.
NOW, LET'S GO.

580
00:22:03,890 --> 00:22:05,658
JUST LETTING OFF
A LITTLE STEAM.

581
00:22:05,692 --> 00:22:06,693
GOTTA GO.

582
00:22:06,727 --> 00:22:08,295
OH, WE GOTTA GO TOO.

583
00:22:08,328 --> 00:22:09,997
NICE MEETING YOU FOLKS.

584
00:22:10,030 --> 00:22:11,632
THANKS FOR EVERYTHING.

585
00:22:16,937 --> 00:22:18,938
WHAT FOOLS.

586
00:22:27,647 --> 00:22:28,782
...PEAS AND CARROTS.

587
00:22:28,815 --> 00:22:31,985
AND WE'LL BE RIGHT BACK
RIGHT AFTER THIS.

588
00:22:32,018 --> 00:22:33,953
KIDS, HERE'S THE GREATEST
AND NEATEST AND LATEST THING--

589
00:22:33,987 --> 00:22:35,755
5,000-PIECE FIGHTIN'
MEN AND MONSTER SET.

590
00:22:35,788 --> 00:22:36,923
SOME PIECES NOT INCLUDED.

591
00:22:36,923 --> 00:22:38,458
ASTONISH AND BAFFLE
YOUR FRIENDS AND FOES

592
00:22:38,492 --> 00:22:39,927
WHILE YOU PULVERIZE JAPAN.

593
00:22:39,960 --> 00:22:41,160
HERE'S WHAT YOU GET--

594
00:22:41,193 --> 00:22:42,328
500 JAPANESE LIGHT INFANTRY.

595
00:22:42,362 --> 00:22:43,597
BODY PARTS
MAY NOT BE MISSING.

596
00:22:43,630 --> 00:22:44,697
36 HELPLESS OFFICIALS,

597
00:22:44,732 --> 00:22:46,467
20 TANKS,
15 RECOILLESS RIFLES.

598
00:22:46,500 --> 00:22:47,500
NOT IN THIS SET.

599
00:22:47,533 --> 00:22:48,535
24 BAZOOKA GUM RUNNERS.

600
00:22:48,568 --> 00:22:49,568
18 AMBULANCE CHASERS.

601
00:22:49,602 --> 00:22:50,837
12 JET FIGHTERS.
STICK NOT INCLUDED.

602
00:22:50,870 --> 00:22:52,005
16 HELICOPTER PARTS,

603
00:22:52,038 --> 00:22:53,273
200 SHOOTING CROUCHERS,

604
00:22:53,307 --> 00:22:55,275
19 FIGHTING CLOWNS,
EIGHT DESERTERS,

605
00:22:55,308 --> 00:22:56,577
SIX GEESE A-LAYING,

606
00:22:56,610 --> 00:22:58,845
24 MOHAWK INDIANS,
AND MUCH, MUCH, MUCH, MUCH MORE.

607
00:22:58,878 --> 00:23:00,680
ACT NOW AND RECEIVE
AT HALF THE EXTRA VALUE

608
00:23:00,713 --> 00:23:02,515
THE MYSTIFYING
MONSTER ACTION PACK.

609
00:23:02,548 --> 00:23:04,383
FLAME ON WITH GAMERA.
TORSO SOLD SEPARATELY.

610
00:23:04,417 --> 00:23:06,620
HE SPITS REAL FIRE
AND CAUSES REAL PAIN.

611
00:23:06,653 --> 00:23:07,853
SOLID RUBBER BARUGON

612
00:23:07,887 --> 00:23:09,288
COMES COMPLETE WITH OPTIONAL
RAM TONGUE ACTION.

613
00:23:09,322 --> 00:23:10,357
NOT RESPONSIBLE
FOR NERVE DAMAGE.

614
00:23:10,357 --> 00:23:11,825
AND AMUSE YOUR FRIENDS

615
00:23:11,858 --> 00:23:13,860
WITH TOPO, MEEP SONG, AND BART
THE BATTLIN' BELGIAN ENDIVE.

616
00:23:13,893 --> 00:23:15,062
SOME PARTS MAY NOT EXIST.

617
00:23:15,095 --> 00:23:17,063
ACT NOW, ACT OFTEN,
AND SNAP ON THE ENTIRE

618
00:23:17,097 --> 00:23:18,532
TOKYO METROPOLITAN AREA,

619
00:23:18,565 --> 00:23:19,833
COMPLETE WITH BUILDINGS,
BRIDGES,

620
00:23:19,867 --> 00:23:21,333
AND THE BREAK-AWAY
MOUNT INUKO DAM.

621
00:23:21,367 --> 00:23:22,568
SMALLER THAN SHOWN.

622
00:23:22,602 --> 00:23:24,303
TRAMPLE THE ADD-ON HAPLESS
CITIZEN PLAY SET,

623
00:23:24,337 --> 00:23:25,338
THEN ABHOR THE ACTION

624
00:23:25,372 --> 00:23:26,840
WITH A FABULOUS
ANTI-WAR PROTEST PACK.

625
00:23:26,873 --> 00:23:28,242
SENATOR WELLSTONE
NOT INCLUDED.

626
00:23:28,275 --> 00:23:29,608
BUT THAT'S NOT ALL.

627
00:23:29,642 --> 00:23:31,410
RELIVE YOUR FAVORITE
JAPANESE MOVIE CARNAGE

628
00:23:31,445 --> 00:23:33,213
WITH THE LIGHTS, GAMERA, GAMERA
ACTION SERIES.

629
00:23:33,247 --> 00:23:34,815
THERE'S THE GIMP, THE GOON,
THE SHAME-FILLED BROTHER,

630
00:23:34,848 --> 00:23:37,050
THE HAPLESS GEISHA,
AND THE PULL-APART VOODOO KENNY.

631
00:23:37,083 --> 00:23:38,785
POSE IN THE NUDE
WITH THE FRISKY KITTEN REVIEW,

632
00:23:38,818 --> 00:23:41,220
THEN WATCH THE ACTION
FROM HIGH ATOP TOKYO TOWER

633
00:23:41,253 --> 00:23:43,157
AS THE TWISTED WORLD
YOU CREATE EXPLODES,

634
00:23:43,190 --> 00:23:45,092
IN RIVERS OF BLOOD
AND ENDLESS PAIN.
ORDER TODAY.

635
00:23:45,125 --> 00:23:46,927
OFFER LIMITED.
NOT AVAILABLE IN UTAH,
PUERTO RICO--

636
00:23:46,960 --> 00:23:48,595
PRICE IS SUBJECT TO END.
PLEASE WEAR RUBBER UNDERWEAR,

637
00:23:48,628 --> 00:23:50,230
AND SOME PARTS
MAY BE MADE OF CHICKEN.

638
00:23:50,263 --> 00:23:51,263
ACT NOW, BUY BONDS...

639
00:23:51,297 --> 00:23:52,732
MOMMY, MOMMY, MOMMY!

640
00:23:52,765 --> 00:23:54,700
OKAY. OKAY.
BREATHE, BOY. BREATHE.

641
00:23:54,733 --> 00:23:55,735
OH. MOMMY.

642
00:23:55,768 --> 00:23:57,137
ALL RIGHT,
THAT WAS A GOOD ONE.

643
00:23:57,170 --> 00:23:58,538
LET'S NOT DO THAT AGAIN.

644
00:23:58,572 --> 00:24:00,207
HERE'S SOMETHING WE THINK
YOU'LL REALLY LIKE.

645
00:24:00,240 --> 00:24:01,307
MOMMY.

646
00:24:01,340 --> 00:24:02,342
[SOBS]

647
00:24:02,375 --> 00:24:04,377
IT'S ALL RIGHT.
THAT'S OKAY.

648
00:24:15,288 --> 00:24:18,225
HEY, I FOUND MY HAMSTER.

649
00:24:18,258 --> 00:24:19,758
WHAT ARE WE
LOOKING FOR AGAIN?

650
00:24:19,792 --> 00:24:22,695
WHAT DOES IT LOOK LIKE?

651
00:24:22,728 --> 00:24:25,398
HMM?

652
00:24:25,432 --> 00:24:29,268
HUH?

653
00:24:29,302 --> 00:24:30,437
A BOWLING BALL?

654
00:24:30,470 --> 00:24:34,573
HEY! IT'S HERE!
IT'S HERE!

655
00:24:34,607 --> 00:24:36,610
EARL ANTHONY'S SIGNATURE.

656
00:24:36,643 --> 00:24:39,745
I'M CRYING.

657
00:24:39,778 --> 00:24:41,113
OUR GAMBLE PAID OFF.

658
00:24:41,147 --> 00:24:42,115
NEAT.

659
00:24:42,148 --> 00:24:44,183
WE GOT THE OPAL.
IT'S OURS.

660
00:24:44,217 --> 00:24:46,787
THOSE MEN, NO WONDER
THEY TRIED TO STOP US.

661
00:24:46,820 --> 00:24:48,388
THAT WAS FAST.

662
00:24:48,422 --> 00:24:50,490
NOW WE'RE
MULTI-MILLIONAIRES.

663
00:24:50,557 --> 00:24:52,158
JUST WAIT TILL I GET HOME.

664
00:24:52,192 --> 00:24:53,827
I'LL BUY A GREAT,
BIG MANSION

665
00:24:53,860 --> 00:24:56,062
AND KEEP ALL THE CUPBOARDS
STOCKED FULL OF FOOD AND WINE.

666
00:24:56,095 --> 00:24:57,430
OF ALL THE DUMB LUCK.

667
00:24:57,463 --> 00:25:00,967
UH-OH.
YOU GOT A LITTLE, UH...

668
00:25:01,000 --> 00:25:02,768
RUBBER SCORPION.

669
00:25:02,802 --> 00:25:04,503
SHE'LL BURST WITH HAPPINESS.

670
00:25:04,537 --> 00:25:06,405
I'LL DO JUST
WHAT I PLEASE FROM NOW ON.

671
00:25:06,438 --> 00:25:08,308
- JUST THINK.
- NO MORE BROCCOLI.

672
00:25:08,342 --> 00:25:10,143
YOU'LL OWN
AN AIRCRAFT COMPANY.

673
00:25:10,177 --> 00:25:12,445
I'M SO PLEASED
I SHALL GO MAD.

674
00:25:12,478 --> 00:25:14,280
ONODERA,
YOU SAY SOMETHING, HUH?

675
00:25:14,313 --> 00:25:15,715
UH, ANY LAST WORDS?

676
00:25:15,748 --> 00:25:18,718
HEY, ONODERA, AREN'T YOU HAPPY
THAT WE FOUND IT?

677
00:25:18,752 --> 00:25:22,155
UH, FRIENDSHIP IS WORTH
MUCH MORE THAN THE OPAL TO ME.

678
00:25:22,188 --> 00:25:23,790
I JUST WANT YOU KIDS
TO BE GOOD.

679
00:25:23,790 --> 00:25:25,725
HIRATAS, YOU'RE
A GOOD FRIEND.

680
00:25:25,758 --> 00:25:28,562
IMAGINE SHARING ALL THIS
WITH US.

681
00:25:28,595 --> 00:25:29,762
IT'S FUN.

682
00:25:29,795 --> 00:25:31,598
THINK HOW HAPPY HE'LL BE
THAT WE FOUND IT.

683
00:25:31,632 --> 00:25:34,633
OH, YEAH.
I WISH I COULD TELL HIM.

684
00:25:34,667 --> 00:25:38,338
HEY, HIRATA!

685
00:25:38,372 --> 00:25:40,407
OLLIE, OLLIE, IN FREE.

686
00:25:40,440 --> 00:25:42,942
WE FOUND THE OPAL ALREADY!

687
00:25:42,975 --> 00:25:44,043
BOY, IS HE HIGH.

688
00:25:44,077 --> 00:25:46,478
EXCUSE ME.
DEATH, WHERE IS THY STING?

689
00:25:46,512 --> 00:25:47,513
WE'RE WAITING.

690
00:25:47,547 --> 00:25:51,718
[WILD LAUGHTER]

691
00:25:51,752 --> 00:25:53,820
WHAT AN ECCENTRIC PERFORMANCE.

692
00:25:53,853 --> 00:25:56,222
ANY MINUTE NOW I THINK HE--

693
00:25:56,255 --> 00:25:58,057
BINGO.

694
00:25:58,090 --> 00:25:59,658
OOP, TIME TO BREAK OUT
THE BACTINE.

695
00:26:03,763 --> 00:26:07,867
WELL, AT LEAST HE'S DYING
A MILLIONAIRE.

696
00:26:07,900 --> 00:26:09,668
I'LL GET
THE FIRST AID KIT.

697
00:26:09,702 --> 00:26:11,705
PUSH DOWN ON THE WOUND.

698
00:26:11,738 --> 00:26:12,738
DON'T GO!

699
00:26:12,772 --> 00:26:14,140
FOR ONE BRIEF,
SHINING MOMENT

700
00:26:14,173 --> 00:26:15,442
THERE WAS A CAMELOT.

701
00:26:15,475 --> 00:26:19,545
[SCREAMS]

702
00:26:19,578 --> 00:26:21,313
OOH.
PUT A TOURNIQUET ON HIS NECK.

703
00:26:21,347 --> 00:26:23,015
IT'S DARK!

704
00:26:23,048 --> 00:26:26,385
OOH.
KISS IT AND MAKE IT BETTER.

705
00:26:26,418 --> 00:26:29,455
OKAY, BEAR DOWN. PUSH.

706
00:26:29,488 --> 00:26:31,590
[SHOUTS]

707
00:26:31,590 --> 00:26:33,025
[IMITATES HEAVY BREATHING]

708
00:26:33,058 --> 00:26:34,493
AH, IT'S A BOY.
CONGRATULATIONS.

709
00:26:34,527 --> 00:26:37,297
KAWAJIRI! KAWAJIRI!

710
00:26:37,330 --> 00:26:38,698
HURRY!

711
00:26:38,732 --> 00:26:42,235
KAWAJIRI, YOU'VE NEVER
GIVEN UP ON ANYTHING BEFORE.

712
00:26:42,268 --> 00:26:44,137
DON'T QUIT NOW, MAN.

713
00:26:44,170 --> 00:26:47,507
KAWAJIRI! KAWAJIRI!

714
00:26:47,540 --> 00:26:51,043
TOM AND JERRY? WHAT?

715
00:26:51,077 --> 00:26:53,713
MUST HAVE BEEN
HIS FAVORITE CARTOON.

716
00:26:53,747 --> 00:26:56,883
OOH.
WE HAD SO MUCH MORE TO DO.

717
00:26:58,985 --> 00:27:01,553
HE DIED AS HE LIVED.
GOOFY.

718
00:27:01,587 --> 00:27:03,957
MM-HMM.

719
00:27:04,023 --> 00:27:05,658
HEY, I HURT TOO, MAN.

720
00:27:05,692 --> 00:27:06,960
HE WAS UNLUCKY.

721
00:27:06,993 --> 00:27:09,928
HEY, I'M DEALING WITH IT.
WHY CAN'T YOU?

722
00:27:12,732 --> 00:27:16,837
CAN I HAVE YOUR WATCH?

723
00:27:16,870 --> 00:27:19,472
SO, LUNCH?

724
00:27:19,505 --> 00:27:21,842
DON'T CRY.
IT'S NO USE.

725
00:27:21,875 --> 00:27:23,008
LET'S GO.

726
00:27:23,042 --> 00:27:24,543
COME ON, MAN.

727
00:27:24,577 --> 00:27:27,780
YEAH, WE STILL GOT
A THOUSAND WONDERFUL HOURS.

728
00:27:31,852 --> 00:27:34,753
HEY, LET'S PUT HIM
IN A REAL SCARY POSE.

729
00:27:34,787 --> 00:27:37,157
WELL, THERE'S ONE
GOOD THING AT LEAST.

730
00:27:37,190 --> 00:27:38,290
WE'VE GOT THE OPAL.

731
00:27:38,358 --> 00:27:41,460
WE MIGHT AS WELL GET GOING.

732
00:27:41,493 --> 00:27:44,930
COME ON. YOU CAN'T
BRING HIM BACK TO LIFE.

733
00:27:44,963 --> 00:27:46,098
WUSS.

734
00:27:46,132 --> 00:27:48,568
OH.

735
00:27:48,602 --> 00:27:51,603
FOR SAFETY,
I'LL KEEP THE OPAL. HMM?

736
00:27:51,637 --> 00:27:54,540
YEAH, I'M BETTER NOW.
I'M ALL RIGHT.

737
00:27:54,573 --> 00:27:56,242
HUH?

738
00:27:56,275 --> 00:27:59,778
HEY, NOW.
DON'T YOU TRUST ME WITH IT?

739
00:27:59,812 --> 00:28:03,282
WELL, I, UH...
TRUST?

740
00:28:03,315 --> 00:28:04,317
HMM.

741
00:28:04,350 --> 00:28:05,352
YOU CAN KEEP THE OPAL.

742
00:28:05,385 --> 00:28:07,120
I'LL TAKE THE GUN.

743
00:28:07,153 --> 00:28:08,922
SORRY. THERE'S A SEVEN-DAY
WAITING PERIOD ON THAT GUN.

744
00:28:08,955 --> 00:28:13,593
HUH.

745
00:28:13,627 --> 00:28:16,763
- OKAY.
- GOOD DEAL.

746
00:28:16,797 --> 00:28:18,998
ONE, TWO, THREE,
GRAB IT.

747
00:28:19,032 --> 00:28:20,433
- WAIT.
- IT'S A FOOTBALL PHONE.

748
00:28:20,467 --> 00:28:22,568
THERE MIGHT BE OTHER JEWELS
HIDDEN IN THE CAVE.

749
00:28:22,602 --> 00:28:24,237
HMM.

750
00:28:24,270 --> 00:28:26,372
I'LL BET OURS
ISN'T THE ONLY ONE.

751
00:28:26,405 --> 00:28:27,807
LET'S LOOK,
NOW THAT WE'RE IN HERE.

752
00:28:27,840 --> 00:28:28,975
HEY, STEVE, DEAD BUDDY,

753
00:28:29,008 --> 00:28:30,443
DO YOU THINK
THAT WAS SMART OF ME

754
00:28:30,477 --> 00:28:31,878
TO GET THE GUN
FOR THE OPAL?

755
00:28:31,912 --> 00:28:33,913
- I DID IT FOR YOU.
- [IMITATES GUN FIRING] OOH!

756
00:28:38,518 --> 00:28:40,653
MM. NIPPLE?

757
00:28:40,687 --> 00:28:42,022
NOW TO DESECRATE
THE BODY.

758
00:28:42,055 --> 00:28:45,692
HEY, THAT'S MY FAMILY.

759
00:28:45,758 --> 00:28:47,760
WONDER WHAT HIS SIGN WAS.
SCORPIO?

760
00:28:47,793 --> 00:28:48,795
[LAUGHTER]

761
00:28:48,828 --> 00:28:51,497
- WITH THE BUG AND THE--
- BING.

762
00:28:56,837 --> 00:28:57,937
TICKLE. TICKLE.

763
00:28:57,970 --> 00:29:00,173
NO ORGAN DONOR CARD.

764
00:29:00,207 --> 00:29:02,675
[IMITATES CRYING]

765
00:29:02,708 --> 00:29:04,677
YOU KNOW,
IT'S A BRUNSWICK.

766
00:29:04,710 --> 00:29:07,047
I'M GONNA BOWL A 300
WITH THIS BABY.

767
00:29:13,653 --> 00:29:16,588
[IMITATES CRYING]

768
00:29:21,660 --> 00:29:23,597
OH, HEY,
THAT'S NOT BEING SUPPORTIVE

769
00:29:23,630 --> 00:29:25,165
OF YOUR FRIEND'S FEELINGS.

770
00:29:25,198 --> 00:29:27,800
AT LEAST HE'S LIGHTING
A FEW CANDLES FOR THE GUY.

771
00:29:27,833 --> 00:29:30,870
YEAH, THAT'S GOOD.

772
00:29:30,903 --> 00:29:32,638
I DON'T THINK
THOSE ARE CANDLES.

773
00:29:32,672 --> 00:29:35,040
SPARKLERS.

774
00:29:37,677 --> 00:29:40,647
AW, THE ROADRUNNER'S
NEVER GONNA FALL FOR THIS.

775
00:29:40,680 --> 00:29:43,382
[MUTTERS]
HUH?

776
00:29:43,415 --> 00:29:44,417
SURPRISE!

777
00:29:44,450 --> 00:29:49,022
HAPPY BIRTHDAY TO YOU.

778
00:29:49,055 --> 00:29:50,055
OH.

779
00:29:50,088 --> 00:29:53,225
FILMED IN SENSURROUND.

780
00:29:53,258 --> 00:29:56,963
IRWIN ALLEN.

781
00:29:56,997 --> 00:29:59,065
AH, SHOOT. I SHOULD HAVE BEEN
OUT OF THE CAVE FIRST.

782
00:29:59,098 --> 00:30:00,098
WHAT WAS I THINKING?

783
00:30:00,132 --> 00:30:01,133
NOTE TO MYSELF--

784
00:30:01,167 --> 00:30:02,902
GET OUT OF CAVE
BEFORE BLOWING IT UP.

785
00:30:07,307 --> 00:30:11,077
ME AND MY BOOTY.

786
00:30:11,110 --> 00:30:12,612
SPEAKING OF.

787
00:30:12,645 --> 00:30:14,313
[CLEARS THROAT]

788
00:30:14,347 --> 00:30:16,782
EASY ON THE VERMOUTH, PLEASE.

789
00:30:16,815 --> 00:30:19,485
AND SHAKEN, NOT STIRRED.
PLEASE.

790
00:30:24,557 --> 00:30:26,893
OH, MY SALAD.
I'M KIDDING.

791
00:30:30,997 --> 00:30:32,565
COME HERE.

792
00:30:32,598 --> 00:30:34,867
NOW!

793
00:30:34,900 --> 00:30:36,870
GUESS NOT.

794
00:30:40,207 --> 00:30:43,442
SAIGON. CAN'T BELIEVE
I'M STILL IN SAIGON.

795
00:30:47,247 --> 00:30:49,215
AW, HE'S MISSING THE LUAU.

796
00:30:49,248 --> 00:30:52,118
[DISTANT DRUMS PLAYING]

797
00:30:52,152 --> 00:30:54,920
OH, HE CAN WAIT.

798
00:30:54,953 --> 00:30:57,123
WHAT AM I DOING
IN THIS PLACE?

799
00:30:57,157 --> 00:30:59,858
WE FOUND YOU IN TIME.

800
00:30:59,892 --> 00:31:02,428
YOU WOULD HAVE BEEN DEAD...

801
00:31:02,462 --> 00:31:03,797
MINUTES LATER.

802
00:31:03,830 --> 00:31:05,698
BUT DON'T THINK THAT WE
SAVED YOU OUT OF KINDNESS.

803
00:31:05,765 --> 00:31:06,798
WE SIMPLY
LIKE OUR MEAT FRESH.

804
00:31:06,832 --> 00:31:08,067
IT'S FAIRLY CLEAR.

805
00:31:08,100 --> 00:31:10,437
THAT FRIEND OF YOURS
FOUND SOMETHING IN THE CAVE.

806
00:31:10,470 --> 00:31:11,803
MAYBE.

807
00:31:11,837 --> 00:31:15,308
HE'S GONE. THERE'S NO NEED
TO COVER FOR HIM.

808
00:31:15,342 --> 00:31:16,642
HE BETRAYED YOU,
DIDN'T HE?

809
00:31:16,675 --> 00:31:18,143
IN A WAY.

810
00:31:18,177 --> 00:31:20,947
HE WANTED
ALL OF WHAT WE FOUND.

811
00:31:20,980 --> 00:31:21,982
AN OPAL.

812
00:31:22,015 --> 00:31:23,015
AN OBOE?

813
00:31:23,048 --> 00:31:24,050
OPAL?

814
00:31:24,083 --> 00:31:26,218
YES, HUGE.
IT WAS AS BIG OF THAT.

815
00:31:26,252 --> 00:31:27,653
OH, YOU'RE THINKING
OF AN OCARINA.

816
00:31:27,687 --> 00:31:30,790
MY BROTHER HID THE OPAL
INSIDE THAT CAVE 20 YEARS AGO.

817
00:31:32,458 --> 00:31:33,525
HMM.

818
00:31:33,558 --> 00:31:35,762
IT WAS TO BE SHARED
BETWEEN US ALL.

819
00:31:40,132 --> 00:31:41,600
DAD, DAD,
HE SAID "OPAL" TO ME.

820
00:31:41,633 --> 00:31:44,370
I THINK
WE'RE GONNA BE MARRIED!

821
00:31:44,403 --> 00:31:47,007
OH. I'M HUNGRY.

822
00:31:47,040 --> 00:31:49,108
HEY, YOU GOT ANY TOAST, OR--
OH.

823
00:31:52,112 --> 00:31:54,513
MAN. I GOT TO GET A COAT HANGER
DOWN THIS THING.

824
00:31:54,547 --> 00:31:56,282
IT'S ITCHING LIKE A BEAR.

825
00:31:59,552 --> 00:32:02,355
[MEN SINGING OUTSIDE]

826
00:32:02,388 --> 00:32:03,422
NOW WHAT?

827
00:32:03,455 --> 00:32:04,590
[SINGING CONTINUES]

828
00:32:04,623 --> 00:32:06,792
GET YOUR POPCORN, PEANUTS,

829
00:32:06,825 --> 00:32:09,128
JEWEL THIEVES, FROSTY MALTS.

830
00:32:09,162 --> 00:32:12,232
BOB HOPE'S OUT THERE.

831
00:32:12,265 --> 00:32:15,335
I THINK OUR FRIEND'S ABOUT
TO BECOME A CASSEROLE.

832
00:32:18,805 --> 00:32:21,707
I BETTER GET A PLAN.
QUICK.

833
00:32:24,910 --> 00:32:26,012
I GOTTA THINK OF SOMETHING.

834
00:32:26,045 --> 00:32:29,515
I GOTTA GET THIS T-SHIRT
BACK TO HENRY CHINASKI.

835
00:32:29,548 --> 00:32:31,350
I TOLD HIM NOT
TO GO IN THE CAVE,

836
00:32:31,383 --> 00:32:32,718
AND NOW LOOK WHAT HAPPENS!

837
00:32:32,752 --> 00:32:35,855
OH, IT'S ALL RIGHT.
GAUGUIN'S HERE.

838
00:32:39,892 --> 00:32:41,995
TELL HIM, DAD.

839
00:32:44,963 --> 00:32:47,733
[CLEARS THROAT]

840
00:32:47,767 --> 00:32:49,735
[CLEARS THROAT]

841
00:32:49,768 --> 00:32:50,770
WHAT ARE THEY DOING?

842
00:32:50,803 --> 00:32:52,005
IT'S A LONG DRUM SOLO.

843
00:32:52,038 --> 00:32:54,840
IT'S NOT YOUR PLACE TO ASK.

844
00:32:54,873 --> 00:32:56,042
THEY ARE PRAYING.

845
00:32:56,075 --> 00:32:59,978
TO WARD OFF THE CURSE
OF THE GODS.

846
00:33:00,012 --> 00:33:01,347
CURSE OF THE GODS?

847
00:33:01,380 --> 00:33:04,750
DO NOT SCORN WHAT EVEN SCIENCE
CANNOT EXPLAIN.

848
00:33:04,783 --> 00:33:06,785
SOMETHING TERRIBLE
WILL HAPPEN...

849
00:33:06,818 --> 00:33:08,420
DIDN'T SOMETHING TERRIBLE
JUST HAPPEN?

850
00:33:08,453 --> 00:33:11,590
THOUSANDS AND THOUSANDS OF LIVES
DEPEND ON ITS RETURN.

851
00:33:13,525 --> 00:33:15,227
I SEE.

852
00:33:15,260 --> 00:33:17,097
THE OPAL'S
WORTH THAT MUCH, HUH?

853
00:33:17,130 --> 00:33:19,265
WHAT YOU FOUND
HAS NO MONETARY VALUE.

854
00:33:19,298 --> 00:33:22,502
OH, TAKE THE MARBLES
OUT OF YOUR MOUTH, OLD MAN.

855
00:33:22,535 --> 00:33:24,470
SO, UH, WHOSE LINE IS IT?

856
00:33:24,503 --> 00:33:27,273
YOURS, MINE?
ARE WE DONE?

857
00:33:27,307 --> 00:33:29,442
IS THAT A WRAP?
OH, WE'RE STILL ROLLING.

858
00:33:29,475 --> 00:33:31,110
[CLEARS THROAT]

859
00:33:31,143 --> 00:33:33,612
DOCTOR, LET ME GET IT BACK
FROM JAPAN.

860
00:33:33,645 --> 00:33:34,980
NO, YOU CAN'T.

861
00:33:35,013 --> 00:33:38,217
YOU'RE A GIRL.

862
00:33:38,250 --> 00:33:39,252
I WILL GO.

863
00:33:39,285 --> 00:33:40,420
OH, NO.

864
00:33:40,453 --> 00:33:41,420
YOU HAVE YOUR PATIENTS HERE

865
00:33:41,453 --> 00:33:42,455
WHO NEED YOU DESPERATELY.

866
00:33:42,488 --> 00:33:44,257
I WILL GO TO JAPAN.

867
00:33:44,290 --> 00:33:45,290
YOU CAN'T.

868
00:33:45,290 --> 00:33:46,892
YOU'VE NEVER
EVEN BEEN THERE.

869
00:33:46,925 --> 00:33:48,928
IT WOULDN'T BE SANE
FOR YOU TO GO OFF ALONE.

870
00:33:48,962 --> 00:33:49,962
I HAVE NO CHOICE.

871
00:33:49,995 --> 00:33:52,098
I MUST TRY
TO SAVE THESE PEOPLE.

872
00:33:52,132 --> 00:33:53,967
MY CHILD.

873
00:33:54,000 --> 00:33:55,768
ASK HIM TO GO WITH ME.

874
00:33:55,802 --> 00:33:59,072
LISTEN. THE THING YOU FOUND
WASN'T A GEM.

875
00:33:59,105 --> 00:34:00,973
YOU STILL THINK
THAT IT WAS AN OPAL?

876
00:34:01,007 --> 00:34:02,208
WELL, YEAH.
WHO DOESN'T?

877
00:34:02,242 --> 00:34:03,877
WE'RE AFRAID
MISFORTUNE WILL FOLLOW.

878
00:34:03,910 --> 00:34:05,545
THAT'S WHY WE ARE PRAYING.

879
00:34:05,578 --> 00:34:08,147
YOU DON'T EXPECT ME
TO BELIEVE THAT STORY, DO YOU?

880
00:34:08,180 --> 00:34:09,182
HA.

881
00:34:09,215 --> 00:34:11,217
SOMETHING TERRIBLE
WILL HAPPEN NOW.

882
00:34:11,250 --> 00:34:14,320
THE LEGEND WARNS
THAT THE GODS WILL BE ANGRY.

883
00:34:14,353 --> 00:34:16,588
YOU'VE DISOBEYED THE ORDER.

884
00:34:16,622 --> 00:34:19,158
NONE OF US HAS EVER DARED
TO VISIT THE VALLEY.

885
00:34:19,225 --> 00:34:20,392
HO, HO, HO.

886
00:34:20,427 --> 00:34:22,528
YOU'VE TOUCHED SOMETHING
EVIL AND FORBIDDEN.

887
00:34:22,562 --> 00:34:23,628
OH, I SUPPOSE
YOU'RE PERFECT.

888
00:34:23,662 --> 00:34:24,930
WHAT IT CAN BE,
I DON'T KNOW,

889
00:34:24,963 --> 00:34:26,565
BUT IT'S CERTAINLY
NOT A GEM.

890
00:34:36,742 --> 00:34:39,212
HEY, IT'S THE START
OF BONANZA.

891
00:34:39,245 --> 00:34:40,345
HOSS, LITTLE JOE.

892
00:34:40,378 --> 00:34:43,482
THANK GOD THEY USED DOWNEY.

893
00:34:53,158 --> 00:34:57,763
THE TIME TUNNEL. IN COLOR.

894
00:34:57,797 --> 00:34:58,932
I THINK IT'S MACKEREL

895
00:34:58,965 --> 00:35:01,233
WITH CHEESE SAUCE
AND A DOLLOP OF CREAM.

896
00:35:05,170 --> 00:35:06,605
OR MAYBE NOT.

897
00:35:06,638 --> 00:35:08,640
IT'S OUT OF FOCUS,
WHATEVER IT IS.

898
00:35:08,673 --> 00:35:10,175
A PIECE OF LIVER.

899
00:35:10,208 --> 00:35:13,178
THIS MOVIE IS FASCINATING.

900
00:35:13,212 --> 00:35:15,815
NOT.

901
00:35:15,848 --> 00:35:18,617
YOU KNOW, I THINK
IT'S A BALLPARK FRANK.

902
00:35:18,650 --> 00:35:20,418
SEE, IT'S PLUMPING
AS HE COOKS IT.

903
00:35:20,452 --> 00:35:23,422
OH.

904
00:35:23,455 --> 00:35:25,323
WELL, I THINK WE'VE
PRETTY MUCH DETERMINED

905
00:35:25,357 --> 00:35:26,825
THAT IT IS NOT AN OPAL.

906
00:35:26,858 --> 00:35:28,127
UGH.

907
00:35:28,160 --> 00:35:31,930
NOTHING SAYS LOVING
LIKE SOMETHING FROM THE OVEN.

908
00:35:31,963 --> 00:35:35,668
CAUTION--FILLING IS HOT.
AND ALIVE.

909
00:35:38,003 --> 00:35:39,538
[WITH FRENCH ACCENT]
AND SO THE EGG,

910
00:35:39,572 --> 00:35:41,340
YOUNG AND BLUE,

911
00:35:41,373 --> 00:35:43,575
SEARCHES FOR ITS MOTHER.

912
00:35:46,212 --> 00:35:47,713
HEY, LITTLE MUC-Y GUY.

913
00:35:47,747 --> 00:35:48,982
[HORN ECHOING]

914
00:35:49,015 --> 00:35:51,483
HEY, SONNY ROLLINS IS PRACTICING
ON THE BRIDGE AGAIN.

915
00:35:51,517 --> 00:35:53,853
HEY, DOCTOR.
PLAY ONE MORE GAME, HUH?

916
00:35:53,887 --> 00:35:57,055
WELL, I HOPE THAT
I'LL BE ABLE TO WIN IT.

917
00:35:57,088 --> 00:35:58,357
SOMEBODY GET THAT GUY A BRA.

918
00:35:58,390 --> 00:35:59,558
IT'S GETTING LATE.

919
00:35:59,592 --> 00:36:01,860
WE AREN'T GOING TO SHORE
TILL TOMORROW.

920
00:36:01,893 --> 00:36:02,962
AREN'T WE?

921
00:36:02,995 --> 00:36:05,130
THE SICK BAY DOOR
WON'T OPEN.

922
00:36:05,163 --> 00:36:06,165
HEY, LOOK. IT'S A CLOWN.

923
00:36:06,198 --> 00:36:07,200
OPEN IT.

924
00:36:07,233 --> 00:36:08,400
PUT THIS FLOWER THERE.

925
00:36:08,433 --> 00:36:10,202
I WANT TO GIVE IT
TO YOUR DEAD FRIEND.

926
00:36:10,235 --> 00:36:12,272
NOT NOW.
SOME OTHER TIME.

927
00:36:12,305 --> 00:36:13,505
HEY, IT'S THE DJ
FROM DEEE-LIGHT.

928
00:36:13,538 --> 00:36:16,508
YOU SEE,
MY FATHER DIED ON THAT ISLAND.

929
00:36:16,542 --> 00:36:18,177
SO YOUR FRIEND
DOESN'T SEEM

930
00:36:18,210 --> 00:36:19,712
LIKE A STRANGER TO ME.

931
00:36:19,778 --> 00:36:22,515
OPEN IT.

932
00:36:22,548 --> 00:36:23,715
PLEASE GIVE HIM THE KEY.

933
00:36:23,748 --> 00:36:25,585
I GOT BOARDWALK,
PARK PLACE.

934
00:36:25,618 --> 00:36:27,520
OH!

935
00:36:27,553 --> 00:36:31,290
HEY, WHO TOOK THE TIRES
OFF THE DOCK?

936
00:36:31,323 --> 00:36:35,193
NEXT WEEK ON "VOYAGE
TO THE BOTTOM OF THE SEA."

937
00:36:35,227 --> 00:36:37,230
WHAT'S GOING ON HERE?

938
00:36:37,263 --> 00:36:39,865
ENGINE ROOM.
GIVE ME THE ENGINE ROOM.

939
00:36:39,898 --> 00:36:42,935
CAPTAIN. CAPTAIN.

940
00:36:42,968 --> 00:36:44,937
UH-OH.

941
00:36:44,970 --> 00:36:46,972
GOODBYE, MOM. BYE.

942
00:36:47,005 --> 00:36:49,142
HEY, JAKE AND ELWOOD.

943
00:36:49,175 --> 00:36:50,810
HMM.

944
00:36:50,843 --> 00:36:54,613
CAB CALLOWAY.

945
00:36:54,647 --> 00:36:55,648
THAT'S A SHIP.

946
00:36:55,682 --> 00:36:57,115
WHAT'S HAPPENING.

947
00:36:57,148 --> 00:37:01,087
TOY BOAT.
TOY BOAT. TOY BOAT.

948
00:37:01,120 --> 00:37:04,523
HIRATA, YOU SURE
THEY'VE GOT THE OPAL?

949
00:37:05,925 --> 00:37:07,460
ALL RIGHT, THEN.
LET ME SEE IT.

950
00:37:07,493 --> 00:37:09,695
YOU'RE ASKING
A VERY HIGH PRICE.

951
00:37:09,728 --> 00:37:11,230
YES, YES.

952
00:37:11,263 --> 00:37:12,765
I KNOW.

953
00:37:12,798 --> 00:37:16,635
OOH, AT 7:00 A.M.
THE MAIN HATCHWAY CAVED IN.

954
00:37:16,668 --> 00:37:17,670
WRECK OF
THE ELLA FITZGERALD.

955
00:37:17,703 --> 00:37:19,938
HEY, ADAM CLAYTON POWELL.

956
00:37:23,275 --> 00:37:24,710
ABANDON SHIP!

957
00:37:24,743 --> 00:37:25,745
[ALL SHOUTING]

958
00:37:25,778 --> 00:37:28,413
AAH! PANIC!

959
00:37:28,447 --> 00:37:30,548
WHAT'S HAPPENED
TO THE SHIP?

960
00:37:30,582 --> 00:37:32,183
IT BLEW UP.

961
00:37:32,217 --> 00:37:34,653
HEY, IT'S FUNNY GIRL,
AND THERE'S BARBRA STREISAND.

962
00:37:37,457 --> 00:37:39,158
McHALE!

963
00:37:39,192 --> 00:37:40,627
TAXI. OH.

964
00:37:40,660 --> 00:37:41,660
TAXI. OH.

965
00:37:41,693 --> 00:37:43,462
CAB! GOING UPTOWN.

966
00:37:43,495 --> 00:37:46,832
JEEP? OH.

967
00:37:46,865 --> 00:37:48,233
WELCOME TO ELLIS ISLAND.

968
00:37:48,267 --> 00:37:49,635
YOUR NAME IS NOW BOB SMITH.

969
00:37:49,668 --> 00:37:52,103
ANDOLINI?
NO, YOU'RE NOW CORLEONE.

970
00:37:52,137 --> 00:37:53,538
AND I THINK
I'LL NAME YOU APPETITE.

971
00:37:53,572 --> 00:37:57,743
THANK YOU. HOPE YOU ENJOYED
YOUR NORWEGIAN PRINCESS CRUISE.

972
00:37:57,777 --> 00:38:00,312
TAKE THE AMBULANCE
OVER THERE.

973
00:38:00,345 --> 00:38:02,615
TAKE THAT BLANKET.

974
00:38:02,648 --> 00:38:05,050
OOPS. I WET 'EM.

975
00:38:05,083 --> 00:38:07,820
HEY, DID YOU EVER
SEE THE MOVIE PAPILLON?

976
00:38:10,155 --> 00:38:12,123
I--I SAVED THIS.

977
00:38:12,190 --> 00:38:14,560
HEY, THEY'RE GIVING AWAY
FREE CLOTHES OVER THERE.

978
00:38:14,593 --> 00:38:16,562
I WAS LUCKY.
SOMETHING IMPORTANT.

979
00:38:16,595 --> 00:38:18,463
SOMETHING IMPORTANT TOO.

980
00:38:18,497 --> 00:38:20,098
WHAT DO YOU GOT THERE?

981
00:38:20,132 --> 00:38:23,468
YOUR FRIEND'S BONES.

982
00:38:23,502 --> 00:38:24,837
YOU CAN KEEP 'EM, YOU FOOL.

983
00:38:24,870 --> 00:38:27,440
- HUH?
- THEY'RE PIGS' BONES.

984
00:38:27,473 --> 00:38:31,043
WAH, WAH, WAH.

985
00:38:31,077 --> 00:38:33,012
PIGS' BONES?

986
00:38:33,045 --> 00:38:34,880
EXCUSE ME. HAVE YOU
COME FROM THAT SHIP?

987
00:38:34,913 --> 00:38:35,915
I HAVE.

988
00:38:35,948 --> 00:38:37,517
DO YOU KNOW
WHERE KEISUKE IS?

989
00:38:37,550 --> 00:38:38,550
WHO'D YOU SAY?

990
00:38:38,583 --> 00:38:39,652
CASEY KASEM?

991
00:38:39,685 --> 00:38:41,753
UH, HE WAS A SEAMEN
ON THE SAME SHIP.

992
00:38:41,787 --> 00:38:42,822
UH, LET ME SEE.

993
00:38:42,855 --> 00:38:45,057
EH, LET'S SEE.
I'M A PSYCHIC.

994
00:38:45,090 --> 00:38:46,392
THE GREAT CARNAC.

995
00:38:46,458 --> 00:38:47,693
LET ME SEE, UM...

996
00:38:47,727 --> 00:38:49,628
ONODERA! ONODERA.

997
00:38:49,662 --> 00:38:50,697
- HUH?
- HMM.

998
00:38:50,730 --> 00:38:51,897
THANK HEAVENS
YOU'RE ALL RIGHT.

999
00:38:51,930 --> 00:38:53,465
[MUTTERS]

1000
00:38:53,498 --> 00:38:56,768
BUT WHERE'S MY BROTHER?
KEISUKE.

1001
00:38:56,802 --> 00:38:58,103
CASEY KASEM?

1002
00:38:58,137 --> 00:38:59,138
BAD NEWS.

1003
00:38:59,172 --> 00:39:01,473
WHAT'S HAPPENED TO HIM THEN?

1004
00:39:01,507 --> 00:39:02,775
BAD NEWS.

1005
00:39:02,808 --> 00:39:03,808
SORRY.

1006
00:39:03,842 --> 00:39:04,843
[BRITISH ACCENT]
SORRY.

1007
00:39:04,877 --> 00:39:05,878
HE'S DEAD.

1008
00:39:05,912 --> 00:39:07,345
HUH?

1009
00:39:07,380 --> 00:39:09,382
HE'S...DEAD?

1010
00:39:09,415 --> 00:39:11,750
MM.
HE SLIPPED AND FELL.

1011
00:39:11,783 --> 00:39:13,318
ONTO SOME LIVE GRENADES.

1012
00:39:13,352 --> 00:39:15,187
SHH.

1013
00:39:15,220 --> 00:39:16,622
KAWAJIRI TOO.

1014
00:39:16,655 --> 00:39:17,857
KAWAJIRI? COWABUNGA.

1015
00:39:17,890 --> 00:39:21,493
I SEARCHED FOR THEM BOTH.
THROUGH THE WHOLE CAVE.

1016
00:39:21,527 --> 00:39:23,028
FOR ABOUT TEN SECONDS.

1017
00:39:23,062 --> 00:39:25,363
BUT I COULDN'T
FIND THEIR BODIES.

1018
00:39:25,397 --> 00:39:26,398
IT WAS TERRIBLE.

1019
00:39:26,432 --> 00:39:27,867
DID YOU FIND THE GEM?

1020
00:39:27,900 --> 00:39:29,302
DID YOU?
I WANNA LOOK AT IT.

1021
00:39:29,335 --> 00:39:31,603
OF COURSE. I'VE GOT IT.

1022
00:39:31,637 --> 00:39:33,605
IS IT TRUE? IS IT?

1023
00:39:33,638 --> 00:39:35,207
LET ME SEE IT THEN.

1024
00:39:35,240 --> 00:39:37,142
THE OPAL SANK
WHEN THE SHIP DID.

1025
00:39:37,175 --> 00:39:39,010
HMM?

1026
00:39:39,043 --> 00:39:41,647
I WAS KEEPING IT SAFE
BY HIDING IT IN MY CABIN.

1027
00:39:41,680 --> 00:39:43,115
I DON'T BELIEVE YOU!

1028
00:39:43,148 --> 00:39:44,350
WELL,
I'M TELLING YOU THE TRUTH.

1029
00:39:44,383 --> 00:39:45,985
ALL RIGHT,
IT WASN'T MY CABIN.

1030
00:39:46,018 --> 00:39:48,420
THE SEA ISN'T VERY DEEP
RIGHT HERE.

1031
00:39:48,453 --> 00:39:51,390
A DIVER CAN RETRIEVE IT.

1032
00:39:51,423 --> 00:39:54,427
NO, NO, NO.
UH, UH, UH, UH.

1033
00:39:54,460 --> 00:39:56,662
NO, NO, NO, NO, NO. NO.

1034
00:39:56,695 --> 00:39:58,530
YOU'RE A FOOL TO THINK
WE'LL EVER GET IT BACK.

1035
00:39:58,563 --> 00:40:00,432
YOU CALL ME
WHEN I'VE FOUND IT.

1036
00:40:00,465 --> 00:40:02,502
TILL THEN,
I'LL KEEP MY MONEY.

1037
00:40:02,535 --> 00:40:03,535
GOODBYE.

1038
00:40:03,568 --> 00:40:04,637
WELL,
IT'S DOWN TO ME AND YOU

1039
00:40:04,670 --> 00:40:07,038
AND ME AND PART OF YOUR EYE.

1040
00:40:07,072 --> 00:40:08,540
BELIEVE ME?

1041
00:40:08,573 --> 00:40:10,242
HEY! WHAT'S THAT?

1042
00:40:10,275 --> 00:40:12,143
IT'S YOUR FINGER,
AND IT'S POINTING.

1043
00:40:12,177 --> 00:40:13,612
DOPE.

1044
00:40:13,645 --> 00:40:15,547
OH, IT'S THE GHOST
OF ESTHER WILLIAMS.

1045
00:40:15,580 --> 00:40:17,550
IT'S--NO, IT'S MR. BUBBLE,

1046
00:40:17,583 --> 00:40:19,818
AND BOY IS HE CHEESED.

1047
00:40:21,687 --> 00:40:23,222
IT'S A MR. BUBBLE
POOL PARTY.

1048
00:40:24,590 --> 00:40:27,627
HELP, POLICE, THERE'S A MAN
IN THE BATHTUB.

1049
00:40:27,660 --> 00:40:28,960
STOP, GRANDMA.
IT'S ME.

1050
00:40:28,993 --> 00:40:30,128
WHAT'LL WE DO?

1051
00:40:30,162 --> 00:40:32,430
WE NEED MORE CALGON.

1052
00:40:35,033 --> 00:40:37,102
THERE ARE TWO
JAPANESE ARMY JEEPS

1053
00:40:37,135 --> 00:40:38,903
IN THE LOT
WITH THEIR LIGHTS ON.

1054
00:40:44,443 --> 00:40:47,012
OH!

1055
00:40:47,045 --> 00:40:48,613
LOOK AT THAT!

1056
00:40:48,647 --> 00:40:51,117
HI, THERE.
I'M A JUICY NEW CHARACTER.

1057
00:40:51,150 --> 00:40:52,317
ENJOY ME.

1058
00:40:52,350 --> 00:40:53,885
I'M WHAT'S KNOWN
AS THE COMPLICATION.

1059
00:40:53,918 --> 00:40:56,888
THE ANTAGONIST, IF YOU WILL.

1060
00:40:56,922 --> 00:40:59,292
AAH!

1061
00:40:59,325 --> 00:41:00,725
WELL, FOR MY FIRST NUMBER,

1062
00:41:00,758 --> 00:41:02,227
I'D LIKE
TO CRASH A WAREHOUSE.

1063
00:41:02,260 --> 00:41:04,197
IT'S AN OLD FAVORITE.
I THINK YOU'RE GONNA LIKE IT.

1064
00:41:04,230 --> 00:41:07,132
IT GOES
SOMETHING LIKE THIS.

1065
00:41:10,002 --> 00:41:12,337
THANK YOU.
THANK YOU VERY MUCH.

1066
00:41:12,370 --> 00:41:14,005
I DID THAT
ON THE SULLIVAN SHOW,

1067
00:41:14,038 --> 00:41:16,208
BUT, UH, THEY ONLY FILMED ME
FROM THE WAIST UP.

1068
00:41:16,242 --> 00:41:17,577
THEY SAY I FLIPPED 'EM OFF,

1069
00:41:17,610 --> 00:41:21,680
BUT IT'S JUST THE WAY
MY FINGERS ARE CONSTRUCTED.

1070
00:41:21,713 --> 00:41:23,148
IF GAMERA CRAVES FIRE,

1071
00:41:23,182 --> 00:41:24,283
WHAT DOES BARUGON CRAVE?

1072
00:41:24,317 --> 00:41:27,252
UH, BEN AND JERRY'S
CHERRY GARCIA.

1073
00:41:27,285 --> 00:41:28,887
NATCH.

1074
00:41:28,920 --> 00:41:30,890
HEY,
I'M DOING MY OWN STUNTS.

1075
00:41:30,923 --> 00:41:32,592
IF WHOLESOME,
FAMILY ENTERTAINMENT

1076
00:41:32,658 --> 00:41:35,493
IS OLD-FASHIONED
THEN CALL ME OLD-FASHIONED.

1077
00:41:39,030 --> 00:41:40,698
HEY, HEY,
LOOK AT THE CLOWN JEEP.

1078
00:41:40,732 --> 00:41:43,602
OH.

1079
00:41:43,635 --> 00:41:44,637
COME, TINY TIM.

1080
00:41:44,670 --> 00:41:49,508
OH, BLESS US, EVERYONE.

1081
00:41:49,542 --> 00:41:52,010
YEAH,
LET'S GET OUT OF HERE!

1082
00:41:52,043 --> 00:41:54,513
WAIT! ONODERA!

1083
00:41:54,547 --> 00:41:56,048
WAIT TILL
WE GET BACK TO OSAKA.

1084
00:41:59,183 --> 00:42:00,385
WHAT'D HE SAY?

1085
00:42:00,418 --> 00:42:02,555
WELL, ROUGHLY TRANSLATED,
IT MEANS "BEAT CHEEKS."

1086
00:42:02,588 --> 00:42:06,992
OH.

1087
00:42:06,992 --> 00:42:08,127
HEY, DRAG THAT NURSE ALONG.

1088
00:42:08,160 --> 00:42:11,897
SHE MIGHT COME IN HANDY.

1089
00:42:11,930 --> 00:42:14,032
OH, HE'S LEAKING.
UGH.

1090
00:42:17,970 --> 00:42:19,705
LIKE IT SO FAR? BUT WAIT.
THERE'S MORE.

1091
00:42:19,738 --> 00:42:21,973
THIS SERRATED EDGE
WILL SLICE TOMATOES SO THIN

1092
00:42:22,007 --> 00:42:23,208
YOU CAN SEE
RIGHT THROUGH THEM.

1093
00:42:23,242 --> 00:42:25,443
ABOUT THIS TIME,
MOST FOLKS ARE WONDERING

1094
00:42:25,477 --> 00:42:26,478
AM I A DOG?

1095
00:42:26,512 --> 00:42:28,047
I DON'T EVEN KNOW.
RUFF RUFF.

1096
00:42:28,080 --> 00:42:29,948
JUST KIDDING.

1097
00:42:35,553 --> 00:42:38,590
OH, NO. HE THINKS
IT'S A GIANT FIRE HYDRANT.

1098
00:42:38,623 --> 00:42:39,958
DON'T LIFT YOUR LEG, BOY.

1099
00:42:40,025 --> 00:42:42,260
I THINK, UH...

1100
00:42:42,293 --> 00:42:43,428
WHY DON'T YOU
TREAT YOURSELF?

1101
00:42:43,462 --> 00:42:45,597
YOU'RE A GROWING MONSTER.
GO AHEAD.

1102
00:42:48,567 --> 00:42:50,768
WHOA. HE GOT THAT
FROM GENE SIMMONS.

1103
00:42:50,802 --> 00:42:53,605
I'M YOUR BOYFRIEND NOW.
BLAGH!

1104
00:42:55,907 --> 00:42:57,242
- TIME TO GO?
- TIME TO GO.

1105
00:42:57,308 --> 00:42:59,077
- AW.
- COME ON.

1106
00:42:59,110 --> 00:43:00,545
I WANNA WATCH THE PUPPY.

1107
00:43:16,262 --> 00:43:17,663
JUST A BEER
AND A BUMP SOMETIMES.

1108
00:43:17,697 --> 00:43:19,097
OH, BUT I NEVER
REALLY DRINK ANYTHING.

1109
00:43:19,130 --> 00:43:20,798
YOU KNOW THAT.
I'LL HAVE THE OCCASIONAL
LIGHT BEER,

1110
00:43:20,832 --> 00:43:22,167
AND MERLE LIKES
HIS SCOTCH, YA KNOW.

1111
00:43:22,200 --> 00:43:23,868
BUT ANYWAY,
YOU'LL NEVER BELIEVE

1112
00:43:23,902 --> 00:43:25,937
WHAT MARGARET TOLD ME
ABOUT THE STEWARD BOY.

1113
00:43:25,972 --> 00:43:27,505
OH, I AM DYING.
JUST TELL ME.

1114
00:43:27,538 --> 00:43:28,607
APPARENTLY WHAT HE'S INTO--

1115
00:43:28,640 --> 00:43:30,708
OKAY,
HOW WAS EVERYTHING, LADIES?

1116
00:43:30,742 --> 00:43:32,343
OH, YOU REALLY DID A NUMBER

1117
00:43:32,377 --> 00:43:35,847
ON THIS MEXI-CITA FAJITA
SUPER BELL GRANDE TREAT-A,
DIDN'T YOU?

1118
00:43:35,880 --> 00:43:37,448
OH, IT WAS GOOD,
AND SO FILLING.

1119
00:43:37,482 --> 00:43:38,917
OH, YES.
EVERYTHING'S JUST WONDERFUL.

1120
00:43:38,950 --> 00:43:40,118
I'M REALLY FULL.

1121
00:43:40,152 --> 00:43:42,353
OKAY, GOOD.
WELL, I'M GONNA BE HEADING BACK

1122
00:43:42,387 --> 00:43:43,955
TO GET THE DESERT TRAY,

1123
00:43:43,988 --> 00:43:45,290
AND, UH,
DO YOU WANT ANYTHING?

1124
00:43:45,323 --> 00:43:47,092
COFFEE, TEA,
SHOT OF TEQUILA?

1125
00:43:47,092 --> 00:43:48,093
HUH?

1126
00:43:48,127 --> 00:43:49,160
[LAUGHTER]

1127
00:43:49,193 --> 00:43:50,395
HEAVENS NO. WE'RE FINE.
THANK YOU.

1128
00:43:50,428 --> 00:43:51,397
OKAY, I'LL BE RIGHT BACK.
EXCUSE ME.

1129
00:43:51,430 --> 00:43:52,998
HE IS SUPER NEAT
AND SO CREATIVE.

1130
00:43:53,032 --> 00:43:54,367
OH, HONEY, THEY ALL ARE.

1131
00:43:54,400 --> 00:43:55,833
THIS IS MY FAVORITE PLACE
TO COME.

1132
00:43:55,867 --> 00:43:57,002
OH, NOT EVERY DAY,

1133
00:43:57,035 --> 00:43:58,437
BUT, YOU KNOW,
A SPECIAL TREAT SOMETIMES.

1134
00:43:58,470 --> 00:44:00,305
YOU SEE ALL THE ANTIQUES
ON THE WALL HERE?

1135
00:44:00,338 --> 00:44:01,340
OH, I LOVE THEM.

1136
00:44:01,373 --> 00:44:02,507
OH, THEY DO IT UP
SO COLORFUL.

1137
00:44:02,540 --> 00:44:04,443
YOU GOTTA GET DOWN HERE
ON HALLOWEEN SOMETIME,

1138
00:44:04,477 --> 00:44:06,245
'CAUSE THEY ALL DRESS UP
IN COSTUMES

1139
00:44:06,278 --> 00:44:08,680
AND IT'S SUPER COLORFUL
AND SO MUCH FUN.

1140
00:44:08,713 --> 00:44:10,748
OKAY, HERE WE ARE, GIRLS.

1141
00:44:10,782 --> 00:44:13,152
OH, MY. OH, WE'RE
IN TROUBLE NOW, HONEY.

1142
00:44:13,185 --> 00:44:14,520
NOW OVER HERE,

1143
00:44:14,553 --> 00:44:18,223
WE'VE GOT TGI TOKYO'S
BIGGEST SELLER.

1144
00:44:18,257 --> 00:44:20,925
HERE IT IS. THE CHOCOLATE
TOWERING INFERNO,

1145
00:44:20,958 --> 00:44:22,393
AND IT IS DECADENT.

1146
00:44:22,427 --> 00:44:25,063
BUT, UH, YOU PROBABLY
DON'T LIKE CHOCOLATE, DO YOU?

1147
00:44:25,097 --> 00:44:26,432
- OH, NO, I LOVE CHOCOLATE.
- YES.

1148
00:44:26,465 --> 00:44:29,233
I'M KIDDING. OF COURSE
EVERYONE LOVES CHOCOLATE.

1149
00:44:29,267 --> 00:44:32,437
UH, THIS ONE HERE YOU PROBABLY
WOULDN'T BE INTERESTED IN.

1150
00:44:32,470 --> 00:44:34,773
I'M JUST KIDDING.
IT'S A LITTLE RICH, YOU KNOW.

1151
00:44:34,807 --> 00:44:38,377
BUT THIS IS OUR APPLE DOUBLE
MURDER SUICIDE TORT.

1152
00:44:38,410 --> 00:44:40,812
IT'S KIND OF SPICY AND IT
HAS A LITTLE RUM IN IT,

1153
00:44:40,845 --> 00:44:43,048
SO I'M GONNA HAVE
TO SEE YOUR IDs, GIRLS.

1154
00:44:43,082 --> 00:44:45,750
OH, YOU ARE SO SWEET.
SO SWEET.

1155
00:44:45,783 --> 00:44:47,418
ANYWAY,
THIS LAST ONE OVER HERE

1156
00:44:47,452 --> 00:44:49,788
IS TOO DENSE
FOR ME TO EVEN PICK UP.

1157
00:44:49,822 --> 00:44:52,257
THIS IS OUR VANILLA
CROSS-COUNTRY KILLING SPREE

1158
00:44:52,290 --> 00:44:53,492
WITH FUDGE SAUCE.

1159
00:44:53,492 --> 00:44:56,395
ONE BITE OF THIS
AND YOU LOCK TONGUES WITH LOKI,

1160
00:44:56,428 --> 00:44:58,030
EVIL GOD
OF STRIFE AND DISCORD

1161
00:44:58,063 --> 00:44:59,665
ON THE SEVENTH PLATFORM
OF HELL.

1162
00:44:59,698 --> 00:45:01,100
I'M JUST KIDDING.
IT'S A LITTLE RICH.

1163
00:45:01,133 --> 00:45:02,533
CAN I GET YOU ONE?

1164
00:45:02,567 --> 00:45:04,335
HONEY, THAT'S THE ONE
I'M GONNA HAVE THERE.

1165
00:45:04,368 --> 00:45:05,370
OH, NOTHING FOR ME, PLEASE.

1166
00:45:05,403 --> 00:45:06,405
AND A DIET PEPSI PLEASE.

1167
00:45:06,438 --> 00:45:07,438
ALL RIGHT, THAT'S GOOD.

1168
00:45:07,472 --> 00:45:09,542
UH, ONE OF THOSE
AND A DIET PEPSI.

1169
00:45:09,575 --> 00:45:11,977
I'LL GET YOU A FORK JUST IN CASE
YOU WANNA TRY IT, OKAY?

1170
00:45:12,010 --> 00:45:13,578
- HE KNOWS ME SO WELL.
- HE SURE DOES.

1171
00:45:13,612 --> 00:45:15,580
- HE'S SUCH A CUTE BOY.
- OH, SAY, WAITER.

1172
00:45:15,613 --> 00:45:16,782
- OH, WAITER?
- YEAH.

1173
00:45:16,815 --> 00:45:18,283
UH, COULD WE HAVE
SEPARATE CHECKS PLEASE?

1174
00:45:18,317 --> 00:45:20,618
UH, I'M SORRY, LADIES, WE DON'T
TO THAT HERE AT TGI TOKYO.

1175
00:45:20,652 --> 00:45:21,653
- AH, WHAT A JERK.
- NO KIDDING.

1176
00:45:21,687 --> 00:45:22,687
- UH, LADIES...
- YES?

1177
00:45:22,720 --> 00:45:26,425
- WE HAVE MOVIE SIGN!
- AAH!

1178
00:45:36,302 --> 00:45:37,803
THAT WAS JUST DELIGHTFUL.

1179
00:45:37,837 --> 00:45:38,837
OH, THAT WAS SWEET.

1180
00:45:38,870 --> 00:45:40,172
OH, YOU GOT ANY TUMS
IN THE CAR?

1181
00:45:40,205 --> 00:45:41,607
I GOT A LITTLE GAS, I THINK.

1182
00:45:41,640 --> 00:45:43,342
I GUESS WE'LL HAVE
TO POSTPONE THE SEARCH

1183
00:45:43,375 --> 00:45:45,343
UNTIL THIS MONSTER'S DEAD.

1184
00:45:45,377 --> 00:45:46,845
WE CAN'T PUT IT OFF FOREVER.

1185
00:45:46,878 --> 00:45:48,180
IT'LL BE TOO LATE.

1186
00:45:48,213 --> 00:45:50,482
THE JUNE WEDDING IS SO CLICHE.

1187
00:45:50,515 --> 00:45:51,650
...THE POLICE
AND THE INSURANCE COMPANY

1188
00:45:51,683 --> 00:45:53,018
ARE BOUND TO MESS AROUND
WITH THAT SHIP.

1189
00:45:53,052 --> 00:45:54,052
OOH, THAT'S GOOD BOOZE.

1190
00:45:54,085 --> 00:45:55,487
THEN WE'LL NEVER
GET THE OPAL BACK.

1191
00:45:55,520 --> 00:45:56,788
SO WE'LL HAVE TO ACT NOW.

1192
00:45:56,822 --> 00:45:59,323
IT'S THE ONLY CHANCE
WE'VE GOT TO FIND IT.

1193
00:45:59,357 --> 00:46:01,427
FIRST, WE'LL NEED MONEY.

1194
00:46:01,460 --> 00:46:04,362
OH, I'VE GOT QUITE A BIT
OF MONEY PUT ASIDE.

1195
00:46:04,395 --> 00:46:06,332
THAT'S GOOD. IS IT IN CASH?

1196
00:46:06,365 --> 00:46:08,067
I HAVE A DOWRY.
WE COULD LIVE WITH MY FOLKS.

1197
00:46:08,100 --> 00:46:09,400
AND WE CAN HIRE THE DIVER.

1198
00:46:09,433 --> 00:46:10,535
HIRATA! HIRATA.

1199
00:46:10,568 --> 00:46:12,905
THE MONSTER
IS GETTING NEARER TO OSAKA.

1200
00:46:12,938 --> 00:46:14,473
- WHAT?
- HUH?

1201
00:46:14,507 --> 00:46:16,542
THE RADIO SAYS SO.

1202
00:46:16,575 --> 00:46:18,543
IT'LL KILL ALL OF US.

1203
00:46:18,577 --> 00:46:20,878
LET'S LEAVE HERE.
LET'S GET OUT.

1204
00:46:20,912 --> 00:46:22,047
FINE, HONEY.
WHAT TIME'S DINNER?

1205
00:46:22,080 --> 00:46:23,715
WE HAVING RICE AGAIN?

1206
00:46:23,748 --> 00:46:26,852
WE CAN'T PULL IT UP, BECAUSE
WE'VE GOT TO LEAVE OSAKA.

1207
00:46:26,885 --> 00:46:28,287
IF WE GO NOW, WE'LL LOSE IT.

1208
00:46:28,320 --> 00:46:30,155
AFTER ALL THE RISKS I'VE TAKEN.

1209
00:46:30,188 --> 00:46:31,790
I'M LEAVING.
LET'S GO TO KOBE.

1210
00:46:31,823 --> 00:46:33,192
- IT'LL BE SAFE THERE.
- YEAH.

1211
00:46:33,225 --> 00:46:35,593
NO. I'M NOT GOING UNTIL
WE'VE BROUGHT THAT OPAL UP HERE.

1212
00:46:35,627 --> 00:46:37,095
THIS CONFUSION'S
JUST WHAT WE NEED.

1213
00:46:37,128 --> 00:46:38,163
NOBODY'LL NOTICE.

1214
00:46:38,197 --> 00:46:40,698
- NOT NOW.
- FOOL. WE'VE GOT TO.

1215
00:46:40,732 --> 00:46:43,035
NO, WE'LL HAVE TO GIVE IT UP
FOR A LITTLE WHILE.

1216
00:46:43,068 --> 00:46:44,068
I CAN'T GIVE IT UP.

1217
00:46:44,102 --> 00:46:45,903
NOT AFTER
I'VE KILLED TWO MEN.

1218
00:46:45,937 --> 00:46:47,138
- HUH?
- OH?

1219
00:46:47,172 --> 00:46:48,673
- ONODERA. ONODERA.
- WE CAN'T WAIT LONGER.

1220
00:46:48,707 --> 00:46:51,377
ONODERA,
WHAT WAS THAT YOU SAID?

1221
00:46:51,410 --> 00:46:53,278
TELL ME. YOU SAID
THAT YOU KILLED TWO MEN.

1222
00:46:53,312 --> 00:46:54,680
UH, OH,
THAT FIGURE OF SPEECH.

1223
00:46:54,713 --> 00:46:56,382
METAPHOR. HA. TEASING.

1224
00:46:56,415 --> 00:46:57,582
YOU KILLED THEM BOTH?

1225
00:46:57,615 --> 00:46:59,317
WELL,
NOT AT THE SAME TIME.

1226
00:46:59,350 --> 00:47:01,152
I ONLY MEANT THEY'VE
GIVEN THEIR LIVES FOR THIS.

1227
00:47:01,187 --> 00:47:02,353
- LIAR.
- PANTS ON FIRE.

1228
00:47:02,387 --> 00:47:03,588
YOU MURDERED MY BROTHER

1229
00:47:03,622 --> 00:47:05,223
SO THAT YOU'D HAVE
THE OPAL TO YOURSELF.

1230
00:47:05,257 --> 00:47:06,858
OF COURSE NOT.

1231
00:47:06,925 --> 00:47:08,593
MAYBE I DID.

1232
00:47:08,627 --> 00:47:09,628
YOU KILLED THEM.

1233
00:47:09,662 --> 00:47:11,863
YOU KILLED THEM BOTH
IN COLD BLOOD.

1234
00:47:11,897 --> 00:47:15,567
NO. NO.

1235
00:47:15,600 --> 00:47:16,602
[IMITATING CHOKING]

1236
00:47:16,635 --> 00:47:19,538
TINY TIM, NO!

1237
00:47:19,572 --> 00:47:20,738
OH, WHATEVER YOU DO,

1238
00:47:20,772 --> 00:47:22,707
DON'T HIT THE INFLATABLE
REINDEER. PLEASE!

1239
00:47:26,912 --> 00:47:29,347
HENRY,
THE BOYS ARE AT IT AGAIN.

1240
00:47:29,380 --> 00:47:33,518
OH.

1241
00:47:33,552 --> 00:47:36,020
YOU KILLED HIM.
YOU KILLED MY BROTHER!

1242
00:47:36,053 --> 00:47:37,488
YOU DIRTY RAT.

1243
00:47:37,522 --> 00:47:39,792
STOP IT.
STOP IT.

1244
00:47:39,825 --> 00:47:44,730
YOU'RE KILLING HIM.

1245
00:47:44,763 --> 00:47:47,765
SHOULDN'T ONE OF THEM
KNOW KUNG FU?

1246
00:47:47,798 --> 00:47:50,235
- NOT ENOUGH ROOM.
- AH.

1247
00:47:50,268 --> 00:47:52,270
THAT'S IT.
OUT YOU PIXIES GO.

1248
00:47:52,303 --> 00:47:54,840
THROUGH THE DOOR.
OUT THE WINDOW.

1249
00:47:54,873 --> 00:47:56,775
YOU'RE KILLING HIM!

1250
00:47:56,808 --> 00:47:58,843
HEY, SHE'S GOT MONEY ON YOU.
DON'T LOSE.

1251
00:48:06,418 --> 00:48:09,320
NO! PLEASE!

1252
00:48:09,353 --> 00:48:10,455
HEY.

1253
00:48:10,488 --> 00:48:11,723
DON'T WORRY.
SHE'S A STUNT MOM.

1254
00:48:11,757 --> 00:48:14,860
OOH. OH.

1255
00:48:18,330 --> 00:48:20,798
OW.

1256
00:48:20,832 --> 00:48:22,500
OH, GREAT. FINISH HIM OFF
WITH A BOWLING LOCKER.

1257
00:48:22,533 --> 00:48:25,570
OH, THAT HAD TO HURT.
WITH HIS BAD BACK?

1258
00:48:25,603 --> 00:48:28,173
...ALL RESIDENTS
MUST EVACUATE OSAKA AT ONCE.

1259
00:48:28,207 --> 00:48:29,207
DO NOT DELAY.

1260
00:48:29,240 --> 00:48:31,577
NOW WHERE ARE THOSE
RAFFLE TICKETS?

1261
00:48:31,610 --> 00:48:35,413
ONODERA. SAVE ME.

1262
00:48:35,447 --> 00:48:37,282
GET ME OUT OF HERE.

1263
00:48:37,315 --> 00:48:39,918
FORGET THE LUNCH
AND GO FOR THE WALLET.

1264
00:48:39,952 --> 00:48:41,987
MM-HMM.

1265
00:48:43,322 --> 00:48:44,288
SAVE ME!

1266
00:48:44,322 --> 00:48:47,258
LET'S SEE.
PICK SIX...

1267
00:48:47,292 --> 00:48:49,160
THANKS FOR A LOVELY DINNER.

1268
00:48:49,193 --> 00:48:53,865
[ALL SHOUTING]

1269
00:48:53,898 --> 00:48:55,467
AREN'T YOU GLAD
YOU USED DIAL?

1270
00:48:55,500 --> 00:48:58,903
DON'T YOU WISH
EVERYONE DID?

1271
00:48:58,937 --> 00:49:00,038
WHEW.

1272
00:49:00,072 --> 00:49:01,038
LET'S GET OUT!

1273
00:49:01,072 --> 00:49:03,808
SMELLS LIKE
A DEAD CAT IN THERE.

1274
00:49:03,842 --> 00:49:05,843
NICE WOOD GRAIN.

1275
00:49:05,877 --> 00:49:08,413
REALLY NICE.

1276
00:49:08,447 --> 00:49:09,815
SHE'S WEARING A GARTER.

1277
00:49:09,848 --> 00:49:13,318
OH.
VERY STYLISH SHOT, REALLY.

1278
00:49:15,353 --> 00:49:17,990
AW, JOEL,
CAN I HAVE A PUPPY LIKE THAT?

1279
00:49:18,023 --> 00:49:19,257
PLEASE?

1280
00:49:19,290 --> 00:49:20,892
YOU KNOW, HE'D BE PERFECT
FOR RING TOSS.

1281
00:49:20,892 --> 00:49:22,227
LOOK AT THE BEAK ON HIM.

1282
00:49:22,260 --> 00:49:24,228
YOU FOLKS GOTTA EXCUSE ME.

1283
00:49:24,262 --> 00:49:27,032
I'M NOT USED TO THIS CITY.

1284
00:49:27,065 --> 00:49:28,667
HOT CHILD IN THE CITY.

1285
00:49:28,700 --> 00:49:30,635
RUNNIN' WILD.
LOOKIN' PRETTY.

1286
00:49:30,668 --> 00:49:32,270
HEY, WHERE ARE ALL
THE NICK GILDER JOKES?

1287
00:49:32,303 --> 00:49:35,473
BOY, LET ME TELL YOU.

1288
00:49:35,507 --> 00:49:37,308
POOR SUCKERS
CHAINED TO A DESK

1289
00:49:37,342 --> 00:49:40,545
WHILE I ROAM FREE.
GO FIGURE.

1290
00:49:40,578 --> 00:49:42,780
YOU KNOW, I MISS
MY HOT WHEELS SET.

1291
00:49:50,022 --> 00:49:52,023
BYE.

1292
00:49:54,827 --> 00:49:56,562
TOYLAND. TOYLAND.

1293
00:49:56,595 --> 00:49:59,798
I CAN'T BELIEVE
I'M STILL IN TOYLAND.

1294
00:49:59,832 --> 00:50:03,268
A WORLD OF WHIMSY.

1295
00:50:03,302 --> 00:50:05,270
OH, LOOK AT HIM GO.

1296
00:50:05,303 --> 00:50:09,307
GOOD THING HE'S SPORTING
TEFLON, HUH?

1297
00:50:09,340 --> 00:50:13,678
HOW ABOUT A TONGUE SANDWICH,
TOKYO?

1298
00:50:13,712 --> 00:50:15,713
YOU KNOW, YOU DON'T SEE THAT
A LOT IN NATURE.

1299
00:50:15,747 --> 00:50:17,382
NO.

1300
00:50:23,122 --> 00:50:26,925
IT'S ALL CHRISTMASY!

1301
00:50:26,958 --> 00:50:28,927
FROSTED MINI TANKS, GANG.

1302
00:50:28,960 --> 00:50:30,728
ROSEBUD.

1303
00:50:30,762 --> 00:50:32,297
HIS TANK WAS CALLED ROSEBUD.

1304
00:50:32,330 --> 00:50:33,798
DID YOU KNOW THAT?

1305
00:50:33,832 --> 00:50:35,633
RUINED IT.

1306
00:50:35,667 --> 00:50:37,368
EVERYTHING WITHIN REACH
IS IMMEDIATELY DESTROYED.

1307
00:50:37,402 --> 00:50:39,570
HI, FOLKS.
HOW'S THE SHOWER, LADY?

1308
00:50:39,603 --> 00:50:41,440
IT'S 10:00. DO YOU KNOW
WHERE YOUR KIDS ARE?

1309
00:50:41,473 --> 00:50:43,208
I ATE 'EM!
HA, I LOVE THAT.

1310
00:50:48,713 --> 00:50:49,915
PROPERTY VALUES PLUMMET

1311
00:50:49,948 --> 00:50:52,683
WHEN WHOLE NEIGHBORHOOD
SUFFERS FROM FREEZER BURN.

1312
00:50:55,020 --> 00:50:56,488
OOH.

1313
00:50:56,522 --> 00:50:57,855
LITTLE NIP IN THE AIR.

1314
00:50:57,888 --> 00:50:59,490
- REALLY.
- HUH?

1315
00:50:59,523 --> 00:51:02,560
UNUSUAL WEATHER
WE'RE HAVING.

1316
00:51:02,593 --> 00:51:07,132
IT'S A MARSHMALLOW WORLD.

1317
00:51:07,165 --> 00:51:09,000
IT'S PRETTY!

1318
00:51:09,033 --> 00:51:11,570
[GOOFY LAUGHTER]

1319
00:51:14,338 --> 00:51:17,775
A FROZEN PAGODA TREAT.

1320
00:51:17,808 --> 00:51:19,377
HUH?

1321
00:51:19,410 --> 00:51:21,747
AH, SHOW ME SOMETHING
I HAVEN'T SEEN.

1322
00:51:21,780 --> 00:51:24,248
YOU KNOW, I SAW A WIRE.
THAT WRECKS THE WHOLE THING.

1323
00:51:24,282 --> 00:51:25,617
- YOU MEAN THIS IS FAKE?
- YEAH.

1324
00:51:25,650 --> 00:51:27,418
OH, FOR CRYING OUT LOUD.

1325
00:51:39,563 --> 00:51:41,432
HOW ABOUT A LITTLE TONGUE,
SCARECROW?

1326
00:51:41,467 --> 00:51:43,835
LET'S SEE. THAT'S CALLED
FRENCH COMBAT, ISN'T IT?

1327
00:51:48,573 --> 00:51:49,573
OH!

1328
00:51:49,607 --> 00:51:52,577
ABORT MISSION.

1329
00:51:52,610 --> 00:51:54,880
UH, WE'RE TAKING ORDERS.
WHO WANTS A BEAR CLAW?

1330
00:51:54,913 --> 00:51:59,650
OH, I'M NOT IN THIS SCENE.

1331
00:51:59,683 --> 00:52:01,587
WAIT A MINUTE.
MAO IS A TOASTMASTER?

1332
00:52:01,620 --> 00:52:04,722
THE MONSTER CAN DESTROY
EVERYTHING WITH ITS TONGUE.

1333
00:52:04,755 --> 00:52:07,125
YOU TRY SAYING THAT
WITHOUT LAUGHING.

1334
00:52:07,158 --> 00:52:08,493
...WEAPONS ARE USELESS.

1335
00:52:08,493 --> 00:52:11,062
- WELL THEN.
- LET'S NOT SEND YOUR MEN.

1336
00:52:11,095 --> 00:52:12,497
...NEXT ATTACK ON IT
FROM SOME DISTANCE.

1337
00:52:12,530 --> 00:52:13,932
WILL THAT BE SAFE ENOUGH?

1338
00:52:13,965 --> 00:52:17,968
POSSIBLY. WE DO HAVE ONE SITE
THAT'S OUT OF HIS RANGE.

1339
00:52:18,002 --> 00:52:21,773
RIGHT HERE. WHERE WE HAVE
OUR MISSILE CORPS STATIONED.

1340
00:52:21,807 --> 00:52:24,175
HEY, THAT'S IRELAND.

1341
00:52:24,208 --> 00:52:25,877
IT'LL BE TOO FAR AWAY.

1342
00:52:25,910 --> 00:52:28,847
THE MONSTER'S TONGUE
CANNOT POSSIBLY REACH IT.

1343
00:52:28,880 --> 00:52:31,082
IT'S ONLY A MILE LONG.

1344
00:52:31,115 --> 00:52:32,517
WHOA.

1345
00:52:32,550 --> 00:52:35,920
ESTES PARK, COLORADO,
MEET THE STINGER, BIG BERTHA,

1346
00:52:35,953 --> 00:52:38,723
THE GREMLIN.

1347
00:52:38,757 --> 00:52:42,860
HE'S DREAMING OF BIG,
MUTATED-ARMOR-COVERED RABBITS.

1348
00:52:42,893 --> 00:52:44,462
ALL RIGHT.

1349
00:52:44,495 --> 00:52:47,698
WHOA. HAS THAT GUY
BEEN NEAR RADIATION?

1350
00:52:47,732 --> 00:52:49,733
HAVING HOT FLASHES.

1351
00:52:49,767 --> 00:52:51,402
THE MEN HAVE
COMPLETED PREPARATION, SIR.

1352
00:52:51,435 --> 00:52:52,970
- H!
[LAUGHTER]

1353
00:52:53,003 --> 00:52:54,372
HELLO ACE AWARDS, YOU TWO.

1354
00:52:54,405 --> 00:52:56,608
WE ARE STANDING BY
FOR ORDERS, SIR.

1355
00:52:56,642 --> 00:52:59,912
RIGHT. BEGIN THE ATTACK.

1356
00:52:59,945 --> 00:53:02,080
- MORNING.
- OH, GOOD MORNING.

1357
00:53:02,113 --> 00:53:04,515
- HI, EVERYBODY.
- AH, GOOD MORNING.

1358
00:53:04,548 --> 00:53:06,183
UGH.

1359
00:53:06,217 --> 00:53:07,618
MORNING.
THIS IS BARUGON.

1360
00:53:07,652 --> 00:53:09,653
STARTING OUR BROADCAST DAY.

1361
00:53:09,687 --> 00:53:13,592
WAIT A MINUTE. SOMETHING'S
ROTTEN IN OSAKA NOW.

1362
00:53:16,193 --> 00:53:20,198
HE WAKES UP WITH THE WORST
BREATH OF THE MILLENNIUM.

1363
00:53:20,232 --> 00:53:23,668
WONDER IF THEY'LL
CALL OFF SCHOOL TODAY.

1364
00:53:23,702 --> 00:53:25,303
IT'S THE ROCKETTES.

1365
00:53:25,337 --> 00:53:27,638
WHOO!

1366
00:53:27,672 --> 00:53:30,842
LEGS UP, GIRLS.

1367
00:53:30,875 --> 00:53:34,980
WHAT? A SPINE
IN TECHNICOLOR SPECTRUM RAY?

1368
00:53:35,013 --> 00:53:37,982
AH, IT'S A SKITTLES
COMMERCIAL.

1369
00:53:38,015 --> 00:53:40,118
OH, YEAH. FROM HELL.

1370
00:53:43,555 --> 00:53:45,290
OH, I'M SURE
HE COULD DO THAT.

1371
00:53:45,323 --> 00:53:47,225
HOW DO HE KNOW?

1372
00:53:52,430 --> 00:53:53,432
BING.

1373
00:53:53,465 --> 00:53:54,498
HMM.

1374
00:53:54,532 --> 00:53:57,035
WELL. THAT WENT WELL.

1375
00:54:00,972 --> 00:54:04,142
GAMERA'S ATTRACTED
BY ANY FORM OF HEAT ENERGY.

1376
00:54:04,175 --> 00:54:06,978
AND I'M ATTRACTED
TO BEA ARTHUR. GO FIGURE.

1377
00:54:07,012 --> 00:54:09,847
...SO GAMERA'S
FLYING TOWARD IT OVER OSAKA.

1378
00:54:09,880 --> 00:54:11,548
HEY.

1379
00:54:12,683 --> 00:54:15,087
OOH.

1380
00:54:15,120 --> 00:54:16,487
OOH.

1381
00:54:16,520 --> 00:54:19,457
HE'S BECOMING A STARBURST
FRUIT CHEW BEFORE MY EYES.

1382
00:54:19,490 --> 00:54:21,058
OH.

1383
00:54:21,125 --> 00:54:22,460
GAMERA'S MELTING
LIKE A LEMON DROP

1384
00:54:22,493 --> 00:54:25,130
HIGH ABOVE THE CHIMNEY TOPS.

1385
00:54:25,163 --> 00:54:29,533
UH, SIR,
IT'S NOT AN ESCALATOR.

1386
00:54:29,567 --> 00:54:30,535
- WHOA!
- AAH!

1387
00:54:30,568 --> 00:54:31,637
RIGHT IN THE EARS.

1388
00:54:31,670 --> 00:54:32,803
THE ATTACK
BY THE MISSILE CORPS

1389
00:54:32,837 --> 00:54:33,838
HAVE PROVED UNSUCCESSFUL

1390
00:54:33,872 --> 00:54:35,407
AGAINST BARUGON'S RAINBOW.

1391
00:54:35,440 --> 00:54:38,877
AND HERE WE END THE 9:00 P.M.
NEWS BULLETIN.

1392
00:54:38,910 --> 00:54:40,045
WHAT, DO YOU THEY GOT RADIOS
IN THEIR KIDS' HEADS?

1393
00:54:40,078 --> 00:54:42,213
- WHAT?
- ...AS THEY HAPPEN.

1394
00:54:42,247 --> 00:54:46,217
IN THE MEANTIME,
SOME MUSIC BY YANNI.

1395
00:54:46,250 --> 00:54:49,920
YOU KNOW, IT'S UNSETTLING,
BUT BEAUTIFUL.

1396
00:54:49,953 --> 00:54:53,458
QUIETLY DISTURBING.

1397
00:54:53,492 --> 00:54:55,893
WHAT A DISMAL PLACE
TO BE HOLD UP WITH...

1398
00:54:55,927 --> 00:54:57,662
NO, YOU CAN'T
PLAY YOUR ACCORDION.

1399
00:54:57,695 --> 00:54:59,097
...STUCK HERE
LIKE A BUNCH OF ANIMALS.

1400
00:54:59,130 --> 00:55:01,165
HUH? WHY ARE THEY
MAKING ALL THIS FUSS

1401
00:55:01,198 --> 00:55:03,167
ABOUT A PHONY
LITTLE MONSTER, HUH?

1402
00:55:03,200 --> 00:55:04,268
WHY?

1403
00:55:04,302 --> 00:55:05,303
WHY DON'T YOU SHUT UP?

1404
00:55:05,337 --> 00:55:06,337
YOU MAKE ME SICK.

1405
00:55:06,370 --> 00:55:08,005
[IMITATES VOMITING]

1406
00:55:08,038 --> 00:55:10,475
OH, NOT REALLY.

1407
00:55:10,508 --> 00:55:13,978
OH, REVEREND MOON'S
HOLDING A PRAYER AND SHARE.

1408
00:55:17,615 --> 00:55:19,850
GAMERA IS VULNERABLE
TO THE COLD.

1409
00:55:19,883 --> 00:55:22,753
HE HAS BEEN FROZEN POWERLESS
BY THIS NEW MONSTER.

1410
00:55:22,787 --> 00:55:24,088
NAMED CLARENCE BIRDSEYE.

1411
00:55:24,122 --> 00:55:26,357
BUT THE SECOND MONSTER
IS UNHARMED,

1412
00:55:26,390 --> 00:55:28,560
AND NOW THE AUTHORITIES
ARE WITHOUT THE MEANS...

1413
00:55:28,627 --> 00:55:31,662
MY GOD.
IT'S BARUGON.

1414
00:55:31,697 --> 00:55:32,697
BARUGON?

1415
00:55:32,730 --> 00:55:33,732
IT IS.

1416
00:55:33,765 --> 00:55:35,300
I THOUGHT IT WAS
ANOTHER MONSTER,

1417
00:55:35,333 --> 00:55:37,402
BUT IT'S MY BARUGON.

1418
00:55:37,435 --> 00:55:38,537
ATTENTION PLEASE.
ATTENTION PLEASE.

1419
00:55:38,570 --> 00:55:41,538
OH, GOD, COULD HE KISS.

1420
00:55:41,572 --> 00:55:44,675
...AIRLINES FLIGHT AB-711...

1421
00:55:44,708 --> 00:55:46,343
KAREN.

1422
00:55:46,377 --> 00:55:49,513
...SAN FRANCISCO, SEATTLE,
AND VANCOUVER

1423
00:55:49,547 --> 00:55:51,115
IS ABOUT TO LEAVE.

1424
00:55:51,148 --> 00:55:52,183
PASSENGERS
WILL PLEASE PROCEED...

1425
00:55:52,217 --> 00:55:55,687
KAREN, WHAT'S WRONG?
ARE YOU ILL?

1426
00:55:55,720 --> 00:55:58,155
I'M CARRYING
BARUGON'S CHILD.

1427
00:56:00,958 --> 00:56:02,660
THEY'VE COME TOO LATE.

1428
00:56:06,832 --> 00:56:10,735
I JUST COULDN'T BELIEVE
THAT YOUR STORY WAS TRUE.

1429
00:56:10,768 --> 00:56:13,672
I'M RESPONSIBLE
FOR BRINGING THIS.

1430
00:56:13,705 --> 00:56:14,705
[ALL]
AAH!

1431
00:56:14,738 --> 00:56:16,473
DON'T DO THAT.

1432
00:56:16,507 --> 00:56:18,777
AS SOON AS IT'S POSSIBLE
TO GET THERE.

1433
00:56:18,810 --> 00:56:20,812
YOU KNOW OF A WAY
TO GET RID OF IT?

1434
00:56:20,845 --> 00:56:22,380
YES, I DO.

1435
00:56:22,413 --> 00:56:24,415
I'VE GOT THE ANSWER HERE.

1436
00:56:24,448 --> 00:56:26,818
LET'S HURRY
TO STOP ALL THIS HORROR.

1437
00:56:26,852 --> 00:56:29,220
OKAY. I'M WITH YOU.

1438
00:56:30,322 --> 00:56:33,257
WHOA.

1439
00:56:33,290 --> 00:56:34,625
HEY!

1440
00:56:34,692 --> 00:56:37,662
GEE, LAY OFF
FOR A MINUTE, WOULD YA?

1441
00:56:37,695 --> 00:56:39,263
CRYING OUT LOUD.

1442
00:56:39,297 --> 00:56:42,300
OH, THAT'S A BRIDGE
OVER TROUBLED MODELS.

1443
00:56:44,468 --> 00:56:46,537
THAT'S CUTE.

1444
00:56:46,570 --> 00:56:51,475
OH, AND I CAN'T EVEN
GET THIS OPEN. D'OH!

1445
00:56:51,508 --> 00:56:53,745
HEY, LOUIE,
YOU STILL OKAY IN THERE?

1446
00:56:53,778 --> 00:56:58,248
[MUFFLED]
YEAH, I'M OKAY.

1447
00:56:58,282 --> 00:57:00,285
- HUH?
- YOU.

1448
00:57:00,318 --> 00:57:03,353
ONODERA.

1449
00:57:03,387 --> 00:57:05,323
OH, IT'S WITH THE THING,
AND THE...

1450
00:57:05,357 --> 00:57:06,958
[NERVOUS LAUGHTER]
SORRY ABOUT THE THING WITH THE--

1451
00:57:06,992 --> 00:57:07,958
BUT IT'S A GOOD THING.

1452
00:57:08,025 --> 00:57:09,260
ASSASSIN.

1453
00:57:11,797 --> 00:57:13,898
[IMITATES CHOKING]

1454
00:57:13,932 --> 00:57:15,700
LOOK AT THAT LOBE.

1455
00:57:15,733 --> 00:57:17,235
MAN, AS LEOPOLD TOO.

1456
00:57:17,268 --> 00:57:21,840
WE'LL BE ABLE
TO FIND THE OPAL.

1457
00:57:21,873 --> 00:57:24,842
YOU FOOL.
IT WASN'T A JEWEL.

1458
00:57:24,875 --> 00:57:26,677
- WHAT'S THAT?
- IT WAS A MONSTER'S EGG.

1459
00:57:26,710 --> 00:57:29,213
[LAUGHS]
DON'T BE RIDICULOUS.

1460
00:57:29,247 --> 00:57:30,248
GOOD ONE.

1461
00:57:30,282 --> 00:57:31,482
I TELL YOU THAT THE OPAL

1462
00:57:31,515 --> 00:57:33,417
IS THE EGG OUT OF WHICH
THE MONSTER HATCHED!

1463
00:57:33,450 --> 00:57:34,785
IT'S OUR FAULT.

1464
00:57:34,818 --> 00:57:37,255
YOU AND I BROUGHT
THIS DESTRUCTION HERE.

1465
00:57:37,288 --> 00:57:39,657
WE'RE GOING TO KILL THAT MONSTER
BEFORE IT'S TOO LATE.

1466
00:57:39,690 --> 00:57:40,925
DON'T GIVE ME THAT STORY.

1467
00:57:40,958 --> 00:57:43,127
NO, HERE'S ONE.
TWO CHINAMEN WALK INTO A BAR.

1468
00:57:43,160 --> 00:57:44,262
HA.

1469
00:57:44,295 --> 00:57:46,130
I'VE JUST COME
FROM MY BROTHER'S.

1470
00:57:46,163 --> 00:57:47,998
HE AND HIS WIFE
ARE BOTH DEAD.

1471
00:57:48,032 --> 00:57:49,367
THEIR HOUSE BURNED.

1472
00:57:49,400 --> 00:57:50,835
SOMEONE SAW YOU
RUNNING OUT OF THEIR HOUSE

1473
00:57:50,868 --> 00:57:52,970
JUST BEFORE THE FIRE.
YOU!

1474
00:57:53,003 --> 00:57:54,905
HEY, I WAS IN AUSTRIA
DURING THE WHOLE THING.

1475
00:57:54,938 --> 00:57:55,940
HONEST.

1476
00:57:55,973 --> 00:57:56,975
NOT MY FAULT.

1477
00:57:57,008 --> 00:57:58,075
YOU LIAR!

1478
00:57:58,108 --> 00:57:59,710
PANTS ON FIRE.

1479
00:57:59,743 --> 00:58:03,782
[IMITATES CHOKING]

1480
00:58:03,815 --> 00:58:05,983
OH, THAT'S GOOD.
HIT HIM WITH WICKER.

1481
00:58:09,753 --> 00:58:11,322
NOT THE JOHNNIE WALKER!

1482
00:58:19,397 --> 00:58:21,265
HEY, UH, HONEY,
YOU CAN JUMP HERE ANY TIME.

1483
00:58:21,298 --> 00:58:22,300
JUMP IN. COME ON.

1484
00:58:22,333 --> 00:58:23,400
THANK YOU. FINALLY.

1485
00:58:23,433 --> 00:58:24,668
THERE WE GO.

1486
00:58:31,408 --> 00:58:34,412
UH-OH. GINSU 2000.

1487
00:58:34,445 --> 00:58:36,982
CUTS THROUGH LEAD PIPE
AND STILL DISEMBOWELS.

1488
00:58:41,552 --> 00:58:44,155
YEAH. FEEL LIKE
I'M WATCHING MANNIX.

1489
00:58:44,188 --> 00:58:48,358
DUN, DUN, DUN, DUN.

1490
00:58:48,358 --> 00:58:50,562
YOU'D THINK THEY'D BE ABLE
TO USE KUNG FU OR SOMETHING.

1491
00:58:50,595 --> 00:58:53,463
YEAH. WHERE'S BRUCE LEE
WHEN YOU NEED HIM?

1492
00:58:59,237 --> 00:59:00,238
SUCKER PUNCH.

1493
00:59:00,272 --> 00:59:02,307
OW.

1494
00:59:02,340 --> 00:59:05,175
OW.

1495
00:59:05,208 --> 00:59:08,278
AH, YOU'RE LUCKY
MY CHICK'S HERE, MAN.

1496
00:59:08,312 --> 00:59:11,315
THAT'S IT.
DON'T TRY TO UNDERSTAND HIM.

1497
00:59:11,348 --> 00:59:14,085
JUST RIDE AND ROPE
AND BRAND HIM.

1498
00:59:14,118 --> 00:59:15,787
NOW, WHEN I LEFT
THE HOUSE THIS MORNING

1499
00:59:15,820 --> 00:59:17,222
I HAD A SHORT ROPE,
A LONG ROPE,

1500
00:59:17,255 --> 00:59:18,255
AND A MEDIUM-SIZED ROPE.

1501
00:59:18,288 --> 00:59:19,457
NOW,
I DON'T KNOW ANY TRICKS--

1502
00:59:19,490 --> 00:59:21,792
SORRY. SORRY.

1503
00:59:24,628 --> 00:59:28,565
CAN YOU PUT YOUR FINGER
THERE FOR A SEC?

1504
00:59:28,600 --> 00:59:30,802
TIME ON THAT?
TIME PLEASE?

1505
00:59:36,773 --> 00:59:38,777
OH, HE'S BEEN SHOOTING UP.

1506
00:59:38,810 --> 00:59:39,910
HUH?

1507
00:59:39,943 --> 00:59:41,478
WHAT IN THE WORLD?

1508
00:59:41,512 --> 00:59:44,048
HOLD ON HERE.

1509
00:59:44,082 --> 00:59:45,917
HEY.

1510
00:59:45,950 --> 00:59:46,952
WAIT A MIN...

1511
00:59:46,985 --> 00:59:51,222
THIS IS ONE WEIRD SCENE.

1512
00:59:51,255 --> 00:59:52,223
UGH.

1513
00:59:52,257 --> 00:59:53,590
UH, YOU GOT A LITTLE, UH...

1514
00:59:53,625 --> 00:59:56,027
AH, FORGET IT.

1515
00:59:56,027 --> 00:59:58,963
YOU ARE ONE SPOOKY CHICK.

1516
00:59:58,997 --> 01:00:02,733
DO YOU MIND IF I DON'T
CALL YOU AGAIN? UGH.

1517
01:00:02,767 --> 01:00:05,135
HE'S JUST HER TYPE TOO.

1518
01:00:05,168 --> 01:00:06,870
"A" POSITIVE, THAT IS.

1519
01:00:06,903 --> 01:00:08,940
YOU KNOW YOU'RE BEAUTIFUL
WHEN YOU'RE BLOODY.

1520
01:00:08,973 --> 01:00:10,708
I'M ALL RIGHT.
LET'S GO.

1521
01:00:10,742 --> 01:00:13,310
HEY. PLEASE HELP ME.

1522
01:00:13,343 --> 01:00:15,747
LET'S GO. LET'S GO.

1523
01:00:15,780 --> 01:00:18,382
HEY. WAIT.

1524
01:00:18,415 --> 01:00:20,250
I--I APOLOGIZE.

1525
01:00:20,283 --> 01:00:21,818
HELP ME.

1526
01:00:21,852 --> 01:00:23,620
I'M TRYING TO SAY I'M SORRY.

1527
01:00:23,655 --> 01:00:25,188
POOR GUY.

1528
01:00:25,222 --> 01:00:27,225
SO...

1529
01:00:27,258 --> 01:00:29,493
HEY, HER HAIR GOT SHORTER.

1530
01:00:29,560 --> 01:00:33,163
MAY I TELL YOU SOMETHING,
IF YOU PLEASE?

1531
01:00:33,197 --> 01:00:34,732
- NO.
- YES, GO AHEAD.

1532
01:00:34,765 --> 01:00:36,367
I SUCKED HIS BLOOD,
AND I LIKED IT.

1533
01:00:36,400 --> 01:00:37,935
BARUGON IS A LAND ANIMAL.

1534
01:00:37,968 --> 01:00:40,605
ONCE IN THE WATER,
HIS CELLS MELT.

1535
01:00:40,638 --> 01:00:42,940
PURPLE BLOOD
FLOWS OUT QUICKLY.

1536
01:00:42,973 --> 01:00:44,175
AT LEAST THAT IS THE LEGEND

1537
01:00:44,208 --> 01:00:45,610
OUR ANCESTORS
HAVE PASSED DOWN TO US.

1538
01:00:45,643 --> 01:00:47,745
- HIS STRENGTH GOES RAPIDLY.
- HMM.

1539
01:00:47,778 --> 01:00:50,080
BUT ALSO HIS TONGUE
WOULD BECOME PARALYZED

1540
01:00:50,113 --> 01:00:51,715
AND THEREFORE HARMLESS,

1541
01:00:51,748 --> 01:00:53,885
AND IT WOULD BE EASY
TO APPROACH HIM

1542
01:00:53,918 --> 01:00:54,918
AND DESTROY HIM THEN.

1543
01:00:54,952 --> 01:00:55,987
HMM,
LIKE THE WICKED WITCH, EH?

1544
01:00:56,020 --> 01:00:57,422
WE MUST LURE BARUGON
TO THE WATER

1545
01:00:57,455 --> 01:00:58,757
AND THEN
HE'LL DROWN HIMSELF.

1546
01:00:58,790 --> 01:00:59,790
IT'S THE ANSWER.

1547
01:00:59,823 --> 01:01:01,058
AND HOW DO WE LURE HIM?

1548
01:01:01,092 --> 01:01:03,260
WITH THIS.

1549
01:01:03,327 --> 01:01:05,363
- HMM.
- DOVE BARS?

1550
01:01:05,397 --> 01:01:06,397
OH.

1551
01:01:06,430 --> 01:01:09,300
[ENGINES WHOOSHING]

1552
01:01:09,333 --> 01:01:13,437
JET TRAFFIC.

1553
01:01:13,470 --> 01:01:15,407
SAY...

1554
01:01:15,440 --> 01:01:17,642
WE HAVE PRESERVED THIS HUGE
DIAMOND IN OUR VILLAGE

1555
01:01:17,675 --> 01:01:18,843
FOR MANY GENERATIONS.

1556
01:01:18,877 --> 01:01:21,478
BUT WHAT HAS THE DIAMOND
GOT TO DO WITH BARUGON?

1557
01:01:21,512 --> 01:01:23,782
AH, KEEP YOUR SHIRT ON.
IT'S CUBIC ZIRCONIA.

1558
01:01:23,815 --> 01:01:27,318
THIS'LL DRAW HIM ON
IRRESISTIBLY.

1559
01:01:27,352 --> 01:01:30,053
WE CAN USE IT
TO LURE HIM INTO THE WATER?

1560
01:01:30,087 --> 01:01:31,855
DOES YOUR VILLAGE HAVE MANY
DIAMONDS THIS SIZE?

1561
01:01:31,888 --> 01:01:34,492
SIMMER DOWN,
YOU GOLD DIGGER. GEE.

1562
01:01:34,525 --> 01:01:36,160
JUST THIS ONE IS LEFT.

1563
01:01:36,193 --> 01:01:38,963
EVERY THOUSAND YEARS
A MONSTER SUCH AS THIS

1564
01:01:38,997 --> 01:01:40,330
IS BORN IN MY VILLAGE.

1565
01:01:40,363 --> 01:01:41,332
THAT'S A LONG
GESTATION PERIOD.

1566
01:01:41,365 --> 01:01:42,567
EACH TIME ONE IS BORN,

1567
01:01:42,600 --> 01:01:44,735
ANOTHER OF OUR DIAMONDS
MUST BE SACRIFICED.

1568
01:01:44,768 --> 01:01:45,970
IT IS DROPPED INTO THE LAKE

1569
01:01:46,003 --> 01:01:47,972
TO LURE THE MONSTER
TO ITS DEATH.

1570
01:01:48,005 --> 01:01:49,673
IF THAT'S THE CASE,
I REALIZE HOW PRECIOUS

1571
01:01:49,707 --> 01:01:51,208
THIS LAST DIAMOND IS.

1572
01:01:51,242 --> 01:01:53,610
ARE YOU SURE
THAT BARUGON WILL RESPOND

1573
01:01:53,643 --> 01:01:55,145
AS THE LEGEND HAS PREDICTED?

1574
01:01:55,178 --> 01:01:56,847
IF YOU DON'T BELIEVE IN IT,

1575
01:01:56,880 --> 01:01:58,548
YOU ARE DOUBTING THE GODS.

1576
01:01:58,582 --> 01:02:00,885
WHOA. GUESS I STEPPED ON
A FEW TOES THERE.

1577
01:02:00,918 --> 01:02:01,918
SORRY.

1578
01:02:01,952 --> 01:02:03,320
WE HAVEN'T TIME TO WASTE.

1579
01:02:03,353 --> 01:02:05,457
IT'S THE ONLY IDEA
THAT HASN'T BEEN TRIED.

1580
01:02:05,490 --> 01:02:06,757
OH, WHAT ABOUT THE "Z" PLAN?

1581
01:02:06,790 --> 01:02:08,192
WE'LL PUT IT TO WORK AT ONCE.

1582
01:02:08,225 --> 01:02:09,293
SORRY.

1583
01:02:09,293 --> 01:02:11,262
IN WHICH DIRECTION
SHALL WE GUIDE YOU?

1584
01:02:11,295 --> 01:02:14,398
IS THERE A LARGE LAKE
TO SINK HIM IN?

1585
01:02:14,432 --> 01:02:17,000
THERE'S BIWA LAKE.

1586
01:02:17,033 --> 01:02:18,102
I CAN'T UNTIE IT.

1587
01:02:18,135 --> 01:02:19,537
WELL, CUT IT WITH THAT KNIFE.
THERE.

1588
01:02:19,570 --> 01:02:22,173
GEISHAS WHO LOVE TOO MUCH.

1589
01:02:22,207 --> 01:02:23,842
HURRY.

1590
01:02:23,875 --> 01:02:25,743
OH, THE ROPE,
NOT MY WRIST.

1591
01:02:25,777 --> 01:02:26,877
CAREFUL.

1592
01:02:26,910 --> 01:02:28,678
...THE SAFEST PLACE
TO DEPOSIT HIM.

1593
01:02:28,712 --> 01:02:31,282
AUTHORITIES HOPE
THAT THE 5,000 KARAT DIAMOND...

1594
01:02:31,315 --> 01:02:33,750
THAT'S IT. TALK IT OVER
WITH JACK DANIELS.

1595
01:02:33,785 --> 01:02:35,820
WOW.
WHAT AN INCREDIBLE SCHEME.

1596
01:02:35,853 --> 01:02:37,388
A 5,000 KARAT DIAMOND,

1597
01:02:37,422 --> 01:02:39,990
TO BE SUNK IN BIWA LAKE,
JUST TO GET THE MONSTER.

1598
01:02:40,023 --> 01:02:41,025
WHAT?

1599
01:02:41,058 --> 01:02:42,460
ARE YOU SURE?

1600
01:02:42,527 --> 01:02:45,328
OF COURSE. A NATIVE GIRL
BROUGHT IT TO JAPAN.

1601
01:02:45,362 --> 01:02:46,563
WHO TOLD YOU?

1602
01:02:46,597 --> 01:02:47,698
THE RADIO ANNOUNCED IT.

1603
01:02:47,732 --> 01:02:49,767
WAS SHE IN
BRIDE OF FRANKENSTEIN?

1604
01:02:53,805 --> 01:02:55,607
THOSE NATIVES
DID HAVE A JEWEL.

1605
01:02:55,640 --> 01:02:58,708
WORTH MORE
THAN I'D EVER DREAMED OF.

1606
01:02:58,742 --> 01:03:00,478
BUT DADDY NEEDS HIS MEDICINE.

1607
01:03:00,512 --> 01:03:02,147
AH.

1608
01:03:02,180 --> 01:03:03,680
LAST CALL.

1609
01:03:03,713 --> 01:03:06,617
ALL RIGHT.
SO I'LL GET IT.

1610
01:03:06,650 --> 01:03:09,320
WANT A DROOL BUCKET?
OH, RIGHT ON ME.

1611
01:03:09,353 --> 01:03:13,190
IN A FINAL ATTEMPT
TO RID JAPAN OF BARUGON,

1612
01:03:13,223 --> 01:03:15,258
OPERATION DIAMOND
IS PUT INTO EFFECT.

1613
01:03:15,292 --> 01:03:16,660
THEY OFFERED HIM A COCKTAIL.

1614
01:03:16,660 --> 01:03:18,128
A 5,000 KARAT DIAMOND
IS USED

1615
01:03:18,162 --> 01:03:19,363
TO TRICK THE MONSTER

1616
01:03:19,397 --> 01:03:22,132
INTO ABANDONING
HIS NATURAL ENVIRONMENT, LAND,

1617
01:03:22,167 --> 01:03:24,068
FOR THE WATERS OF LAKE BIWA.

1618
01:03:24,102 --> 01:03:28,205
SCENIC LAKE BIWA.

1619
01:03:28,238 --> 01:03:30,608
YEAH, RIGHT.
I'M HEADING OFF TO A LAKE?

1620
01:03:30,642 --> 01:03:32,243
YOU THINK
I WAS BORN YESTERDAY?

1621
01:03:32,277 --> 01:03:34,712
OH, WAIT. I WAS.

1622
01:03:34,745 --> 01:03:36,513
TRAFFIC ON THE I-94 OUTBOUND

1623
01:03:36,547 --> 01:03:37,548
IS STILL BUMPER TO BUMPER

1624
01:03:37,582 --> 01:03:39,417
DURING THE SUNDOWN SLOWDOWN.

1625
01:03:44,555 --> 01:03:46,323
[ROARS]

1626
01:03:46,357 --> 01:03:48,025
WANT IT.

1627
01:03:50,327 --> 01:03:53,230
BARUGON, ARE YOU UP TO ONE
OF YOUR LITTLE SCHEMES AGAIN,

1628
01:03:53,263 --> 01:03:56,800
YOU LITTLE CONNIVER?

1629
01:03:56,833 --> 01:03:58,402
GET ME.
I'M CAROL CHANNING.

1630
01:03:58,435 --> 01:04:00,003
NO, HE'S CUTER
THAN CAROL CHANNING.

1631
01:04:00,037 --> 01:04:02,973
OH.

1632
01:04:03,007 --> 01:04:04,775
YOU KNOW,
DON'T YOU THINK A DISCO BALL

1633
01:04:04,808 --> 01:04:06,143
WOULD HAVE BEEN
A LITTLE CHEAPER?

1634
01:04:06,177 --> 01:04:09,313
MM-HMM.

1635
01:04:09,347 --> 01:04:10,715
OH, LOOK.
THERE'S LIZ TAYLOR.

1636
01:04:10,748 --> 01:04:12,048
NO, HE'S SMALLER
THAN LIZ TAYLOR.

1637
01:04:12,082 --> 01:04:13,517
COME ON. BE NICE.

1638
01:04:13,550 --> 01:04:15,687
OH, FUN.

1639
01:04:17,455 --> 01:04:18,455
WHAT'S WRONG?

1640
01:04:18,488 --> 01:04:19,823
KEEP DANGLING
AND SHAKING IT.

1641
01:04:19,857 --> 01:04:21,725
I THINK HE'S GOING FOR IT.

1642
01:04:21,758 --> 01:04:23,962
TRY JERK BAIT.

1643
01:04:26,830 --> 01:04:28,732
I--I GOTTA GO WALKIES.

1644
01:04:28,765 --> 01:04:30,467
UGH.

1645
01:04:33,905 --> 01:04:36,540
NO USE.
HE WON'T FOLLOW.

1646
01:04:36,573 --> 01:04:39,977
WE'VE FAILED.

1647
01:04:40,010 --> 01:04:41,445
HERE'S ONE FOR YOU.

1648
01:04:41,478 --> 01:04:42,680
WHY DID I CROSS THE ROAD?

1649
01:04:42,713 --> 01:04:44,715
THERE'S NO RIGHT ANSWER.
I DON'T EVEN KNOW.

1650
01:04:44,748 --> 01:04:46,183
[LAUGHTER]

1651
01:04:46,217 --> 01:04:47,918
NOW WHAT?

1652
01:04:47,952 --> 01:04:51,088
WE SMELL ONE.

1653
01:04:51,122 --> 01:04:52,623
SHAME, SHAME, ALL AROUND.

1654
01:04:52,657 --> 01:04:54,292
I DON'T UNDERSTAND.

1655
01:04:59,430 --> 01:05:02,065
OVERPASS?
I DON'T THINK SO.

1656
01:05:10,742 --> 01:05:12,242
IF THIS LEGEND
THAT THE VILLAGERS BELIEVE IN

1657
01:05:12,277 --> 01:05:13,543
- IS REALLY TRUE...
- AND I DOUBT IT.

1658
01:05:13,577 --> 01:05:16,613
THEN KINDLY TELL ME WHY
HE DISREGARDED THE DIAMOND.

1659
01:05:16,647 --> 01:05:18,182
HE DIDN'T LIKE THE CUT,
THE CLARITY,

1660
01:05:18,215 --> 01:05:19,250
THE COLOR, OR KARAT.

1661
01:05:19,283 --> 01:05:20,685
I SUSPECTED THE VALIDITY
OF HER STORY

1662
01:05:20,718 --> 01:05:22,520
FROM THE FIRST TIME
THAT I HEARD HER SPEAK.

1663
01:05:22,553 --> 01:05:23,955
IT WAS TOO MUCH
OF A FAIRYTALE

1664
01:05:23,988 --> 01:05:25,455
AND WE SHOULD NEVER
HAVE LISTENED TO HER.

1665
01:05:25,488 --> 01:05:27,023
AW, JEEZ,
HEAP MORE SHAME ON HER.

1666
01:05:27,057 --> 01:05:29,460
BESIDES, I DOUBT VERY MUCH
THAT THERE WAS A REAL DIAMOND.

1667
01:05:29,527 --> 01:05:31,528
IF A GEM THAT SIZE
EXISTED ANYWHERE IN THE WORLD,

1668
01:05:31,562 --> 01:05:32,930
THERE'D BE REPORTS OF IT.

1669
01:05:32,963 --> 01:05:35,565
SO IT FAILED.
BUT IT ISN'T HER FAULT.

1670
01:05:35,598 --> 01:05:37,735
SHE WAS DOING HER BEST
TO GIVE YOU HER HELP.

1671
01:05:37,768 --> 01:05:39,970
- LISTEN.
- YOU'RE JUST TRYING TO LAY
ALL THE BLAME ON US.

1672
01:05:40,003 --> 01:05:41,905
[ALL]
YEAH, AND SCARECROW'S BRAIN!

1673
01:05:41,938 --> 01:05:43,340
JUST REMEMBER
THAT IT WAS YOUR GREED

1674
01:05:43,373 --> 01:05:45,475
THAT BROUGHT ALL THIS MISERY
UPON US IN THE FIRST PLACE.

1675
01:05:45,508 --> 01:05:46,510
YOU GOT ME.

1676
01:05:46,543 --> 01:05:48,045
BUT STILL.
WE TRIED TO HELP.

1677
01:05:48,078 --> 01:05:49,347
BE QUIET!

1678
01:05:49,380 --> 01:05:50,580
AND GO TO YOUR ROOM.

1679
01:05:50,613 --> 01:05:52,550
I ACTED SHAMEFULLY,
I KNOW.

1680
01:05:52,583 --> 01:05:54,218
SHE'S BLAMELESS.

1681
01:05:54,252 --> 01:05:56,153
SHE GAVE YOU ONE POSSIBLE PLAN.

1682
01:05:56,187 --> 01:05:59,323
IT'S JUST BEEN A FOOLISH
WASTE OF PRECIOUS TIME.

1683
01:05:59,357 --> 01:06:00,992
I KNOW,
BUT IT ISN'T HER FAULT.

1684
01:06:01,025 --> 01:06:02,860
DIE! DIE! DIE!

1685
01:06:02,860 --> 01:06:06,563
I'M SORRY. FORGIVE ME.

1686
01:06:06,597 --> 01:06:10,500
AREAS TO THE WEST
HAVE BEEN MOVED...

1687
01:06:10,533 --> 01:06:11,735
I HAVE TO GO NOW.

1688
01:06:11,768 --> 01:06:14,905
TO THE LITTLE
GENERAL'S ROOM, YOU KNOW.

1689
01:06:14,938 --> 01:06:18,908
HE HURTS ME SO.

1690
01:06:18,942 --> 01:06:20,177
THERE, THERE, DEAR.

1691
01:06:20,210 --> 01:06:22,145
LET'S GET YOU A PINT
OF FRESH TYPE "A."

1692
01:06:25,515 --> 01:06:27,985
HMM?

1693
01:06:28,018 --> 01:06:29,220
OH, GET A ROOM.

1694
01:06:29,253 --> 01:06:30,855
MM-HMM.

1695
01:06:30,888 --> 01:06:32,890
I'LL REPEAT THAT MESSAGE...

1696
01:06:32,923 --> 01:06:34,858
UH, I HATE TO PULL RANK
ON YOU, SON,

1697
01:06:34,892 --> 01:06:35,927
BUT, UH, HMM.

1698
01:06:35,993 --> 01:06:37,895
IN FACT, WE'RE VERY MUCH
OBLIGED TO YOU.

1699
01:06:37,928 --> 01:06:40,097
YOU TRIED YOUR BEST.

1700
01:06:40,130 --> 01:06:42,533
SHE IS A WILD TIGRESS,
ISN'T SHE?

1701
01:06:42,567 --> 01:06:44,835
EXCUSE ME.
THIS GENTLEMAN IS DR. SATO.

1702
01:06:44,868 --> 01:06:45,870
HELLO.

1703
01:06:45,903 --> 01:06:47,303
AH. HOW ARE YOU?

1704
01:06:47,337 --> 01:06:48,905
- FINE, THANKS.
- GOOD.

1705
01:06:48,938 --> 01:06:50,073
YOU?

1706
01:06:50,107 --> 01:06:51,242
THIS TIME YOU'VE GOT
SOME REAL TROUBLE.

1707
01:06:51,275 --> 01:06:53,143
OH, WE CERTAINLY HAVE.

1708
01:06:53,177 --> 01:06:54,378
THINK YOU CAN HELP US?

1709
01:06:54,412 --> 01:06:55,913
HAVE YOU GOT SOME
SUGGESTIONS TO MAKE?

1710
01:06:55,947 --> 01:06:58,548
I'M GLAD I STOPPED BY.
ON MY WAY OVER HERE...

1711
01:06:58,582 --> 01:07:00,083
I BELIEVE THAT BARUGON

1712
01:07:00,117 --> 01:07:03,087
WAS EXPOSED TO AN INFRARED RAY
WHILE STILL AN EGG.

1713
01:07:03,120 --> 01:07:05,588
AND I BELIEVE FOR EVERY
DROP OF RAIN THAT FALLS

1714
01:07:05,622 --> 01:07:06,590
A FLOWER GROWS.

1715
01:07:06,623 --> 01:07:07,958
YOU SEE,
I WAS ON THE SHIP

1716
01:07:07,992 --> 01:07:09,627
THAT BROUGHT THE EGG
HERE TO JAPAN.

1717
01:07:09,660 --> 01:07:11,928
ONODERA. HE WAS THE MAN
WHO FOUND THE EGG,

1718
01:07:11,962 --> 01:07:13,597
THINKING IT WAS A GEM.

1719
01:07:13,630 --> 01:07:15,933
HE WAS THEN RECEIVING
INFRARED-RAY TREATMENT

1720
01:07:15,967 --> 01:07:16,967
FOR ATHLETE'S FOOT.

1721
01:07:17,000 --> 01:07:18,202
WHAT'S SO ABSORBING, JUNIOR?

1722
01:07:18,235 --> 01:07:19,437
NOW IT SEEMS QUITE POSSIBLE

1723
01:07:19,470 --> 01:07:20,938
THAT HE FORGOT
TO TURN THE LAMP OFF.

1724
01:07:20,972 --> 01:07:23,673
IT WAS PROBABLY DIRECTED
TOWARDS THE EGG.

1725
01:07:23,707 --> 01:07:25,542
HEY, LOOK BACK THERE.

1726
01:07:25,575 --> 01:07:28,145
IT'S CARY GRANT
IN THE FABERGE YEARS.

1727
01:07:28,178 --> 01:07:29,280
AT VERY CLOSE RANGE,

1728
01:07:29,313 --> 01:07:31,248
AND OVER QUITE A SUBSTANTIAL
PERIOD OF TIME.

1729
01:07:31,282 --> 01:07:32,983
CASTRO'S THERE TOO.

1730
01:07:33,017 --> 01:07:36,120
...SPEEDED UP CONSIDERABLY
THE GROWTH OF THE MONSTER.

1731
01:07:36,153 --> 01:07:37,688
THEN THAT EXPLAINS IT.

1732
01:07:37,722 --> 01:07:39,990
NOW I UNDERSTAND
WHAT'S HAPPENED.

1733
01:07:40,023 --> 01:07:42,358
THE LEGEND SAYS BARUGON
SHOULD TAKE TEN YEARS

1734
01:07:42,392 --> 01:07:43,593
TO REACH HIS PRESENT SIZE.

1735
01:07:43,593 --> 01:07:45,128
AH, INDEED.

1736
01:07:45,162 --> 01:07:48,265
ARE YOU CERTAIN THAT IT SHOULD
TAKE TEN YEARS TO MATURE?

1737
01:07:48,298 --> 01:07:49,767
YES. I AM.

1738
01:07:49,800 --> 01:07:52,603
BARUGON IS REALLY A FREAK
WITH AN ABNORMAL BODY.

1739
01:07:52,637 --> 01:07:53,703
I KNOW THE FEELING.

1740
01:07:53,737 --> 01:07:55,907
THAT'S SOMETHING
WE DOCTORS CAN EXPLAIN.

1741
01:07:55,940 --> 01:07:59,310
IF AN EXPECTANT MOTHER
IS EXPOSED TO RADIOACTIVITY,

1742
01:07:59,343 --> 01:08:00,310
A FREAK MAY BE BORN.

1743
01:08:00,343 --> 01:08:01,812
LIKE RICK JAMES?

1744
01:08:01,845 --> 01:08:05,015
SO THEN THAT'S WHY IT SHOWED
NO INTEREST IN THE DIAMOND.

1745
01:08:05,048 --> 01:08:06,050
THAT'S RIGHT.

1746
01:08:06,083 --> 01:08:07,918
HE'S A SUPER FREAK.

1747
01:08:07,952 --> 01:08:10,855
LISTEN. NOW THAT WE KNOW
THAT IT'S A FREAK,

1748
01:08:10,888 --> 01:08:13,290
ISN'T THERE SOME DIFFERENT WAY
THAT WE SHOULD ATTACK IT?

1749
01:08:13,323 --> 01:08:14,892
IT'S HERBIE!

1750
01:08:14,925 --> 01:08:17,327
EXPOSE THE DIAMOND
TO THE INFRARED RAY.

1751
01:08:17,327 --> 01:08:18,762
WILL THAT DO US ANY GOOD?

1752
01:08:18,795 --> 01:08:22,365
NO, BUT IT WILL
PAD THE FILM OUT A LITTLE BIT.

1753
01:08:22,398 --> 01:08:25,235
...BARUGON MUST THEREFORE
RESPOND FAVORABLY TO IT.

1754
01:08:25,268 --> 01:08:27,538
YEAH, I'M BUYING THIS
BIG TIME.

1755
01:08:27,572 --> 01:08:31,108
NOW THEN. PERHAPS THE DIAMOND,
IF RADIOACTIVE,

1756
01:08:31,142 --> 01:08:32,142
WILL BE EFFECTIVE.

1757
01:08:32,175 --> 01:08:34,010
BARUGON MAY RESPOND TO IT

1758
01:08:34,043 --> 01:08:35,145
AS YOU FIRST HOPED.

1759
01:08:35,178 --> 01:08:36,547
BARUGON, THAT'S ME.

1760
01:08:36,580 --> 01:08:39,717
KAREN, IS THERE ANY WAY TO MAKE
HIM STAY WHERE HE IS NOW?

1761
01:08:39,750 --> 01:08:41,218
UH, WE COULD STAPLE HIM
TO THE FLOOR.

1762
01:08:41,252 --> 01:08:42,418
THERE'S ONE POSSIBILITY.

1763
01:08:42,452 --> 01:08:45,055
OUR VILLAGES HAVE ALL
BEEN PRAYING FOR RAIN.

1764
01:08:45,088 --> 01:08:47,925
IF HEAVEN CARES,
IT WILL SEND US RAIN.

1765
01:08:47,958 --> 01:08:48,958
WHY RAIN?

1766
01:08:48,992 --> 01:08:50,160
YOU GOT A BETTER IDEA?

1767
01:08:50,193 --> 01:08:51,562
WATER WILL WEAKEN HIM.

1768
01:08:51,595 --> 01:08:55,232
OUR LEGEND SAYS THAT THE MONSTER
CANNOT MOVE WHILE IT RAINS.

1769
01:08:55,265 --> 01:08:57,300
SHE KIDDIN' US?

1770
01:08:57,333 --> 01:08:59,270
BUT WHY WAIT FOR THE GODS.

1771
01:08:59,303 --> 01:09:02,172
ISN'T IT EASY NOW
TO CREATE RAIN?

1772
01:09:02,205 --> 01:09:03,640
HECK, MY AUNT COULD DO IT.

1773
01:09:03,673 --> 01:09:05,108
WE'LL PRODUCE IT, ALL RIGHT.

1774
01:09:05,142 --> 01:09:06,143
YOU DIRECT.

1775
01:09:06,177 --> 01:09:09,413
MANMADE RAIN
FROM HELICOPTERS.

1776
01:09:09,447 --> 01:09:11,848
A FLIGHT OF HELICOPTERS
IS SENT TO FLY OVER BARUGON...

1777
01:09:11,882 --> 01:09:13,017
[COUGHING]

1778
01:09:13,050 --> 01:09:15,218
...SPRAYING ONTO HIM
MANMADE RAIN.

1779
01:09:15,252 --> 01:09:17,722
A MIST-LIKE LIQUID,
WHICH IT IS HOPED,

1780
01:09:17,755 --> 01:09:19,723
WILL ARREST
THE MONSTER'S MOVEMENTS.

1781
01:09:19,757 --> 01:09:21,458
SEND IN THE CLOUDS.

1782
01:09:21,492 --> 01:09:22,693
THE RAIN SHOULD MAKE BARUGON

1783
01:09:22,727 --> 01:09:24,562
UNABLE TO EXHALE
HIS FREEZING VAPOR,

1784
01:09:24,595 --> 01:09:26,563
THUS RENDERING HIM HARMLESS.

1785
01:09:26,597 --> 01:09:27,665
OR AT LEAST DROWSY

1786
01:09:27,698 --> 01:09:29,733
AND UNABLE TO OPERATE
HEAVY MACHINERY.

1787
01:09:33,837 --> 01:09:35,472
[WITH BRITISH ACCENT]
WELL, COULD BE WORSE.

1788
01:09:35,505 --> 01:09:36,473
HOW?

1789
01:09:36,507 --> 01:09:37,507
COULD BE RAININ'.

1790
01:09:37,542 --> 01:09:39,710
WHOA.

1791
01:09:39,743 --> 01:09:44,080
CATCH THE DROPS ON YOUR TONGUE.
IT'S FUN.

1792
01:09:44,113 --> 01:09:48,352
YOU KNOW, UH, RAINY DAYS
AND MONDAYS ALWAYS GET ME DOWN.

1793
01:09:48,385 --> 01:09:49,387
IT'S TRUE.

1794
01:09:49,420 --> 01:09:53,623
POPPIES.
POPPIES WILL MAKE HIM SLEEP.

1795
01:09:53,657 --> 01:09:55,592
WELL, LET'S HEAD OVER
TO THE BOZO DRUM!

1796
01:09:55,625 --> 01:09:56,760
HOO-HOO!

1797
01:09:56,827 --> 01:09:58,728
THIS MACHINE IS CALLED
A DEATH RAY PROJECTOR,

1798
01:09:58,762 --> 01:10:01,832
AND A RUBY IS PUT IN
TO ACT UPON THE LIGHT MOLECULES.

1799
01:10:01,865 --> 01:10:05,202
THUS THE WAVES OF LIGHT
ARE BROKEN DOWN.

1800
01:10:05,235 --> 01:10:07,037
- RIGHT NOW...
- OH, JUST GET ON WITH IT.

1801
01:10:07,070 --> 01:10:09,038
YOU CAN SEE THE MACHINE
IS IN THE EXPERIMENTAL STAGE,

1802
01:10:09,072 --> 01:10:11,442
AND CANNOT BE PUT
TO PRACTICAL USE.

1803
01:10:11,475 --> 01:10:15,478
BUT NOW POSSIBLY
WE CAN EMPLOY THE DIAMOND

1804
01:10:15,512 --> 01:10:16,513
- INSTEAD OF THE RUBY.
- NEAT.

1805
01:10:16,547 --> 01:10:18,848
- LET'S INSERT IT.
- TOGETHER.

1806
01:10:18,882 --> 01:10:20,683
AND TRY ITS EFFECTIVENESS.

1807
01:10:20,717 --> 01:10:22,687
YOU'RE TRYING
MY EFFECTIVENESS.

1808
01:10:22,720 --> 01:10:24,655
WE'RE ANXIOUS
TO TRY IT OUT AT ONCE.

1809
01:10:24,688 --> 01:10:27,490
TURN IT ONTO BARUGON
AND SEE IF IT WORKS.

1810
01:10:27,523 --> 01:10:29,327
OKAY.

1811
01:10:29,360 --> 01:10:31,995
HE'S SLEEPING. SOMEBODY
PUT HIS HAND IN WARM WATER.

1812
01:10:37,668 --> 01:10:40,037
DARN POACHERS.

1813
01:10:43,373 --> 01:10:44,975
WELL, THERE GOES OUR RIDE.

1814
01:10:50,913 --> 01:10:52,248
HI.

1815
01:10:56,553 --> 01:10:58,722
WHY, BARUGON,
YOU'RE CRYING.

1816
01:10:58,755 --> 01:11:03,260
FAKE.
I'M JUST RESTING MY EYES.

1817
01:11:03,327 --> 01:11:05,895
OH, LOOK AT HIM.
HE'S ALL OVER THE ROAD.

1818
01:11:07,263 --> 01:11:09,667
OH, NO. OH, AND HERE COMES
A HAPLESS FAMILY

1819
01:11:09,700 --> 01:11:11,002
ON A SUNDAY RIDE.

1820
01:11:11,035 --> 01:11:12,903
UM, HONEY, THERE'S SOMETHING
IN THE ROAD AHEAD.

1821
01:11:18,942 --> 01:11:22,112
WHAT IS THIS,
THE UNIVERSAL TOUR?

1822
01:11:22,145 --> 01:11:23,147
BEGIN.

1823
01:11:23,180 --> 01:11:24,548
THE BEGUINE.

1824
01:11:26,283 --> 01:11:29,387
[HUMS]

1825
01:11:29,420 --> 01:11:31,222
OOH.

1826
01:11:34,358 --> 01:11:35,658
RIGHT. MOVE FORWARD.

1827
01:11:35,692 --> 01:11:38,295
LOVE IS KINDA CRAZY WITH
A SPOOKY LITTLE GIRL LIKE HER.

1828
01:11:38,328 --> 01:11:40,197
MM-HMM.

1829
01:11:43,667 --> 01:11:45,068
HMM?

1830
01:11:45,102 --> 01:11:48,138
OH, COMPANY.
MY FAVORITE SNACK.

1831
01:11:52,475 --> 01:11:54,077
KAREN, GOT IT?

1832
01:11:54,110 --> 01:11:56,747
SHE NEVER LOST IT.

1833
01:11:56,780 --> 01:11:58,948
AH, BE CAREFUL.

1834
01:11:58,982 --> 01:12:02,820
MUSIC GOES ROUND AND ROUND
AND COMES OUT HERE.

1835
01:12:04,755 --> 01:12:06,290
WHOA.
LOOK, HE'S LEAKING.

1836
01:12:06,323 --> 01:12:07,490
NO, HE'S JUST DIESELING.

1837
01:12:07,523 --> 01:12:08,525
OH.

1838
01:12:08,558 --> 01:12:09,693
PREPARATIONS READY, SIR.

1839
01:12:09,727 --> 01:12:10,993
GOOD. START.

1840
01:12:10,993 --> 01:12:13,630
OH. BEGIN.

1841
01:12:13,663 --> 01:12:14,865
WE'LL START.

1842
01:12:14,898 --> 01:12:16,233
- GET GOING.
- ENGAGE.

1843
01:12:16,267 --> 01:12:17,633
- MAKE IT SO.
- NOW.

1844
01:12:17,667 --> 01:12:18,668
- FIRE.
- INITIATE.

1845
01:12:18,702 --> 01:12:21,238
- GO.
- TIME TO GET IT MOVING.

1846
01:12:21,272 --> 01:12:22,873
WHATEVER HAPPENED TO GAMERA?

1847
01:12:22,907 --> 01:12:24,007
YOU KNOW,
HE GOT TOP BILLING.

1848
01:12:24,040 --> 01:12:25,975
HE MUST HAVE A REALLY GOOD
AGENT, I THINK.

1849
01:12:26,008 --> 01:12:29,680
I SUPPOSE SO.

1850
01:12:29,713 --> 01:12:30,780
NOW...

1851
01:12:30,813 --> 01:12:32,750
HE'S MOVING!
IT'S MOVING!

1852
01:12:32,783 --> 01:12:34,183
HEY!

1853
01:12:34,217 --> 01:12:35,652
GOOD. DRIVE ON.

1854
01:12:35,685 --> 01:12:36,887
THERE'S THAT GLOWING GUY AGAIN.

1855
01:12:36,920 --> 01:12:38,722
ONCE HE GETS
INTO THE SPOTLIGHT,

1856
01:12:38,755 --> 01:12:42,025
WE'RE EXPECTING HIM TO DO
A COUPLE JAZZY SHOW TUNES.

1857
01:12:44,728 --> 01:12:49,232
[DRAMATIC MUSIC]

1858
01:12:49,265 --> 01:12:54,070
SPOTLIGHT DANCE.
BARUGON.

1859
01:12:54,103 --> 01:12:55,105
DOING THE DOG.

1860
01:12:55,138 --> 01:12:57,340
GOOD.

1861
01:12:57,373 --> 01:12:59,810
WELL SAID.

1862
01:12:59,843 --> 01:13:02,478
AH, YOU KNOW,
I WAS SINGING FOR THE PEOPLE.

1863
01:13:02,512 --> 01:13:03,713
THEY WERE CRAWLING AT ME.

1864
01:13:03,747 --> 01:13:07,550
THEY WERE THROWING...

1865
01:13:07,583 --> 01:13:11,088
SHE'S GOT THE FLARE-NOSTRIL LOOK
I LOVE SO MUCH.

1866
01:13:13,257 --> 01:13:14,390
OH, NOW WATCH.

1867
01:13:14,425 --> 01:13:16,593
HE'LL HAVE BLACK RINGS
AROUND HIS EYES

1868
01:13:16,627 --> 01:13:17,560
WHEN HE PULLS
THE BINOCULARS DOWN.

1869
01:13:17,593 --> 01:13:18,795
COME ON, HERE IT GOES.

1870
01:13:18,828 --> 01:13:22,833
HERE IT GOES--AW.

1871
01:13:22,867 --> 01:13:23,900
OH, NO!

1872
01:13:23,933 --> 01:13:25,068
WHAT'S WRONG?

1873
01:13:25,102 --> 01:13:27,470
EVERYTHING.
WE GOTTA LENGTHEN THE MOVIE.

1874
01:13:31,842 --> 01:13:33,577
I'M SO EMBARRASSED.

1875
01:13:33,610 --> 01:13:35,212
RUFF. RUFF.

1876
01:13:35,245 --> 01:13:36,447
LET'S GET OUT OF HERE!

1877
01:13:36,480 --> 01:13:37,447
RIGHT!

1878
01:13:37,480 --> 01:13:41,050
[ENGINE STRUGGLING]

1879
01:13:41,083 --> 01:13:42,820
WON'T START, HUH?

1880
01:13:42,853 --> 01:13:47,023
MOMMY!

1881
01:13:47,057 --> 01:13:49,325
MOMMY, MOMMY,
IT'S YOUR BOY!

1882
01:13:49,358 --> 01:13:50,660
OH, NO.
HE'S DOING JOLSON.

1883
01:13:50,727 --> 01:13:54,030
TURN OUT THE LIGHT.
QUICKLY.

1884
01:13:54,063 --> 01:13:56,032
OKAY.

1885
01:13:56,065 --> 01:13:57,767
HEY.

1886
01:13:57,802 --> 01:13:59,970
HEY, GUESS YOU SAW IT.

1887
01:14:00,003 --> 01:14:01,003
RIGHT.

1888
01:14:01,037 --> 01:14:02,572
NOW I'LL DO EARTHA KITT.

1889
01:14:02,605 --> 01:14:07,577
♪ C'EST SI BON... ♪

1890
01:14:07,610 --> 01:14:09,613
DON'T GO TOO CLOSE.
BE CAREFUL.

1891
01:14:09,647 --> 01:14:11,282
IT'S GOING TO BE DANGEROUS.

1892
01:14:11,315 --> 01:14:13,083
NO.

1893
01:14:13,117 --> 01:14:15,285
NOW. SWITCH ON.

1894
01:14:15,318 --> 01:14:16,987
FOR ACTION!

1895
01:14:17,020 --> 01:14:19,923
AND NOW I'D LIKE TO TELL A FEW
THINGS ABOUT SHOW BUSINESS...

1896
01:14:19,957 --> 01:14:22,993
ABOUT THE TIME
THAT I MET THIS MAN

1897
01:14:23,027 --> 01:14:27,363
THAT WAS COMING TO ME
ON BROADWAY.

1898
01:14:27,397 --> 01:14:28,865
RIGHT. BOARD NOW.

1899
01:14:28,898 --> 01:14:29,900
YES, SIR.

1900
01:14:29,933 --> 01:14:33,403
ORDERS CAME DOWN.

1901
01:14:33,437 --> 01:14:37,107
- DON'T SAY IT.
- RIGHT.

1902
01:14:38,675 --> 01:14:41,312
SO HERBERT NORVILLE
COMES TO ME,

1903
01:14:41,345 --> 01:14:42,645
AND HE SAYS THAT...

1904
01:14:44,915 --> 01:14:48,085
COMMENCE PROGRESS, NOW!

1905
01:14:48,118 --> 01:14:49,185
TO THE LAKE!

1906
01:14:49,218 --> 01:14:50,187
YAY, WE'RE ALL GOING
TO THE LAKE!

1907
01:14:50,220 --> 01:14:51,855
YAY! WHOOPEE!

1908
01:14:51,888 --> 01:14:54,190
BRING THE INFLATABLE DOG.

1909
01:14:57,293 --> 01:14:58,662
I'M NOT GOING IN THE TUNNEL.

1910
01:14:58,695 --> 01:15:01,698
WELL, I'M SURE NOT
GOING TO LOSE THAT DIAMOND.

1911
01:15:01,732 --> 01:15:03,000
TIME TO BLOW.

1912
01:15:03,033 --> 01:15:05,268
NO, DON'T GO.
YOU CAN'T TAKE SUCH A RISK.

1913
01:15:05,302 --> 01:15:07,103
LET GO OF ME
AND STAY OUT OF MY CAR.

1914
01:15:07,137 --> 01:15:09,372
PLEASE DON'T GO.
COME BACK HERE.

1915
01:15:09,405 --> 01:15:10,407
GET AWAY!

1916
01:15:10,440 --> 01:15:13,177
NO, DON'T GO. DON'T GO!

1917
01:15:21,985 --> 01:15:23,553
[HUMMING]

1918
01:15:23,587 --> 01:15:24,988
OH, HEY, CROW,

1919
01:15:25,022 --> 01:15:27,190
ANYMORE BREWSKIS
IN THE COOLER THERE?

1920
01:15:27,223 --> 01:15:29,593
UH, NO. HOW ABOUT
A FROZEN DAIQUIRI CONVECTION?

1921
01:15:29,627 --> 01:15:31,328
OH, SURE.
THAT SOUNDS GREAT.

1922
01:15:31,328 --> 01:15:33,497
BOY, IT SURE IS
A NICE DAY TODAY, HMM?

1923
01:15:33,530 --> 01:15:36,633
YEAH, LIKE A WARM
SUMMER NIGHT BACK HOME.

1924
01:15:36,667 --> 01:15:37,867
YOU KNOW, BACK ON EARTH

1925
01:15:37,902 --> 01:15:39,703
WE USED TO HANG OUT
AT THE BEACH ALL THE TIME.

1926
01:15:39,737 --> 01:15:42,940
OR ELSE WE'D GO TO THE DRIVE-IN,
WHICH WAS REALLY FUN.

1927
01:15:42,973 --> 01:15:44,007
THE DRIVE-IN?

1928
01:15:44,040 --> 01:15:45,042
OH, YEAH.

1929
01:15:45,075 --> 01:15:46,510
WE'D ALL PILE INTO THE CAR

1930
01:15:46,543 --> 01:15:48,278
AND HEAD OUT
TO THE OLD LUCKY TWIN

1931
01:15:48,312 --> 01:15:50,713
BACK IN BUFFALO
ON ROUTE FIVE.

1932
01:15:50,747 --> 01:15:52,917
OH. JOEL, TELL US
ABOUT THE MOVIES AGAIN, HMM?

1933
01:15:52,950 --> 01:15:55,518
WELL, MY LITTLE
CINEMATIC SIDEKICKS,

1934
01:15:55,552 --> 01:15:57,853
YOU KNOW, IN THOSE DAYS,
WE HAD REAL STARS.

1935
01:15:57,887 --> 01:16:00,223
WE DIDN'T NEED DIALOGUE.
WE HAD FACES.

1936
01:16:00,257 --> 01:16:02,158
OH, KINDA LIKE THIS GAMERA FILM,
HUH, JOEL?

1937
01:16:02,192 --> 01:16:03,293
OH, YEAH, BUT THAT'S--

1938
01:16:03,327 --> 01:16:04,762
THIS FILM CERTAINLY
HAD A LOT OF FACES.

1939
01:16:04,762 --> 01:16:06,162
I'LL GIVE YOU THAT
FOR FREE.

1940
01:16:06,195 --> 01:16:08,598
BUT THESE FILMS NEVER SEEM
TO HAVE ANY BIG-NAME STARS.

1941
01:16:08,632 --> 01:16:10,800
WELL, THAT'S WHERE
YOU AND I SPLIT THE DOG,

1942
01:16:10,833 --> 01:16:12,002
MY LITTLE RED PAL.

1943
01:16:12,035 --> 01:16:14,705
UH, THIS FILM IS PACKED
WITH CELLULOID HEROES,

1944
01:16:14,738 --> 01:16:16,340
AND THEY NEVER
FEEL ANY PAIN.

1945
01:16:16,373 --> 01:16:17,373
HUH.

1946
01:16:17,407 --> 01:16:19,208
IT WAS A MAGIC TIME
IN HOLLYWOOD.

1947
01:16:19,242 --> 01:16:22,678
STARS JUMPED AT THE CHANCE
TO APPEAR IN A GAMERA FILM.

1948
01:16:22,712 --> 01:16:25,182
HERE, I'LL SHOW YOU.
CAMBOT, DO IT LIKE I LIKE IT.

1949
01:16:25,215 --> 01:16:27,717
SEE, CHECK IT OUT.
THERE'S EDWARD G. ROBINSON,

1950
01:16:27,750 --> 01:16:29,887
FRESH FROM HIS ROLE
IN SOYLENT GREEN.

1951
01:16:29,920 --> 01:16:32,388
NOW SHUT UP AND EAT
YOUR SOYLENT GREEN, SEE.

1952
01:16:32,422 --> 01:16:34,557
SOYLENT GREEN
IS MADE FROM PEOPLE.

1953
01:16:34,590 --> 01:16:37,893
YEAH, WHATEVER.
HERE'S ELVIS COSTELLO
MAKING HIS SCREEN DEBUT.

1954
01:16:37,893 --> 01:16:39,963
I DON'T KNOW. LOOKS MORE
LIKE MARSHALL CRENSHAW TO ME.

1955
01:16:40,030 --> 01:16:41,163
OR ARNOLD STANG.

1956
01:16:41,197 --> 01:16:43,133
OH, YEAH, LOOK.
HERE'S PETER USTINOV.

1957
01:16:43,167 --> 01:16:45,968
HEY, IT LOOKS "USTINOV"
LIKE HIM TO ME.

1958
01:16:46,002 --> 01:16:48,805
UH, YEAH. AND HERE
WE HAVE LON CHANEY, JR.

1959
01:16:48,838 --> 01:16:50,040
UH, RIGHT. SURE, JOEL.
THAT'S--

1960
01:16:50,073 --> 01:16:51,908
HEY, LET ME FINISH.
NEXT WE HAVE STEVE ALLEN.

1961
01:16:51,942 --> 01:16:53,577
CLAUDE AKINS
AND HARRISON FORD.

1962
01:16:53,610 --> 01:16:55,278
ODDJOB AND WILLEM DAFOE,

1963
01:16:55,312 --> 01:16:57,680
ROBERT BLAKE
AND WILLEM DAFOE.

1964
01:16:57,713 --> 01:16:58,915
UH, JOEL, ARE YOU OKAY?

1965
01:16:58,948 --> 01:17:00,917
HEY, SHUT UP.
HANK WILLIAMS, JR.

1966
01:17:00,950 --> 01:17:03,087
JERRY LEWIS
AND WILLEM DAFOE.

1967
01:17:03,120 --> 01:17:04,353
UH, JOEL, WHEN YOU WENT
TO THE DRIVE-IN,

1968
01:17:04,387 --> 01:17:05,455
DID YOU SPEND A LOT
OF TIME TO THE TRUNK?

1969
01:17:05,488 --> 01:17:07,223
DID I MENTION
JERRY TO YOU BOTS?

1970
01:17:07,257 --> 01:17:08,625
YOU GUYS
PROBABLY DON'T KNOW HIM

1971
01:17:08,658 --> 01:17:10,493
HARDLY WORKING
OR CRACKING UP,

1972
01:17:10,493 --> 01:17:13,863
BUT, OH, LADY MISTER
HEEMINY HOMEN,

1973
01:17:13,897 --> 01:17:15,865
WHAT IN THE HEY? OH...

1974
01:17:15,898 --> 01:17:18,668
PLEASE HELP ME.
UH...

1975
01:17:18,702 --> 01:17:21,237
UH, FOLKS,
WE'LL BE RIGHT BACK.

1976
01:17:21,270 --> 01:17:23,173
SORRY YOU HAD TO SEE THIS.

1977
01:17:23,207 --> 01:17:25,708
[WHISTLES]
OH, BOY.

1978
01:17:34,617 --> 01:17:35,618
UGH.

1979
01:17:35,652 --> 01:17:38,355
THINK I GOT A SUNBURN.

1980
01:17:38,388 --> 01:17:41,825
TOLD YOU THERE'S A LOT
OF STARS IN THIS MOVIE.

1981
01:17:41,858 --> 01:17:42,858
NEAT.

1982
01:17:42,892 --> 01:17:43,993
CAREFUL, ROBIN.

1983
01:17:43,993 --> 01:17:47,830
BOTH HANDS ON THE BAT ROPE
AT ALL TIMES.

1984
01:17:47,863 --> 01:17:49,967
IT'S YOU.
WHY ARE YOU HERE?

1985
01:17:50,000 --> 01:17:53,037
- I'M GETTING THAT DIAMOND.
- FIGURES.

1986
01:17:53,070 --> 01:17:55,372
HASN'T YOUR GREED
CAUSED ENOUGH GRIEF ALREADY?

1987
01:17:55,405 --> 01:17:57,007
WHY DON'T YOU
GET OUT OF HERE?

1988
01:17:57,040 --> 01:17:58,242
OH, BOY.
YOU KNOW, GUYS,

1989
01:17:58,275 --> 01:17:59,242
I'M STARTING TO DOUBT
THEIR FRIENDSHIP.

1990
01:17:59,275 --> 01:18:02,645
AAH!

1991
01:18:02,678 --> 01:18:04,413
CRYING OUT LOUD.

1992
01:18:04,447 --> 01:18:05,982
[WOMAN SCREAMS]

1993
01:18:06,015 --> 01:18:09,052
HUMANS.
WHO CAN UNDERSTAND 'EM?

1994
01:18:09,085 --> 01:18:10,387
GO FIGURE.

1995
01:18:10,420 --> 01:18:11,388
WHAT'S GOING ON?

1996
01:18:11,422 --> 01:18:14,157
HEY, SERGEANT, GO AND CHECK.

1997
01:18:14,190 --> 01:18:17,127
- DOCTOR. DOCTOR.
- GIVE ME THE NEWS.

1998
01:18:17,160 --> 01:18:19,595
I HAVE A RIGHT
TO GET AT THAT DIAMOND.

1999
01:18:19,628 --> 01:18:21,063
NO, YOU HAVEN'T.

2000
01:18:21,097 --> 01:18:23,300
DANCE. DANCE.
THE LAMBADA.

2001
01:18:23,333 --> 01:18:25,102
- THE FORBIDDEN DANCE?
- YEAH.

2002
01:18:25,135 --> 01:18:27,070
OR ELSE I'LL SHOOT.

2003
01:18:28,772 --> 01:18:30,140
- HI.
- OH, THERE.

2004
01:18:30,173 --> 01:18:32,608
[ENGINE REVS]

2005
01:18:32,642 --> 01:18:35,212
AH, WAIT, WAIT.
I DON'T HAVE MY SKIS UP.

2006
01:18:35,245 --> 01:18:36,245
AAH!

2007
01:18:36,278 --> 01:18:38,315
[ROARS]

2008
01:18:41,350 --> 01:18:43,620
UH-OH.

2009
01:18:43,653 --> 01:18:46,222
OH, THAT'S GIVING HIM
THE RASPBERRY.

2010
01:18:46,255 --> 01:18:49,558
HELP ME!
I'VE BEEN FRENCHED TO DEATH!

2011
01:18:55,998 --> 01:18:58,235
I CALL THAT A MANWICH.
[LAUGHS]

2012
01:18:58,268 --> 01:19:00,803
JUST SOMETHING TO HOLD HIM OVER
UNTIL HE GETS TO OSAKA.

2013
01:19:00,837 --> 01:19:02,238
NOW YOU CAN'T GO BACK
IN THE WATER

2014
01:19:02,272 --> 01:19:06,342
FOR ANOTHER HOUR.
REMEMBER THAT.

2015
01:19:06,375 --> 01:19:07,577
WHY ARE THEY SO SAD?

2016
01:19:07,610 --> 01:19:09,378
THAT'S THE GUY
THAT KILLED HIS BROTHER.

2017
01:19:09,412 --> 01:19:12,282
WELL, THERE'S SOMETHING
ABOUT WATCHING A MAN
GET TONGUED TO DEATH.

2018
01:19:12,315 --> 01:19:15,485
WELL, THAT'S THE WAY
I WANT TO GO. WHOO!

2019
01:19:15,518 --> 01:19:17,620
WELL, THAT'S IT.
WE'RE LICKED.

2020
01:19:17,653 --> 01:19:20,323
SORRY. SORRY! SORRY.

2021
01:19:20,357 --> 01:19:22,725
THAT'S WHAT YOU GET.

2022
01:19:24,795 --> 01:19:26,697
MOM, MOM, WATCH ME DIVE!

2023
01:19:26,730 --> 01:19:29,867
THROW ME A STICK.
I'LL CATCH IT.

2024
01:19:29,900 --> 01:19:31,468
THE PLAN HAS FAILED.

2025
01:19:31,502 --> 01:19:33,203
BARUGON HAS SWALLOWED
THE MASSIVE DIAMOND.

2026
01:19:33,237 --> 01:19:35,172
OUR ONLY HOPE
IS THAT HE'LL PASS IT.

2027
01:19:35,205 --> 01:19:36,940
THE ONLY METHOD
THAT WE HAVE LEFT

2028
01:19:36,973 --> 01:19:38,808
TO GET RID OF THE MONSTER
HAS NOW BEEN...

2029
01:19:38,842 --> 01:19:39,943
O.A.K.

2030
01:19:39,977 --> 01:19:41,243
- GET THE HELICOPTERS.
- SIR.

2031
01:19:41,277 --> 01:19:43,213
HAVE THEM PRODUCE RAIN
SO BARUGON CAN'T MOVE.

2032
01:19:43,247 --> 01:19:47,850
- THERE IS NO OTHER WAY.
- SIR.

2033
01:19:47,883 --> 01:19:51,622
I LOVE THE THEATER.
I DO.

2034
01:19:51,655 --> 01:19:55,158
MEANWHILE, AT A STORAGE UNIT
OUTSIDE OF OSAKA...

2035
01:20:00,397 --> 01:20:02,198
HMM?

2036
01:20:03,300 --> 01:20:06,737
WHAT ARE THEY,
AT A COLUMBO TRYOUT?

2037
01:20:06,770 --> 01:20:08,103
IT'S USELESS
LOOKING AROUND HERE.

2038
01:20:08,137 --> 01:20:09,338
WE WON'T FIND A THING.

2039
01:20:09,372 --> 01:20:10,707
YEAH,
THE AUDIENCE HAS LEFT TOO.

2040
01:20:10,740 --> 01:20:11,908
EVER SINCE I WAS A CHILD,

2041
01:20:11,942 --> 01:20:13,610
I'VE BEEN TOLD
OF THE DISASTROUS RAINBOW

2042
01:20:13,643 --> 01:20:16,445
THAT THE MONSTER CAN MAKE.

2043
01:20:16,478 --> 01:20:18,882
OH, WHAT'S SHE GOING ON ABOUT?

2044
01:20:18,915 --> 01:20:21,618
BECAUSE ONE IS BORN
ONLY AFTER EACH THOUSAND YEARS,

2045
01:20:21,652 --> 01:20:23,820
I WANTED TO SEE IT
WITH MY OWN EYES.

2046
01:20:23,853 --> 01:20:25,522
I WAS TOO YOUNG
THE LAST TIME.

2047
01:20:25,555 --> 01:20:29,092
NO MATTER HOW
TERRIFYING IT WAS.

2048
01:20:29,125 --> 01:20:31,493
MM-HMM.

2049
01:20:31,528 --> 01:20:34,430
[HUMS]

2050
01:20:34,463 --> 01:20:36,967
OH, SORRY.
I DIDN'T KNOW.

2051
01:20:41,503 --> 01:20:43,207
I'M SORRY.
I WASN'T LISTENING.

2052
01:20:43,240 --> 01:20:44,373
DID YOU SAY SOMETHING?

2053
01:20:44,407 --> 01:20:48,110
NO ONE WILL EVER BE ABLE
TO GET RID OF IT NOW.

2054
01:20:48,143 --> 01:20:50,080
IT'S OUR PUNISHMENT
FOR WANTING SO MUCH WEALTH.

2055
01:20:50,113 --> 01:20:54,350
SO WHAT'S GONNA HAPPEN
TO DONALD TRUMP?

2056
01:20:54,383 --> 01:20:56,318
YES.
YES, SHE'S BUYING IT.

2057
01:20:56,352 --> 01:20:58,288
IF ONLY
I COULD WORK UP A TEAR.

2058
01:20:58,322 --> 01:21:01,257
OH.
SHE'S GOING FOR IT.

2059
01:21:01,290 --> 01:21:03,860
WAIT A MINUTE.
A NAPKIN?

2060
01:21:03,893 --> 01:21:05,462
THAT GIVES ME AN IDEA.

2061
01:21:05,528 --> 01:21:08,063
HONEY, YOU'RE BRILLIANT.

2062
01:21:08,097 --> 01:21:11,768
[SNIFFS]
UGH.

2063
01:21:11,802 --> 01:21:12,802
HMM?

2064
01:21:12,835 --> 01:21:13,837
NOW, WHAT ARE THESE?

2065
01:21:13,870 --> 01:21:15,238
SNAP ZOOMS.

2066
01:21:15,272 --> 01:21:17,373
THEY LOOK LIKE
REARVIEW MIRRORS.

2067
01:21:17,407 --> 01:21:19,875
THEY'RE ALL THAT'S LEFT
OF THE JEEP.

2068
01:21:19,910 --> 01:21:21,243
ARE THESE QUESTIONS
RHETORICAL?

2069
01:21:21,277 --> 01:21:23,212
...ALONG WITH EVERYTHING ELSE.

2070
01:21:23,247 --> 01:21:24,982
THEY APPEAR TO BE IMPERVIOUS.

2071
01:21:25,015 --> 01:21:26,683
NEAT.

2072
01:21:26,717 --> 01:21:27,917
SEE WHAT THAT MEANS?

2073
01:21:27,950 --> 01:21:29,385
THERE'S A WEAKNESS
IN THE RAINBOW.

2074
01:21:29,418 --> 01:21:31,622
AND THERE'S MORE OF US!

2075
01:21:31,655 --> 01:21:32,655
OH. OH.

2076
01:21:32,688 --> 01:21:34,057
NOW, DOCTOR,

2077
01:21:34,090 --> 01:21:36,793
ISN'T THE RAINBOW SIMILAR
TO A DEATH RAY PROJECTOR?

2078
01:21:36,827 --> 01:21:38,862
WELL, IT'S KIND OF A REACH,
BUT MAYBE.

2079
01:21:38,862 --> 01:21:40,030
I BELIEVE THAT'S RIGHT.

2080
01:21:40,063 --> 01:21:41,063
YES!

2081
01:21:41,097 --> 01:21:42,865
- SEEMS LOGICAL.
- SURE.

2082
01:21:42,898 --> 01:21:44,700
WHEN THE RAINBOW
HIT THE MIRROR,

2083
01:21:44,733 --> 01:21:46,235
IT SEEMS
TO HAVE BEEN REFLECTED

2084
01:21:46,268 --> 01:21:47,703
IN JUST THE WAY LIGHT IS.

2085
01:21:47,737 --> 01:21:49,172
IT WASN'T HARMED.

2086
01:21:49,205 --> 01:21:51,875
BECAUSE THE ENERGY
DIDN'T PENETRATE IT.

2087
01:21:51,908 --> 01:21:53,443
- AH, I SEE.
- YES.

2088
01:21:53,477 --> 01:21:55,612
- REFLECTED.
- KILL HIM. OH.

2089
01:21:55,645 --> 01:21:58,013
THE PRINCIPAL ITSELF'S REALLY
A SIMPLE-ENOUGH ONE.

2090
01:21:58,047 --> 01:21:59,515
HMM.

2091
01:21:59,548 --> 01:22:00,950
YOU MAY HAVE HIT ON
SOMETHING IMPORTANT.

2092
01:22:00,983 --> 01:22:02,885
BUT WILL THIS HELP US?

2093
01:22:02,918 --> 01:22:05,022
CAN WE USE IT AGAINST BARUGON?

2094
01:22:05,055 --> 01:22:06,555
NO, BUT IT'S SOMETHING TO DO.

2095
01:22:06,588 --> 01:22:07,623
YES, SIR.

2096
01:22:07,657 --> 01:22:09,025
I'M AN AMATEUR
IN THESE MATTERS,

2097
01:22:09,058 --> 01:22:10,960
BUT I HAVE AN IDEA.

2098
01:22:13,162 --> 01:22:15,932
HMM?

2099
01:22:15,965 --> 01:22:17,200
HERE,
NOW HOLD OUT YOUR ARM.

2100
01:22:17,233 --> 01:22:19,635
THESE FLAMES CAN REACH
AN EXTREMELY INTENSE HEAT.

2101
01:22:19,668 --> 01:22:21,470
THEY CAN EVEN MELT STEEL.

2102
01:22:21,503 --> 01:22:23,340
AND YET, THE STOVE ITSELF

2103
01:22:23,373 --> 01:22:25,042
IS QUITE UNAFFECTED
BY ALL THIS HEAT.

2104
01:22:25,075 --> 01:22:26,943
NOW WHY?

2105
01:22:26,977 --> 01:22:27,977
- HO!
- AAH!

2106
01:22:28,010 --> 01:22:29,178
DON'T...
JEEZ.

2107
01:22:29,212 --> 01:22:31,147
THE FLAMES ARE EJECTED
OUTWARDS AWAY FROM IT.

2108
01:22:31,180 --> 01:22:32,548
BUT IF THEY'RE TURNED IN,

2109
01:22:32,582 --> 01:22:35,785
ONTO THE BURNER ITSELF,
WHAT WOULD HAPPEN THEN?

2110
01:22:35,818 --> 01:22:39,422
OH, GREAT. WE'RE TAKING
A SHOP COURSE ALL OF A SUDDEN.

2111
01:22:39,455 --> 01:22:42,958
NOW I'M, UH, GONNA MAKE
A BIRD HOUSE FOR YOU FOLKS.

2112
01:22:45,662 --> 01:22:48,665
- SO YOU SEE?
- I MADE A FLUTE.

2113
01:22:48,698 --> 01:22:50,867
...BY ITS OWN FLAME.
WHEN EXPOSED TO IT.

2114
01:22:50,900 --> 01:22:51,968
MM-HMM.

2115
01:22:52,002 --> 01:22:54,303
IN THE SAME WAY,
BARUGON CAN BE DESTROYED.

2116
01:22:54,337 --> 01:22:55,672
UH, COME AGAIN?

2117
01:22:55,705 --> 01:22:57,873
DO WE NEED TO KNOW THIS
FOR THE TEST?

2118
01:22:57,907 --> 01:22:59,108
WHAT DO YOU THINK, SIR?

2119
01:22:59,142 --> 01:23:00,610
YOU'RE TOASTED, AREN'T YOU?

2120
01:23:00,643 --> 01:23:02,812
THAT'S QUITE AN IDEA.

2121
01:23:02,845 --> 01:23:05,715
BUT SURELY IT'S IMPOSSIBLE
TO APPLY IT HERE.

2122
01:23:05,748 --> 01:23:06,750
ON BARUGON.

2123
01:23:06,783 --> 01:23:08,952
WHY CAN'T YOU
EVER SUPPORT ME?

2124
01:23:08,985 --> 01:23:10,287
THESE MIRRORS.

2125
01:23:10,320 --> 01:23:12,288
WE'LL MAKE A MIRROR LARGE ENOUGH

2126
01:23:12,322 --> 01:23:14,857
AND REFLECT HIS RAINBOW
ONTO HIM.

2127
01:23:14,890 --> 01:23:16,458
SO, IN THEORY,

2128
01:23:16,492 --> 01:23:18,395
BARUGON WILL BE MADE TO DIE
BY HIS OWN RAINBOW.

2129
01:23:18,462 --> 01:23:20,763
YEAH, IF THAT MAKES IT WORK
FOR YOU. OF COURSE.

2130
01:23:20,797 --> 01:23:21,965
HMM.

2131
01:23:21,998 --> 01:23:24,633
- HOW VERY FITTING.
- IRONIC. I LOVE IT.

2132
01:23:24,667 --> 01:23:26,837
ALL RIGHT. PLEASE GET READY
TO CARRY IT OUT.

2133
01:23:26,870 --> 01:23:28,872
GET YOUR COSTUMES ON.

2134
01:23:28,905 --> 01:23:31,640
SO THE MICROWAVE ANTENNA
AT THE SUMMIT OF MT. KASHIKA

2135
01:23:31,673 --> 01:23:32,942
IS TURNED INTO A MIRROR,

2136
01:23:32,975 --> 01:23:35,545
IN READINESS FOR
OPERATION REARVIEW MIRROR.

2137
01:23:35,578 --> 01:23:37,280
GIANT SHREDDED WHEAT
IS DEPLOYED.

2138
01:23:37,313 --> 01:23:38,748
HUNDREDS OF WORKMEN
ARE EMPLOYED,

2139
01:23:38,782 --> 01:23:40,850
TREATING EVERYTHING THAT HOLDS
THE MIRRORS IN PLACE

2140
01:23:40,883 --> 01:23:42,352
WITH A MERCURY PREPARATION.

2141
01:23:42,385 --> 01:23:44,320
TANKS OF WINDEX ARE COMMISSIONED
BY THE GOVERNMENT.

2142
01:23:44,353 --> 01:23:47,223
KIDS ARE TOLD BY THE THOUSANDS
NOT TO SMUDGE THE MIRRORS.

2143
01:23:52,928 --> 01:23:54,963
AT THE SAME TIME,
ACTION IS BEING TAKEN

2144
01:23:54,997 --> 01:23:57,133
TO KEEP BARUGON IN ONE SPOT.

2145
01:23:57,167 --> 01:24:00,470
GEORGE WINSTON MUSIC
IS PLAYED FOR HIM.

2146
01:24:00,503 --> 01:24:02,438
PREPARATIONS FOR OPERATION
REARVIEW MIRROR

2147
01:24:02,472 --> 01:24:04,640
HAVE BEEN COMPLETED.

2148
01:24:04,673 --> 01:24:06,175
THE GROUND FORCE IS MAKING USE

2149
01:24:06,208 --> 01:24:07,610
OF ALL ITS MOST
ADVANCED WEAPONS

2150
01:24:07,643 --> 01:24:09,445
IN THE ATTACK
AGAINST BARUGON.

2151
01:24:09,478 --> 01:24:12,282
IT IS HOPED THAT IN THIS WAY
BARUGON WILL BE ANGERED.

2152
01:24:12,315 --> 01:24:14,150
AND MAYBE A LITTLE PUT-OUT.

2153
01:24:14,183 --> 01:24:17,253
HE WILL RESPOND BY SENDING OUT
HIS MOST POWERFUL WEAPON--

2154
01:24:17,287 --> 01:24:19,122
- THE RAINBOW.
- OF FORGIVENESS.

2155
01:24:19,155 --> 01:24:20,357
LEFT BY 300 DEGREES.

2156
01:24:20,390 --> 01:24:21,825
300 "DEGWEES"?

2157
01:24:21,858 --> 01:24:22,825
LEFT BY 300 DEGREES.

2158
01:24:22,858 --> 01:24:25,962
"WOGER."

2159
01:24:25,962 --> 01:24:27,563
OH.

2160
01:24:27,597 --> 01:24:30,333
DOWN 28 DEGREES,
FIVE SECONDS.

2161
01:24:30,367 --> 01:24:32,068
DOWN 28 DEGREES,
FIVE SECONDS.

2162
01:24:32,102 --> 01:24:33,770
HECK OF A TAN
IN THAT THING.

2163
01:24:33,803 --> 01:24:36,773
STOP. CORRECT RANGE.

2164
01:24:36,807 --> 01:24:38,307
"COWWECTING" RANGE, SIR.

2165
01:24:38,340 --> 01:24:39,675
35, SIR.

2166
01:24:39,708 --> 01:24:41,010
RIGHT!

2167
01:24:41,043 --> 01:24:42,878
WE'RE READY NOW.
EVERYTHING'S IN PLACE TO BEGIN.

2168
01:24:42,912 --> 01:24:45,682
DOCTOR. WON'T IT BE BETTER
TO WAIT UNTIL NIGHT

2169
01:24:45,715 --> 01:24:47,150
WHEN WE CAN SEE THE RAINBOW?

2170
01:24:47,183 --> 01:24:49,285
I AGREE. WE'LL WAIT.

2171
01:24:49,318 --> 01:24:51,420
YOU KNOW,
NO ONE IN MY ORGANIZATION

2172
01:24:51,453 --> 01:24:54,790
HAS EVER TALKED TO ME LIKE THAT.
I LIKE IT.

2173
01:24:54,823 --> 01:24:57,427
[IMITATING DRAMATIC MUSIC]

2174
01:24:57,460 --> 01:24:58,595
I LOVE IT SO.

2175
01:24:58,628 --> 01:25:00,130
[DRAMATIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

2176
01:25:00,163 --> 01:25:02,465
OH.
GRAND CANYON SUITE.

2177
01:25:02,498 --> 01:25:04,300
THERE'S NO ONE UP THERE.

2178
01:25:04,333 --> 01:25:05,735
NO WORKMEN OR OTHERS.

2179
01:25:05,768 --> 01:25:07,303
OH, NO. EVERYTHING
AT THE ANTENNA

2180
01:25:07,337 --> 01:25:08,572
IS DONE BY REMOTE CONTROL.

2181
01:25:08,605 --> 01:25:10,540
I LIKE YOUR SHIRT.
IT'S KIND OF DRAPEY.

2182
01:25:10,573 --> 01:25:12,675
FIRE!

2183
01:25:17,580 --> 01:25:21,483
WHAT NOW? I WAS POSING
FOR CRYING OUT LOUD.

2184
01:25:24,587 --> 01:25:27,257
UH, WHAT WAS THAT ABOUT
REPOSITIONING THE TANKS?

2185
01:25:27,290 --> 01:25:29,825
TOO LATE.

2186
01:25:29,858 --> 01:25:31,627
CAN'T RUN
FROM THE RAINBOW.

2187
01:25:31,627 --> 01:25:33,228
- MM-MM.
- MM-MM.

2188
01:25:33,228 --> 01:25:35,898
FROSTED LUCKY CHARMS.

2189
01:25:35,932 --> 01:25:37,867
OH.

2190
01:25:37,900 --> 01:25:40,068
AH, THAT'S A CHEAP SHOT.

2191
01:25:40,102 --> 01:25:42,072
OOH. CAN YOU IMAGINE
HOW THAT MUST SMELL?

2192
01:25:42,105 --> 01:25:45,908
- UGH.
- YEESH.

2193
01:25:45,942 --> 01:25:49,245
AH, YOU KNOW WHAT REALLY
BURNS MY BUTT? ME.

2194
01:25:49,278 --> 01:25:52,915
THAT'S CUTE.

2195
01:25:52,948 --> 01:25:54,883
OH. OH, HOT. OH, HOT.

2196
01:25:54,917 --> 01:25:56,518
OH, WATER. WATER. OOH.

2197
01:25:56,552 --> 01:26:00,190
[HISSING]
AAH.

2198
01:26:00,223 --> 01:26:03,827
OOH.

2199
01:26:05,295 --> 01:26:06,562
BARUGON'S DEAD.

2200
01:26:06,562 --> 01:26:08,163
AND GARSON'S GOT HIM!

2201
01:26:08,197 --> 01:26:12,068
I THINK SO.

2202
01:26:12,102 --> 01:26:14,537
UH-HUH.

2203
01:26:14,570 --> 01:26:17,040
HE'S DEAD.
YOU'VE KILLED HIM.

2204
01:26:17,073 --> 01:26:19,708
[WHISPERING]
I'M FAKING.

2205
01:26:19,742 --> 01:26:21,043
SHH.

2206
01:26:21,077 --> 01:26:22,712
OH, THIS IS GONNA BE
JUST LIKE FATAL ATTRACTION.

2207
01:26:22,745 --> 01:26:23,747
I KNOW IT.

2208
01:26:23,780 --> 01:26:26,548
OH, WHAT, IS DAVID LYNCH
DIRECTING NOW?

2209
01:26:26,582 --> 01:26:31,053
SUPPURATING FISTULAS
MADE FROM DELICIOUS
SMUCKER'S GRAPE JELLY.

2210
01:26:32,922 --> 01:26:33,923
UGH.

2211
01:26:33,957 --> 01:26:35,325
[CLEARS THROAT]

2212
01:26:35,358 --> 01:26:37,760
OH.
WE JUST GAVE HIM A RASH.

2213
01:26:37,793 --> 01:26:41,397
WE FAILED. THE RAYS WEREN'T
POWERFUL ENOUGH FOR IT.

2214
01:26:41,430 --> 01:26:43,165
WE'VE GOT TO TRY AGAIN?

2215
01:26:43,198 --> 01:26:45,435
- HUH?
- HUH?

2216
01:26:45,468 --> 01:26:46,668
YEAH, YOU'VE GOT A DRAGON.

2217
01:26:46,702 --> 01:26:47,703
WE MUST AROUSE HIM.

2218
01:26:47,737 --> 01:26:49,405
HEY, I LISTENED
TO THE DIAMOND THING,

2219
01:26:49,438 --> 01:26:51,373
BUT I AM NOT
GOING TO AROUSE HIM.

2220
01:26:51,407 --> 01:26:53,810
BARUGON WON'T SEND OUT
ANOTHER RAINBOW.

2221
01:26:53,843 --> 01:26:56,778
BUT WHY NOT?
WHY NOT, KAREN?

2222
01:26:56,812 --> 01:26:58,982
I'VE GROWN UP
IN THE JUNGLE.

2223
01:26:59,015 --> 01:27:00,683
AND I'VE LIVED AMONGST
THE WILD ANIMALS.

2224
01:27:00,717 --> 01:27:01,717
SO?

2225
01:27:01,750 --> 01:27:03,185
SO I KNOW ABOUT THEIR WAYS.

2226
01:27:03,218 --> 01:27:05,988
WHEN AN ANIMAL HAS ONCE BEEN
HURT BY ITS OWN MISTAKE,

2227
01:27:06,022 --> 01:27:07,990
IT WILL NEVER MAKE
THE SAME MISTAKE AGAIN.

2228
01:27:08,023 --> 01:27:09,025
NOT LIKE US.

2229
01:27:09,058 --> 01:27:11,727
WHAT SHE SAYS IS RIGHT.

2230
01:27:11,760 --> 01:27:13,495
IT WILL NEVER
SEND ANOTHER RAINBOW.

2231
01:27:13,528 --> 01:27:15,097
EVERYTHING'S IN THE TOILET.

2232
01:27:15,130 --> 01:27:18,433
OPERATION REARVIEW MIRROR
IS AT AN END.

2233
01:27:18,467 --> 01:27:20,937
SO LET'S GO EAT.
WHO'S HUNGRY?

2234
01:27:24,540 --> 01:27:25,542
YOU BUYIN'?

2235
01:27:25,575 --> 01:27:28,612
OH, NO.
THERE'S NOTHING WE CAN DO.

2236
01:27:32,082 --> 01:27:36,785
THAT'S THE SPIRIT.

2237
01:27:36,818 --> 01:27:37,820
NOTHING.

2238
01:27:37,853 --> 01:27:40,923
[IMITATES CRYING]

2239
01:27:40,957 --> 01:27:42,725
AH, SHUT UP,
YOU PATHETIC BASTARD.

2240
01:27:42,758 --> 01:27:44,927
GET UP!
QUIT YOUR CRYING.

2241
01:27:49,598 --> 01:27:52,335
AH, YOU'RE NOTHING
BUT A GAL DARN COWARD.

2242
01:27:52,368 --> 01:27:55,070
GIVE ME SOMETHING
TO SLAP HIM WITH.

2243
01:27:55,103 --> 01:27:58,140
BUT NOW, THE BUILDINGS
FROZEN BY BARUGON

2244
01:27:58,173 --> 01:27:59,508
HAVE BEGUN TO THAW.

2245
01:27:59,542 --> 01:28:02,345
THE ICE MELTS AWAY
FROM OSAKA CASTLE.

2246
01:28:02,378 --> 01:28:04,647
GAMERA HAS REGAINED
CONSCIOUSNESS.

2247
01:28:04,680 --> 01:28:06,682
AND HIS PILOT HAS RE-LIT.

2248
01:28:06,715 --> 01:28:07,850
AH.

2249
01:28:07,883 --> 01:28:11,020
[CLAPS] HEY, ARE THOSE
LEE PRESS-ON NAILS?

2250
01:28:17,927 --> 01:28:21,197
FINALLY, A FIGHT.

2251
01:28:21,230 --> 01:28:24,833
[SCREECHES]

2252
01:28:24,867 --> 01:28:27,037
HOW ABOUT A LITTLE
DEATH BITE ON THE NECK?

2253
01:28:27,070 --> 01:28:28,070
[LAUGHS]

2254
01:28:28,103 --> 01:28:31,207
WHEE.

2255
01:28:31,240 --> 01:28:33,475
HEY, BITE THIS.

2256
01:28:33,508 --> 01:28:36,978
YOU MEAN LIKE THIS?

2257
01:28:37,013 --> 01:28:40,483
I AM WIRED.

2258
01:28:40,517 --> 01:28:42,318
HE IS, TOO.

2259
01:28:42,352 --> 01:28:44,420
[ROARS]

2260
01:28:45,788 --> 01:28:47,290
HEY, HEY, HEY, YOU KIDS.

2261
01:28:47,323 --> 01:28:49,658
NO SPLASHING. COME ON.

2262
01:28:49,692 --> 01:28:52,862
HEY, THIS WATER GOT WARM
ALL OF A SUDDEN.

2263
01:29:02,372 --> 01:29:04,073
MARION, DON'T LOOK
AT THE LIGHT, MARION.

2264
01:29:04,107 --> 01:29:05,073
LOOK AWAY.

2265
01:29:05,107 --> 01:29:06,608
[SCREECHES]

2266
01:29:06,642 --> 01:29:09,678
IF YOU THINK OF THEM AS TWO GUYS
IN RUBBER SUITS, IT'S REAL SAD.

2267
01:29:09,712 --> 01:29:11,347
YEAH.

2268
01:29:11,380 --> 01:29:12,815
RUB MY TUMMY.
RUB MY TUMMY.

2269
01:29:12,848 --> 01:29:16,085
[LAUGHTER]

2270
01:29:16,118 --> 01:29:20,490
AND OUT FROM THE LIZARD
CAME A BUBBLIN' CRUDE.

2271
01:29:20,523 --> 01:29:22,058
BILE, THAT IS.

2272
01:29:22,092 --> 01:29:23,592
TEXAS TEA.

2273
01:29:23,625 --> 01:29:25,795
OH, NO. I DON'T WANNA
GET MY HAIR WET.

2274
01:29:25,795 --> 01:29:26,795
OOH.

2275
01:29:26,828 --> 01:29:29,065
OH, LOOK.
HE'S IN THE WATER.

2276
01:29:29,098 --> 01:29:30,098
MM.

2277
01:29:30,132 --> 01:29:31,833
I'M HERE, STEVE.

2278
01:29:31,867 --> 01:29:33,402
IT JUST MAY SUCCEED.

2279
01:29:33,435 --> 01:29:34,637
IT'S A CRAZY IDEA,

2280
01:29:34,670 --> 01:29:36,538
BUT IT JUST...MIGHT...WORK.

2281
01:29:42,845 --> 01:29:44,313
OH, THAT'S...

2282
01:29:51,787 --> 01:29:54,357
HE'S DROWNING
IN IS OWN GRAVY.

2283
01:29:54,390 --> 01:29:56,525
UGH.

2284
01:29:56,558 --> 01:29:57,660
HEY, THAT FLUORIDE TREATMENT

2285
01:29:57,693 --> 01:30:01,563
SHOWS HE'S REALLY
NEEDING TO FLOSS.

2286
01:30:01,597 --> 01:30:03,767
BY THIS TIME, MY LUNGS
WERE ACHING FOR AIR.

2287
01:30:03,800 --> 01:30:06,202
THAT IS THE LAST TIME
YOU CAN EVER DO THAT.

2288
01:30:06,235 --> 01:30:08,103
DON'T HIT.
OR YELL.

2289
01:30:08,137 --> 01:30:12,575
HURTS, HUH?
WE DIE TOGETHER, MY FRIEND.

2290
01:30:12,608 --> 01:30:14,043
COME ON NOW.
FIGHT.

2291
01:30:14,077 --> 01:30:16,245
YOU'VE NEVER GIVEN UP
ON ANYTHING IN YOUR LIFE.

2292
01:30:16,278 --> 01:30:20,950
NOW FIGHT!

2293
01:30:20,983 --> 01:30:22,118
HEY, IT'S THE...

2294
01:30:22,152 --> 01:30:26,822
A NIGHT THE LIGHTS
WENT OUT ON BARUGON.

2295
01:30:26,855 --> 01:30:29,325
OH, NO. SHE SAID HE WOULDN'T
DO ANOTHER RAINBOW.

2296
01:30:29,358 --> 01:30:31,160
HEY, IT'S STOPPING NOW.

2297
01:30:31,193 --> 01:30:32,995
BARUGON'S FINISHED.

2298
01:30:37,133 --> 01:30:38,868
HE'S COMPLETELY DEFEATED.

2299
01:30:38,902 --> 01:30:41,137
THEN WHY DO I
FEEL SO EMPTY?

2300
01:30:41,170 --> 01:30:42,172
BARUGON'S FINISHED!

2301
01:30:42,205 --> 01:30:46,642
[ALL CHATTERING]

2302
01:30:46,675 --> 01:30:48,343
VICTORY...

2303
01:30:48,377 --> 01:30:50,345
OH, GIVE HER A KISS,
YOU BIG LUG.

2304
01:30:50,378 --> 01:30:51,380
COME ON.

2305
01:30:51,413 --> 01:30:55,117
[LAUGHS]
LITTLE SUGAR ON THE JAW.

2306
01:30:55,150 --> 01:30:58,787
- HE'S FINISHED.
- LET'S GO HOME.

2307
01:30:58,822 --> 01:31:00,723
YOU KNOW,
SHOULDN'T THEY KILL GAMERA

2308
01:31:00,757 --> 01:31:02,425
NOW THAT THEY
GOT HIM RIGHT THERE?

2309
01:31:02,458 --> 01:31:03,425
NOT A BAD IDEA.

2310
01:31:03,458 --> 01:31:06,628
I DON'T KNOW.
CALL ME PRUDENT.

2311
01:31:06,662 --> 01:31:08,965
YOU KNOW,
AFTER THE THRILL IS GONE,

2312
01:31:08,998 --> 01:31:10,500
WE'RE LEFT
WITH THE COLD REALITY

2313
01:31:10,533 --> 01:31:14,137
THAT THE CHASE
WAS ALL WE EVER HAD.

2314
01:31:14,170 --> 01:31:16,305
MY GREAT EXPEDITION
WAS A DISASTER.

2315
01:31:16,338 --> 01:31:17,707
YEP. UH-HUH.

2316
01:31:17,740 --> 01:31:21,577
ALL THAT WAY,
JUST TO BRING BACK ANGUISH.

2317
01:31:21,610 --> 01:31:24,880
BUT YOU DID YOUR BEST
TO HELP WHEN YOU FOUND OUT.

2318
01:31:24,913 --> 01:31:27,283
THEN YOU'LL HAVE ME?

2319
01:31:27,317 --> 01:31:30,185
IT WAS YOU
WHO GAVE UNSELFISH HELP.

2320
01:31:30,218 --> 01:31:34,390
YEP, YOU'RE RIGHT.
IT WAS ME.

2321
01:31:34,423 --> 01:31:37,125
I'VE LEARNED
WE SHOULD NEVER LET GREED

2322
01:31:37,158 --> 01:31:38,627
DIRECT OUR ACTIONS.

2323
01:31:38,660 --> 01:31:40,697
YEAH, BUT LET'S PICK OUT
MY RING FIRST.

2324
01:31:40,730 --> 01:31:44,333
KAREN, I'LL TAKE YOU HOME.

2325
01:31:44,367 --> 01:31:47,403
BACK TO YOUR PEACEFUL VILLAGE.

2326
01:31:47,437 --> 01:31:51,840
WILL YOU?

2327
01:31:51,873 --> 01:31:55,110
I FEEL SO ABSOLUTELY ALONE
RIGHT NOW.

2328
01:31:55,143 --> 01:31:57,112
SOLIPSISM
IS ITS OWN REWARD.

2329
01:31:57,145 --> 01:31:59,348
...MY BROTHER'S DEAD.

2330
01:32:02,585 --> 01:32:07,357
GOSH,
YOUR HAND IS CLAMMY.

2331
01:32:07,390 --> 01:32:08,590
I COULD NEVER LOVE YOU.

2332
01:32:08,623 --> 01:32:10,192
DON'T MAKE ME LAUGH.

2333
01:32:10,225 --> 01:32:13,897
YOU'RE NOT ALONE.

2334
01:32:13,930 --> 01:32:15,530
AW.

2335
01:32:15,565 --> 01:32:17,867
HEY, THERE'S, LIKE,
EIGHT HANDS DOWN THERE.

2336
01:32:17,900 --> 01:32:19,702
HEY, GET YOUR HANDS
OUT OF THERE.

2337
01:32:19,735 --> 01:32:22,405
[IMITATES BONES CRACKING]

2338
01:32:22,438 --> 01:32:25,040
YOU'RE SQUEEZING TOO HARD.

2339
01:32:25,073 --> 01:32:26,408
YOUR GRIP...

2340
01:32:26,442 --> 01:32:28,877
[DRAMATIC MUSIC]

2341
01:32:28,912 --> 01:32:29,912
[IMITATES MUSIC]

2342
01:32:29,945 --> 01:32:33,815
AND SO WE WAVE GOODBYE
TO OUR FRIENDS.

2343
01:32:33,848 --> 01:32:36,685
BACK TO THE OCEAN.
THE SOURCE OF ALL CREDITS.

2344
01:32:39,422 --> 01:32:43,525
GAMERA WILL BE BACK IN
"SUPPORT YOUR LOCAL SHERIFF."

2345
01:32:43,558 --> 01:32:45,093
NOBODY KNOWS WHY.

2346
01:32:45,127 --> 01:32:46,328
OH, SANDY FRANK.

2347
01:32:46,362 --> 01:32:48,297
I DON'T THINK
I'VE SEEN HIS NAME BEFORE.

2348
01:32:48,330 --> 01:32:49,532
GOODNIGHT, EVERYONE.
ENJOY THE BUFFET.

2349
01:32:49,565 --> 01:32:51,567
WE SHOULD GET OUT OF HERE.
COME ON.

2350
01:32:51,600 --> 01:32:53,168
I'M GONNA STICK AROUND.

2351
01:32:53,202 --> 01:32:55,170
I WANNA SEE
HOW THIS TURNS OUT.

2352
01:32:55,203 --> 01:32:56,205
OH, WE SHOULD GO.

2353
01:32:56,238 --> 01:32:57,407
IT'S JUST WATER CROW.

2354
01:32:57,440 --> 01:33:00,710
YOU CAN STAY JUST
A LITTLE BIT LONGER, OKAY?

2355
01:33:00,743 --> 01:33:02,312
MUCHO AGUA.

2356
01:33:02,345 --> 01:33:05,915
CROW, IF YOU STAY IN TOO LONG,
YOU'LL GET WRINKLY, DEAR.

2357
01:33:05,948 --> 01:33:08,183
[IMITATING MUSIC]

2358
01:33:08,217 --> 01:33:09,218
COME ON. COME ON.

2359
01:33:09,252 --> 01:33:11,087
WHAA!

2360
01:33:22,097 --> 01:33:24,767
AH, GEE, JOEL, THAT WASN'T
MUCH OF A GAMERA MOVIE.

2361
01:33:24,800 --> 01:33:26,902
YEAH, I MEAN, GAMERA WAS HARDLY
IN THE MOVIE AT ALL,

2362
01:33:26,935 --> 01:33:28,137
YET HE GETS TOP BILLING.

2363
01:33:28,170 --> 01:33:29,172
WHY'S THAT, HMM?

2364
01:33:29,205 --> 01:33:31,273
WELL, YOU SEE,
UH, IN THIS FILM,

2365
01:33:31,307 --> 01:33:34,577
GAMERA WANTED TO SPEND A LOT
MORE TIME BEHIND THE CAMERA.

2366
01:33:34,610 --> 01:33:35,845
OH.

2367
01:33:35,878 --> 01:33:37,347
SEE, YEAH, AND THAT'S HOW
IT ALL WORKED OUT.

2368
01:33:37,380 --> 01:33:38,447
YOU SEE, IN HOLLYWOOD,

2369
01:33:38,480 --> 01:33:40,917
GAMERA IS CONSIDERED
A TRIPLE THREAT--

2370
01:33:40,950 --> 01:33:43,987
A PERFORMER,
DIRECTOR, AND MONSTER.

2371
01:33:44,020 --> 01:33:45,922
OH, KINDA LIKE
BARBARA STREISAND.

2372
01:33:45,955 --> 01:33:47,122
YEAH, EXACTLY.

2373
01:33:47,155 --> 01:33:49,158
YOU KNOW, YOU'LL READ ABOUT
THE WHOLE STORY

2374
01:33:49,192 --> 01:33:50,927
OF GAMERA VERSUS BARUGON

2375
01:33:50,960 --> 01:33:54,997
IN THIS NEW BOOK,
YOU'LL NEVER EAT THIS TOWN
FOR LUNCH AGAIN!

2376
01:33:55,030 --> 01:33:56,232
SEE, IT'S ALL IN THERE.

2377
01:33:56,265 --> 01:33:58,000
THAT'S REALLY INTERESTING.

2378
01:33:58,033 --> 01:34:00,770
YOU KNOW, WHEN IT COMES
TO BEHIND-THE-SCENES STORIES
ABOUT MONSTER MOVIES,

2379
01:34:00,803 --> 01:34:03,305
I'D LIKE TO READ MORE ABOUT IT.

2380
01:34:03,338 --> 01:34:04,807
EXACTLY, TOM.

2381
01:34:04,840 --> 01:34:07,343
READING OPENS UP
A WONDERFUL WORLD

2382
01:34:07,377 --> 01:34:09,145
OF WHIMSY AND ENCHANTMENT,

2383
01:34:09,178 --> 01:34:11,347
GRADES THREE TO FIVE.

2384
01:34:11,380 --> 01:34:12,915
OH, I WANNA READ THAT ONE.

2385
01:34:12,948 --> 01:34:14,983
HEY, HOLLYWOOD BARUGON:

2386
01:34:15,017 --> 01:34:17,520
THE SEAMY
SIDE OF MONSTER MOVIES.

2387
01:34:17,553 --> 01:34:18,553
THAT'S REALLY NEAT.

2388
01:34:18,587 --> 01:34:20,022
THE NEXT ONE LOOKS GOOD TOO.

2389
01:34:20,055 --> 01:34:22,392
THE BEST PLACES
TO EAT JAPANESE.

2390
01:34:22,425 --> 01:34:23,925
OOH, HOW ABOUT THAT?

2391
01:34:23,958 --> 01:34:26,362
HOW TO DESTROY A CITY
WITHOUT REALLY TRYING.

2392
01:34:26,362 --> 01:34:29,898
YEAH, NEXT ONE,
THE OLDEST-LIVING
JAPANESE MUTANT TELLS ALL.

2393
01:34:29,932 --> 01:34:31,000
MOVE YOUR HAND.

2394
01:34:31,033 --> 01:34:32,402
AND THIS ONE'S GREAT
FOR KIDS,

2395
01:34:32,435 --> 01:34:34,737
THE FABULOUS
WHERE'S BARUGON BOOKS.

2396
01:34:34,770 --> 01:34:36,305
DELIGHTFUL.

2397
01:34:36,338 --> 01:34:38,007
YOU KNOW,
THERE'S A LOT OF GREAT

2398
01:34:38,040 --> 01:34:39,475
ALSO BOOKS ON TAPE
ABOUT MONSTERS.

2399
01:34:39,508 --> 01:34:41,177
I WAS JUST
ABOUT TO ASK ABOUT THOSE.

2400
01:34:41,210 --> 01:34:43,412
THIS ONE'S THE VELVETEEN TURTLE
READ BY MERYL STREEP.

2401
01:34:43,445 --> 01:34:44,880
LET'S LISTEN TO THAT ONE,
CAMBOT.

2402
01:34:44,913 --> 01:34:48,083
AND SO THE VELVETEEN TURTLE
SAID TO THE LITTLE TOY SOLDIER,

2403
01:34:48,117 --> 01:34:49,918
"YOU'RE NOT LIKE
THE OTHER TOYS, ARE YOU?

2404
01:34:49,952 --> 01:34:50,953
"YOU'RE DIFFERENT.

2405
01:34:50,987 --> 01:34:53,555
"THAT IS WHY
I AM GOING TO KILL YOU.

2406
01:34:53,588 --> 01:34:55,657
WHY? BECAUSE YOU
ARE GOING TO DIE."

2407
01:34:55,690 --> 01:34:58,460
- YEAH.
- THAT'S DELIGHTFUL.
VERY TOUCHING.

2408
01:34:58,493 --> 01:35:00,195
AND THEN THERE'S
SHARP TONGUE: A MEMOIR,

2409
01:35:00,195 --> 01:35:01,197
AS READ BY BARUGON.

2410
01:35:01,230 --> 01:35:02,432
LET'S HEAR THAT ONE,
CAMBOT.

2411
01:35:02,465 --> 01:35:06,768
[CREATURE GROWLING]

2412
01:35:06,802 --> 01:35:09,205
HEY,
WHAT ARE THESE BOOKS, JOEL?

2413
01:35:09,238 --> 01:35:11,440
LESS THAN ZERO,
I AM NOT SPOCK,

2414
01:35:11,473 --> 01:35:12,908
TEKWARS
BY WILLIAM SHATNER.

2415
01:35:12,942 --> 01:35:14,277
OH, THESE ARE--

2416
01:35:14,310 --> 01:35:16,412
AN ACTOR PUBLISHES A NOVEL
TONIGHT ON EMERGENCY 911.

2417
01:35:16,445 --> 01:35:17,580
THESE ARE JUST MINE
OVER THERE.

2418
01:35:17,613 --> 01:35:19,382
WHY DON'T WE, UH,
READ A LETTER, GUYS?

2419
01:35:19,415 --> 01:35:21,417
OH, WHY NOT?
THAT SOUNDS GOOD TO ME.

2420
01:35:21,450 --> 01:35:23,518
UH, LET'S PUT THAT
ON STILL STORE THERE.

2421
01:35:23,552 --> 01:35:25,922
ANYWAY,
THIS IS FROM JOE KARNES

2422
01:35:25,955 --> 01:35:27,490
OF NAPERVILLE, ILLINOIS.

2423
01:35:27,523 --> 01:35:31,293
JOE, UH, WRITES,
"DEAR JOEL AND GANG ON MST,

2424
01:35:31,327 --> 01:35:32,528
"I REALLY LIKE YOUR SHOW.

2425
01:35:32,562 --> 01:35:33,762
"MY FAVORITE PEOPLE ARE CROW,

2426
01:35:33,828 --> 01:35:35,932
TOM SERVO, GYPSY,
CAMBOT, AND YOU."

2427
01:35:35,965 --> 01:35:37,900
THAT'S JUST ABOUT ALL OF US,
ISN'T IT?

2428
01:35:37,933 --> 01:35:39,635
"I DON'T LIKE
YOUR BOSSES TOO MUCH."

2429
01:35:39,668 --> 01:35:40,668
WE DON'T EITHER.

2430
01:35:40,702 --> 01:35:42,137
"FRANK IS KIND OF A CRYBABY,

2431
01:35:42,170 --> 01:35:44,107
"AND DR. FORRESTER
YELLS AT FRANK TOO MUCH.

2432
01:35:44,140 --> 01:35:47,142
"I'M 12-YEARS-OLD AND WATCH
YOUR SHOW ALL THE TIME.

2433
01:35:47,175 --> 01:35:48,510
"I LOVE
THE INVENTION EXCHANGE.

2434
01:35:48,543 --> 01:35:50,078
"Y'ALL MAKE
TERRIFIC INVENTIONS.

2435
01:35:50,112 --> 01:35:51,313
HOPE TO SEE
MORE OF YOUR SHOW."

2436
01:35:51,347 --> 01:35:52,782
LET'S PUT THAT
UP ON THE SCREEN.

2437
01:35:52,815 --> 01:35:53,982
TELL 'EM WHERE
THEY CAN WRITE, TOM.

2438
01:35:54,015 --> 01:35:55,952
THEY CAN WRITE
TO THE MYSTERY SCIENCE THEATER

2439
01:35:55,985 --> 01:35:58,887
INFORMATION CLUB...
[MUMBLES]

2440
01:35:58,920 --> 01:35:59,888
DO IT TODAY.

2441
01:35:59,922 --> 01:36:00,923
WHAT DO YOU THINK, SIRS?

2442
01:36:00,957 --> 01:36:02,958
FUNNY YOU SHOULD MENTION
BOOKS, BUBBIE.

2443
01:36:02,992 --> 01:36:04,827
I ASKED FRANK
TO PICK ME UP A BOOK

2444
01:36:04,860 --> 01:36:06,562
TO READ AT THE BEACH
THIS WEEKEND.

2445
01:36:06,595 --> 01:36:07,797
UH, WHAT DID YOU GET, FRANK?

2446
01:36:07,830 --> 01:36:09,765
OH, YOU'RE GONNA LOVE IT.
THIS IS GREAT.

2447
01:36:09,798 --> 01:36:11,867
IT'S THE STAND
BY STEPHEN KING.

2448
01:36:11,900 --> 01:36:13,802
THIS IS THE NEW UNCUT VERSION,

2449
01:36:13,835 --> 01:36:15,403
WHICH CONTAINS
ALL THE PASSAGES

2450
01:36:15,437 --> 01:36:17,940
THAT WERE CUT
FROM THE RESTORED VERSION.

2451
01:36:17,973 --> 01:36:19,875
IT'S REALLY GREAT.
YOU'RE GONNA REALLY ENJOY THAT.

2452
01:36:19,908 --> 01:36:20,910
OH, THANK YOU, FRANK.

2453
01:36:20,943 --> 01:36:24,112
PUSH THE BUTTON, FRANK.
